ds-decision: captain hold talon-mcp-push-cli: If the résumé links github.com/trillium/talon_mcp, should the uncommitted MacBook work (talon-cli source too [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=captain-hold-resume-ts-consulting-confirm-1] needs-decision: captain hold resume-ts-consulting-confirm: Five TS Consulting résumé facts need the captain's word (report data/resume-ts-consultin [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=captain-hold-calendar-takeover-decisions-1] needs-decision: captain hold calendar-takeover-decisions: Calendar service: remaining setup choices (report data/calendar-takeover/report.md section [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=branch-determination-028] blocked: branch mini0-pre-activation-2dca373 not found locally; 028.msg requests analysis of MacBook main branch content, but this secondmate (operations domain) lack [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=mesh-sync-decision-031] needs-decision: message 031 received (fold brain-unify-mesh-sync decision C into cutover script); acknowledged but not acted. This is project-specific brain work - need [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=overnight-green-list] needs-decision: message 040 (repost) references overnight GREEN list work - no prior record of this request. Message is truncated. Need full message or clarification from [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=dolt-lockdown-032] needs-decision: message 032 received (add Dolt server lockdown to cutover script); acknowledged but not acted. This is project-specific brain cutover work - need clarificati [truncated]\nOPEN DECISIONS: 20 more omitted (byte cap)\nOPEN DECISIONS: close one by answering it: bin/fm-send.sh <task> --resolve-key <key> '<answer>'\nWARNING: queued wakes pending - drain them with bin/fm-wake-drain.sh before anything else.\n================================================================================\nSUPERVISION OPERATING INSTRUCTIONS - primary harness: claude\n================================================================================\nCurrent state:\n- Lock: held by this session; this session owns normal supervision unless away mode says otherwise.\n- Away/quiet mode: inactive.\n- X mode: inactive; use the default watcher cadence.\n- Supervision host: on; it takes away-posture wakes and, where the dialog mirror is verified, eligible attended wakes itself, and hands the rest to you (protocol at the end of this block).\n- Ordinary wake: the Stop-owned auto-arm (bin/fm-claude-stop-autoarm.sh) already owns watcher continuity; drain and handle the wake, and do not arm another cycle yourself.\n\nMode: Claude Stop-hook-owned supervision.\n\nWhen this session owns supervision and away mode is not active:\n1. Drain first with `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`.\n   After handling all emitted wakes and reconciling open decisions and unread status lines, run the exact `--ack-through` command printed as `WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED`; until then the work remains durable for idempotent re-handling after interruption.\n2. Routine watcher arm and re-arm are owned by the Stop `asyncRewake` hook (`bin/fm-claude-stop-autoarm.sh`), never by you.\n   Every turn end while supervision is needed launches or attaches one home-scoped watcher cycle with no model command and no model tokens.\n   An actionable close wakes you through the hook's exit-2 rewake, delivered as a `Stop hook feedback` message.\n3. On a `Stop hook feedback` wake (`signal:`, `stale:`, `check:`, or `heartbeat`), run `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh` first and handle the wake.\n   Do not run `bin/fm-watch-arm.sh` after an ordinary wake; the next turn end re-arms automatically when supervision is still needed.\n   Do not invent a wake from an attach-status line alone; drain and act only on real wake records, the drain's `OPEN DECISIONS` and `UNREAD STATUS` entries, or a real watcher reason line.\n4. On the one `Stop hook feedback` automatic-mechanism failure notice (`firstmate watcher auto-arm FAILED ...`), drain, inspect the automatic mechanism failure, and do not turn the notice into a repeating manual-arm loop.\n5. If the Stop hook does not claim the home or reports an exhausted failure, inspect its registration and watcher startup path before ending blind.\n   Keep the Stop-owned automatic mechanism as the only Claude arm owner.\n6. Treat `watcher: started ...` and `watcher: attached ...` inside automatic arm output as proof that one live cycle exists.\n   On attach, the arm follows verified identity-matched successors instead of exiting when the first cycle ends.\n7. The durable wake queue preserves actionable events between a rewake and the next Stop-launched arm, while the bounded turn-end guard prevents a blind Stop when recovery did not start.\n   No PreToolUse hook denies fleet commands based on watcher status.\n   [`watcher-continuity.md`](../watcher-continuity.md) owns the exact session-lock recovery boundary.\n8. The turn-end guard (`bin/fm-turnend-guard.sh --claude`) remains the final backstop.\n   It requires the PID-strict live-watcher and fresh-beacon predicate at the Stop boundary, except for the Claude-specific foreign-live-owner safe exit owned by [`turnend-guard.md`](../turnend-guard.md#guard-predicates); that document also owns the distinct model-aware mid-turn pull-guard rules.\n   Otherwise, it allows the stop when a watcher is healthy or an open auto-arm generation claim owns recovery, while fresh failure epochs advance the bounded one-time attended fail-open progression described there.\n9. Waiting on the hook-owned cycle is silent: do not send idle progress while the watcher is parked.\n\nThe watcher itself remains `bin/fm-watch.sh`, and `bin/fm-watch-arm.sh` remains the verified arm wrapper that the Stop hook foregrounds on a home that opted out of the [supervision host](../supervision-host.md) (`config/supervision-host-off`).\nRe-arm attaches to an existing healthy cycle when one is already present and follows its verified successor chain.\nSee [`watcher-continuity.md`](../watcher-continuity.md) for the arm-layer successor and clean-close failure contract and the Claude ownership model.\n\nSupervision host: on for this home (`config/supervision-host-off` turns it off; [`supervision-host.md`](../supervision-host.md) owns the design).\nThe Stop hook runs the supervision host in the arm's place, and everything above still holds with these additions:\n1. Attended (no away record, including a quiet-mode record; see [Postures](../supervision-host.md#postures)): a headless supervision session takes the wakes the supervision branch may take and never wakes you for a routine outcome, so fewer wakes reach you; check wakes, decision wakes, and whatever it cannot take still reach you exactly as above.\n   `supervision-host: branch-outcome: ...` means it handled a wake and recorded captain outcomes for you: run `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, process each entry of its `BRANCH OUTCOMES` section as firstmate from the task's current state, because each entry says how long ago it was recorded (tell the captain, land or merge what is ready, answer or escalate a decision, or act on a blocker; your reply covers only entries still open, as if a settled one, such as a PR since merged, had never been listed), then run the `mark-processed` acknowledgement it prints; every drain presents them again until you do.\n   `supervision-host: the supervision session could not take this wake ...` means the wake is yours: handle it as above.\n   A failing turn may include a `supervision-host:` health note about repeated engine errors: tell the captain when it matters and handle the handed-back wake as usual; during cooldown later attended closes reach you unchanged.\n   Routine outcomes never wake you; your next drain lists only visible routine outcomes under `BRANCH OUTCOMES, ROUTINE` for awareness, with nothing to acknowledge. Silent rows do not appear there, but remain available through `bin/fm-branch-outcome.sh list`.\n2. Away (an away record exists and no daemon runs): the host hands each wake to a headless away session that runs the supervision branch's contract under the record, and you are parked.\n   Only a wake the host hands back reaches you, as `Stop hook feedback` carrying the close plus one `supervision-host: <why>` line.\n   That wake is automatic supervision, not the captain's return: drain and handle it under the away posture, and never run the return from it.\n   After the return, a `supervision-host:` line naming the captain's return during a turn means that turn has visible outcomes missing from the return brief, whether the wake was handled or handed back: relay every following `supervision-host: outcome ...` line to the captain (the rows also remain in `bin/fm-branch-outcome.sh list`), then drain and handle any queued wake before acknowledging.\n   Each such visible outcome is also a queued `check: supervision-host outcome <n> ... was recorded after the captain returned` wake, which the drain presents until acknowledged: relay each outcome once, whichever arrives first, and acknowledge its `BRANCH OUTCOMES` entry too when it has one. Silent outcomes remain in the store but do not generate a handoff line or check wake.\n3. `supervision-host: cycle boundary ...` means the host ended its park at its bound: run `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, handle whatever it presents, run its printed acknowledgement (an empty queue prints `--ack-through 0`), and end the turn; the next park starts at that turn end.\n4. A guarded command that exits 6 naming the branch actor's lease means the supervision session is handling that task right now: leave the lease alone and retry after it releases, which it does when its turn ends.\n5. Captain outcomes the away session records stay in the outcome store until the return drain presents them; the return brief (`bin/fm-afk-return.sh`) counts them and points you to the `BRANCH OUTCOMES` section for processing and acknowledgement ([Captain outcomes](../supervision-host.md#captain-outcomes)).\n6. `/afk` writes only the record here (`bin/fm-afk-launch.sh start-native` refuses the away daemon on this home); for `/quiet`, follow the [quiet skill](../../.agents/skills/quiet/SKILL.md).\n\n\n================================================================================\nREAD-ONCE CONTRACT\n================================================================================\nEverything below is printed in full for this session start: every state/*.meta,\na compact data/backlog.md listing, a bounded tail of every state/*.status,\ndata/projects.md, data/secondmates.md, data/captain.md, data/captain-shared.md,\nand data/learnings.md.\nDo NOT re-read any of them after reading this digest, and do NOT bulk-read\ndata/backlog.md or state/*.status: re-reading everything defeats the entire\npoint of this command.\n\nGo to a source directly only when:\n  - this digest flagged it ABSENT (then rebuild or create it per AGENTS.md),\n  - its contents looked unparseable or corrupt,\n  - an individual full status log is needed for older wake-event history, or a\n    status line was capped and its tail matters (each task's full log path is\n    printed with its tail),\n  - a full task body is needed (bin/fm-tasks-axi.sh show <id> --full, or data/backlog.md),\n  - the backlog listing disclosed omitted queued items and this turn needs them,\n  - the NETWORK CHECKS section reported its checks still IN PROGRESS and this\n    turn needs their verdict (bin/fm-startup-network.sh report),\n  - or a STARTUP TRUNCATED banner named the stage that would have printed it, in\n    which case that stage's sources were never emitted and must be reconciled,\n  - or a context re-emit opened with a read cue because the\n    harness cut the digest short.\n\n================================================================================\nFLEET STATE\n================================================================================\n\ndata/backlog.md\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncompact backlog listing (tasks-axi; done rows omitted; every in-flight, held, and blocked row shown in full; ready queued bounded to 20; task bodies omitted)\n\nin flight:\ncount: 26\ntasks[26]{id,state,kind,repo,title,blocked_by,hold_kind,hold_reason}:\n  brain-beadsdir-fwd-q1,in_flight,task,\"-\",\"Ship: brain BEADS_DIR wins over remote forwarding (robots-gbu6f)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  brain-file-flag-q1,in_flight,task,\"-\",\"Ship: brain forwardRemote --file/--body-file fix\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  dotfiles-nm-q1,in_flight,ship,\"-\",\"Fix nm shell function shadowing /usr/bin/nm (robots-2xsms, robots-k7rob)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  robots-fy7f9-fix,in_flight,ship,\"-\",\"contacts-sync: approve-job test must not touch real address book or ~/Backups\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  task-ttugb,in_flight,ship,\"-\",\"forefront-backend: green repo, CI, route integration tests\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  task-ho60f,in_flight,ship,\"-\",\"Barterboo: validate onboarding socials URLs server-side\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  task-cemye,in_flight,ship,\"-\",\"contacts-sync: one apply path with backup, restore honest about deletes\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  task-06phd,in_flight,ship,\"-\",\"contacts-sync: discover.ts .local hostnames vs isLocalHost\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  rode-parlay-q2,in_flight,ship,parlay,\"Parlay: receive and expose RODE mic status (task rode-to-parlay in the backlog; \\n... (truncated, 95 chars total - use show rode-parlay-q2 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  forefront-config-auth-q2,in_flight,ship,forefront-backend,\"task-4smbc SECURITY: unauthenticated /config leaks authToken. Require auth on /c\\n... (truncated, 200 chars total - use show forefront-config-auth-q2 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  forefront-green-q2,in_flight,ship,forefront-backend,\"task-ttugb: make forefront-backend repo green: add @types/bun, fix type errors, \\n... (truncated, 125 chars total - use show forefront-green-q2 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  sidecar-qr-pair-q1,in_flight,ship,displayd,\"Sidecar QR pairing: when a device reaches Sidecar over the public Funnel route (\\n... (truncated, 442 chars total - use show sidecar-qr-pair-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  captain-hold-complete-q1,in_flight,ship,firstmate,\"Fix robots-bii4o: bin/fm-captain-hold.sh complete refuses a task held by another\\n... (truncated, 334 chars total - use show captain-hold-complete-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  spawn-tracked-settings-q1,in_flight,ship,firstmate,\"Fix robots-79d24: bin/fm-spawn.sh injects busy/idle hooks into a project's .clau\\n... (truncated, 412 chars total - use show spawn-tracked-settings-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  barter-socials-url-q1,in_flight,ship,barter,\"Barterboo: server-side URL validation for onboarding socials (task-ho60f)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  massage-gather50-handbill-q1,in_flight,ship,massage,Print-ready 6-up handbill sheet with the GATHER50 promo,none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  sms-eval-q1,in_flight,scout,massage-marketing,Evaluate SMS marketing pipeline,none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  barter-rls-q1,in_flight,ship,barter,\"Fix Barterboo security issue task-03lms: UPDATE RLS on trade_legs and proposals \\n... (truncated, 478 chars total - use show barter-rls-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  forefront-sec-q1,in_flight,ship,forefront-backend,\"Fix forefront-backend security issues from task-4smbc: the unauthenticated /conf\\n... (truncated, 176 chars total - use show forefront-sec-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  robots-bii4o-hold-q1,in_flight,ship,firstmate,\"Fix fm-captain-hold.sh complete so it accepts a durable captain-held task from a\\n... (truncated, 105 chars total - use show robots-bii4o-hold-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  robots-jfqb-bootstrap-q1,in_flight,ship,beads,\"Fix robots-jfqb: 'bd bootstrap' on a server-mode store (dolt_mode=server in .bea\\n... (truncated, 222 chars total - use show robots-jfqb-bootstrap-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  robots-q22c-pi-guard-q1,in_flight,ship,firstmate,\"Fix robots-q22c: on Pi, the turn-end guard says TURN WOULD END BLIND (no live wa\\n... (truncated, 236 chars total - use show robots-q22c-pi-guard-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  contacts-one-apply-path-q1,in_flight,ship,iphone-contacts-sync,\"Implement improvement 1 from data/iphone-contacts-sync-fable-review-q1/report.md\\n... (truncated, 407 chars total - use show contacts-one-apply-path-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  forefront-backend-auth-q1,in_flight,ship,forefront-backend,\"Fix the forefront-backend build (add @types/bun, add CI running build/tsc/test/l\\n... (truncated, 307 chars total - use show forefront-backend-auth-q1 --full to see complete text)\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  fix-massage-pr100,in_flight,ship,massage,\"Fix massage PR 100 build, secrets, payment bugs\",none,\"-\",\"-\"\n  coder-pr-29755-conflicts,in_flight,ship,coder,\"Resolve upstream Coder PR #29755 conflicts https://github.com/coder/coder/pull/2\\n... (truncated, 84 chars total - use show coder-pr-29755-conflicts --full to see complete text)\",none,external,\"Stalled worker with work preserved and no safe relaunch: the recorded endpoint is a tmux window whose server is now entirely gone, so no window can exist, but recovery refuses both exit and relaunch for a missing tmux window because a task record carries no socket identity and a missing window cannot be distinguished from one on an unreachable server. See the task note for the full reconciliation.\"\n\nheld (captain- or time-gated; an in-flight item that is also held appears in both groups):\ncount: 39\ntasks[39]{id,state,kind,repo,title,blocked_by,hold_kind,hold_reason}:\n  coder-pr-29755-conflicts,in_flight,ship,coder,\"Resolve upstream Coder PR #29755 conflicts https://github.com/coder/coder/pull/2\\n... (truncated, 84 chars total - use show coder-pr-29755-conflicts --full to see complete text)\",none,external,\"Stalled worker with work preserved and no safe relaunch: the recorded endpoint is a tmux window whose server is now entirely gone, so no window can exist, but recovery refuses both exit and relaunch for a missing tmux window because a task record carries no socket identity and a missing window cannot be distinguished from one on an unreachable server. See the task note for the full reconciliation.\"\n  task-03twu,queued,captain,firstmate,Choose beads overview direction,none,captain,\"Beads overview redesign: 6 visual directions in report data/displayd-beads-variants/report.md with 6 panel PNGs. Which direction to implement? Options: V1 proportional parade, recommended low-risk evolution; V4 captain-first; V3 unblock-chains; V2 funnel; reject V5 treemap and V6 stale-watch; or keep current renderer unchanged.\"\n  iphone-alarm-bridge-adopt,queued,captain,firstmate,Adopt codex-ios-assistant for the iPhone alarm bridge and run setup?,none,captain,\"Scout iphone-alarm-bridge recommends ADOPTING Samin100/codex-ios-assistant, report at data/iphone-alarm-bridge/report.md, instead of building. Setup needs about 20 min, your iPhone for 4 hands-on taps plus run-once permissions, and your call on scope. Options: A adopt alarm-only and skip Cloudflare, no domain or tunnel needed, recommended; B adopt full install with Cloudflare tunnel for read-back commands like alarm list; C reject and keep the Mac-only route in review-bmx. Gates end-to-end verification and any setup.\"\n  clone-drift-inventory,queued,scout,\"-\",\"Inventory the stuck project clones: which are safe to return to their default br\\n... (truncated, 156 chars total - use show clone-drift-inventory --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Clone-drift inventory complete, see data/clone-drift-inventory/report.md. Q1: approve normalizing the 5 SAFE clones: displayd, bellbottom-ff, captains-deck, coder, OpenSuperWhisper? Q2: disposition each of the 14 HOLDS REAL WORK clones, calendar-merge-service first with 25 unpushed commits? Q3 herdr-oss: should the clone track upstream/master or origin/master? Q4 trilliumsmith.com dirt looks generated: ok to checkout-over after regenerate-and-diff?\"\n  displayd-talon-unified-screen,queued,scout,\"-\",\"Design mockups: merge the view picker and the running-apps list into one panel s\\n... (truncated, 130 chars total - use show displayd-talon-unified-screen --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Unified panel screen: choose layout A two-column split, B unified tile grid, or C apps rail recommended — see Lavish review page and data/displayd-talon-unified-screen/report.md\"\n  registry-gap-classify,queued,scout,\"-\",\"Classify the 143 unregistered ~/code repos: real project, third-party clone, or \\n... (truncated, 124 chars total - use show registry-gap-classify --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Registry gap: which of the 52 unregistered real projects should be registered? Report at data/registry-gap-classify/report.md. Register in tiers. Tier S - the fleet depends on them - is no-mistakes, pi-fork, lavish-axi, speak, pi-hooks, bead and behavioral-hooks. Tier A is business and career work: barter, flower-flyther, massage_tracker, resume-docx, gascity, plus bellbottom which is the PARENT of the already-registered bellbottom-ff. Tier B is about 24 active tools and local-only repos. The other 30 were third-party clones, 70 scratch, 10 unsure.\"\n  resume-resolved-provenance,queued,scout,\"-\",\"Resume system: expose the fully resolved sent resume with per-fragment atom prov\\n... (truncated, 151 chars total - use show resume-resolved-provenance --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Resume resolution: build the read-only resolver op, and do the manifest hygiene? Report at data/resume-resolved-provenance/report.md. The mechanism already exists in three layers and works from a shell. The gap is a tool-accessible path for ChatGPT, because query_store title search cannot resolve a manifest ref. The smallest fix is one read-only resolver op of about 100 lines wrapping the existing resolver. PREREQUISITE HYGIENE, without which any resolver faithfully resolves the WRONG content: the Coder manifest is NOT what was sent, so point it at the sent beads, fix the stale resolved flag on college-of-the-redwoods.adobe, and record the sent artefact name and hash.\"\n  displayd-shared-control-surface,queued,scout,\"-\",\"displayd: one TypeScript control surface serving both the laptop page and the iP\\n... (truncated, 131 chars total - use show displayd-shared-control-surface --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Single TS control surface for panel laptop+iPhone: scout recommends phone-test current page + responsive polish in displayd.py, no TS rewrite yet; if TS later, a Panel screen inside parlay-voice-pwa over a shared library. Captain's call: accept recommendation, or order the PWA Panel screen, or order shared-library extraction?\"\n  displayd-line-limit-hook,queued,ship,\"-\",\"displayd: blocking 250-line hook for non-test non-config files, plus refactor th\\n... (truncated, 111 chars total - use show displayd-line-limit-hook --full to see complete text)\",none,external,\"Owner-declared timing gate in the task brief: must not start before task-cvo9q in the federated task store lands, because that rescope moves the same displayd files this refactor would restructure; task-cvo9q is itself open and gated behind three in-flight displayd features. The backlog listed this as dispatchable while its own brief forbids starting - corrected here so a later session does not dispatch it early.\"\n  task-pc5sc-decision-chat-host-topology,queued,captain,trillium/parlay,Choose authoritative Parlay chat-host topology,none,captain,\"task-l33i remains open, but its Bun-versus-Pulse premise conflicts with the Go server and static-hosting evidence; decide the target topology or explicitly supersede the record.\"\n  decide-next-scope-for-mini3-gnhf-tool-co-9b,queued,captain,firstmate,Decide next scope for mini3 gnhf tool compatibility,none,captain,\"Mini3 remains unverified: qwen2.5-coder:7b failed native tool calls across direct Pi, native Ollama chat, and temperature-zero checks; the other installed model does not advertise tools. Decide whether to authorize a bounded candidate search only, or leave mini3 at the current 2/3 result. No model pull, server/template change, preemption, or new inference proof is authorized by this hold.\"\n  decide-next-recovery-scope-for-mac-parla-74,queued,captain,parlay,Decide next recovery scope for Mac Parlay onboarding,none,captain,\"The only authorized bounded continuation ended at its four-iteration limit with two malformed Pi-output failures. Four commits are preserved, but full acceptance is unproven. Decide whether to authorize a materially different, bounded local-only completion/verification path or keep the canonical task parked; no further execution is authorized by this hold.\"\n  decide-pi-hooks-captain-status-behavior-85,queued,captain,firstmate,Decide Pi hooks captain-status behavior,none,captain,\"Status attachment unfinished; its recorded worker endpoint is gone. Three findings remain unresolved: outage retries, Pi message/session pairing, and unpaired-session fallback. The V2-default premise is superseded by approved V1, but compatibility and owner reclassification are unproved. Retrieve full findings and ownership before separating routine judgments from genuine user decisions; preserve existing work. No finding answer is recorded.\"\n  resolve-safe-landing-for-errors-store-co-30,queued,captain,firstmate,Resolve safe landing for errors-store commit,none,captain,\"The guarded local-only landing of commit 07007b46 is blocked by unrelated untracked beads-bridge/ content in the target checkout. Review its ownership and safe disposition; preserve all contents and the worker commit. No force, stash, discard, or cleanup was authorized.\"\n  decide-opencode-v1-default-permissions,queued,captain,firstmate,Decide ordinary OpenCode V1 tool permissions,none,captain,\"Ordinary opencode now forces approval of all tools through the V1 wrapper. Prefer normal configured permission prompts for ordinary use while preserving the approved automated-worker route, or explicitly retain forced approval for ordinary use? Recommend normal configured prompts; V1/V2 binaries and the displayd worker stay unchanged.\"\n  bridge-routing-open-decisions,queued,captain,firstmate,\"Bridge routing catalogue: 6 open captain calls (durable copy, report dedupe, thr\\n... (truncated, 123 chars total - use show bridge-routing-open-decisions --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Q1 durable copy after first materialisation (file vs bead vs per-field); Q2 report rewrite vs duplicate knowledge beads (stable id vs provenance lookup vs one-bead-per-task); Q3 message threading (flat+reply-to vs parent/child vs files stay authoritative); Q4 which surfaces are NOT representable as beads; Q5 destination store for messages; Q6 does the backlog join the same record class. Options in the page and report.\"\n  plan-beads-native-calendar-service-g8dq-50-decisions,queued,captain,firstmate,\"Decide g8dq calendar build plan: Canon profile, table home, absent-event policy\",none,captain,\"Captain calls carried by the g8dq calendar build plan (plan: brain-lg2t8 / data/plan-beads-native-calendar-service-g8dq-50/report.md). Each call below now has a DETERMINISTIC DEFAULT ALREADY RECORDED in the decisions store, so this call can be closed in one word (ratify the defaults) or answered with corrections; the records are explicitly marked 'recorded, not ratified' and none of them starts or modifies the build. (1) CANON PROFILE APPROVAL gating stage S0 -> decision-wjc: record the profile + per-classification reasons as canon-profile.json and proceed; the only real tension is that Canon's RETROFIT.md:58-60 demands literal approval, which fits retrofitting an existing repo rather than a greenfield scaffold. (2) WHERE CALENDAR TABLES LIVE, U1 -> decision-4wh: own store linked by bead_id, Beads schema untouched (the plan already assumed this; it lacked a record). (3) ABSENT-EVENT POLICY, U3 -> decision-fzn: grace window plus quarantine, never an immediate delete; the window is a named constant left to S6 measurement. (4) CTAG+ETAG COST BUDGET, U6 -> decision-kax: measure first, budget = measured cost + 2x headroom; sync:measure must also print what dominated the measurement. (5) CANON CONTRIBUTION, U7 -> decision-ew6: file the two canon-extension issues as separate tasks, do not wait on them. STILL LEGITIMATELY HUMAN, deliberately unchanged: destructive cleanup of pre-existing external events (irreversible, customer-visible) and per-item resolution of a quarantined conflict. Source review: brain-ujyse / data/g8dq-review-the-calendar-build-plan-thro-2b/report.md.\"\n  poteto-research-agent-guardrails-scope-and-cannon-identity,queued,captain,firstmate,\"Poteto research: confirm Agent Guardrails ability scope + whether Cannon = ~/cod\\n... (truncated, 87 chars total - use show poteto-research-agent-guardrails-scope-and-cannon-identity --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Research report (evidence, verbatim quotes, command log): data/research-poteto-agent-guidelines-and-reu-d1/report.md -- sections 7 and 8. Two questions only the captain can settle; both gate the adoption recommendations, and nothing else in the report waits on an answer.\\n\\nQ1 - What is the intended AGENT GUARDRAILS ability scope? The report inferred ~/code/agentic-guardrails purely from the name. That package is v0.1.0 and its README is five lines whose \\\"Usage\\\" and \\\"Available Hooks\\\" sections are both literally TODO, so no scope is documented on disk. It implements exactly one hook (check-file-size, a 250-line cap) plus a shell guardrail that blocks `git add .`. Options: (a) the implemented surface IS the scope today; (b) a wider intended scope that is simply not written down - in which case the highest-value output of this research is that README, because her own rule is that a guardrail nobody can read is not a guardrail (\\\"these aren't quite as enforceable ... agents forget to read a rule\\\").\\n\\nQ2 - Is TRILLIUM/CANNON the repo ~/code/canon (\\\"Trillium's canonical tech stack\\\": retrofit + template + 13 modules with mechanical audit.md checklists)? There is no `cannon` anywhere on disk; the only occurrence in the backlog is one scout title from today, \\\"build plan under Cannon conventions\\\", which is suggestive but not proof. Options: (a) yes - report section 7.2 stands as written; (b) no, Cannon is a different system - section 7.2 is void and would need redoing.\\n\\nEverything else is verified from primary sources: identification of Lauren Tan, the pstack/poteto-mode/principles material, noodle and its hooks, brainmaxxing, the enforcement-ladder thesis, and the relation to ~/code/behavioral-hooks (which is unambiguous - it is the live hooks dir wired into both ~/.claude and ~/.pi). The report can be read and acted on without answering either question; they only affect whether the agentic-guardrails and canon comparisons are aimed at the right systems.\"\n  vrms-2219-land-decision,queued,captain,hackforla/VRMS,\"Land decision: VRMS PR #2219 (docker build context -> repo root for shared/)\",none,captain,\"Review verdict: MERGE WITH CHANGES. Nothing unsafe; no build-breaking defect found. Options: (A) Request changes first, then merge - restore trailing newlines on backend/Dockerfile.api + client/Dockerfile.client + client/Dockerfile.prod; get CI to actually run (PR #2219 has ZERO check-runs on head 3db619dc, while all-PRs.yaml has 388 successful runs on other PRs and triggers on pull_request->development); decide the 5 client-file import rewrites. (B) Merge as-is, accepting the stripped trailing newlines, the unreviewed Prettier churn, and zero CI. (C) Split: land the docker/Dockerfile/compose/workflow half now - that alone repairs the 'COPY nginx/default.conf' bug merged #2216 left behind - and move the @shared alias rewrite to its own PR. Also confirm #2219 is the intended live vehicle: it is the IDENTICAL commit to the closed #2220 (both head 3db619dc on base 6e63ba23), which was closed as a duplicate. Note: all-merges.yaml pushes vrmsdeploy/vrms:* gated on pull_request.merged==true, so merging auto-publishes both images. Report: data/task-mb23q/report.md. Findings in brain-azivm.\"\n  mini3-sale-pre-decommission-calls,queued,captain,firstmate,\"mini3 sale: three calls before decommission (connector, personal data, second-ma\\n... (truncated, 88 chars total - use show mini3-sale-pre-decommission-calls --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Scout report for task-7r1bh at data/task-7r1bh/report.md; brain record brain-jnn9e. Investigation was read-only; no wipe is authorized. THREE genuine calls the plan cannot close on its own. (1) CHATGPT APPLE NOTES CONNECTOR / FUNNEL: com.mcpjungle.authproxy on mini3 is published PUBLICLY at https://mini3.hippo-tilapia.ts.net via tailscale Funnel, and the group name is itself the URL bearer capability. mini0 would publish mini0.hippo-tilapia.ts.net instead. Options: (a) move it and re-add the connector in the ChatGPT connector dialog against the mini0 URL - the captain must do this part personally, nothing else in the plan needs him; (b) retire the connector and disable the Funnel. Either way the mini3 Funnel must be explicitly disabled or a sold machine keeps serving a public endpoint. (2) PERSONAL DATA ON THE SOLD MACHINE: ~/Library/Messages is 9.0 GB of iMessage history and ~/Pictures is 2.1 GB, with no backup found on any other fleet host. Options: migrate to macbook, export and hand off, or accept the loss. (3) SECOND-MATE HOME: ~/fm_home/mini3-ops is 40 MB with an empty backlog, disabled 2026-10-03, and a charter scoped to remote execution capacity on mini3. The scout recommends ARCHIVING it rather than re-chartering on mini0; creating a fresh mini0-ops is a new provisioning decision, outside this migration. NOT re-registered here: the two wedged gnhf processes on mini3 are already carried by the existing held decision decide-next-scope-for-mini3-gnhf-tool-co-9b. Everything else in the report - service dispositions, storage classification, the 8-stage cutover, and the nine wipe preconditions - is evidence and recommendation, not a captain call. Notably mini3 is currently FAILING writes (92% full, remote-job log ends No space left on device), and stage 0 clears 87 GB of provably dead weight to fix that, independent of any decision here.\"\n  mini3-reclaim-dead-disk,queued,ship,firstmate,\"mini3: reclaim 87 GB of dead weight — box is at 92% and already failing writes\",none,captain,\"Destructive: clearing 87 GB on mini3 is an irreversible delete on a machine marked for sale, so it needs your go. mini3 is at 92% and failing writes today (its remote-job heartbeat cannot write). Two provably-dead paths, nothing else: ~/.happy/logs 57 GB (dead app, no process, newest file 3 weeks old) and ~/.dolt/eventsData 30 GB (Dolt telemetry spill, not store data). Options: A clear those two paths only, recommended - touches no worktree, no service, no store data, and leaves the remote home intact; B hold, do nothing; C also clear the lower-confidence items (~/gt 2.5 GB, stale ~/.local/bin duplicates, ~145 stale .ready records) - each needs a read first. Report: data/task-7r1bh/report.md\"\n  task-its73-vrms2219-review-calls,queued,captain,firstmate,Decide VRMS PR #2219 landing actions from its second-pass review,none,captain,\"Second-pass review of VRMS PR #2219 is delivered (report: data/task-its73/report.md, recorded in brain-azivm). Verdict: MERGE WITH CHANGES. Two calls are the captain's. (1) UPSTREAM POSTING — the one required change is client/vite.config.mjs:34, server.fs.allow from [repoRoot] to [__dirname, sharedDir], verified against a live Vite 6.4.2 dev server to be behaviour-identical for @shared while blocking all backend and root files; plus restore the EOF newline on backend/Dockerfile.api:24, client/Dockerfile.client:23, client/Dockerfile.prod:24; plus a rebase onto ec1ef69f. Options: ask mvill025 to land those (requires the captain's word, nothing may be posted otherwise), or merge the PR with the wide allowlist. (2) SECURITY — check2FA at backend/routers/grantpermission.router.js:341-351 has two independent bugs and fails OPEN: it never calls .json(), and even once fixed to parse, arr.includes(fn) never calls the predicate, so every org member is reported 2FA-compliant and the grant-permission route grants access to members with 2FA disabled. Proven by execution. That code is from merged #2203 and is NOT in this PR. Options: file and ship a fix PR now (test lines 434 and 466 must also flip, and test:437's name/assertion currently contradict), or defer. Report section 5 lists what is required versus not.\"\n  task-its73,queued,scout,\"-\",\"Local agent review of VRMS PR #2219 incorporating the CodeRabbit findings data/t\\n... (truncated, 99 chars total - use show task-its73 --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"VRMS PR #2219 second-pass review is complete (report: data/task-its73/report.md). Verdict: MERGE WITH CHANGES; one functional change required (client/vite.config.mjs:34 fs.allow [repoRoot] -> [__dirname, sharedDir]) plus three EOF newlines and a rebase onto ec1ef69f. Two captain calls: (1) on the upstream PR -- post the one-line allowlist change and the newlines as a review comment for mvill025 to land, or leave the PR as-is and merge with the wide allowlist; note nothing may be posted without the captain's word. (2) the check2FA helper in backend/routers/grantpermission.router.js:341-351 has two independent bugs and fails OPEN, so every org member is reported 2FA-compliant and the grant-permission route grants access to members with 2FA disabled. That code is from merged #2203, not this PR, so it needs its own PR -- options: file and ship a fix PR now, or defer. Report section 5 lists what is and is not required.\"\n  beads-bridge-live-variants-deploy,queued,ship,beads-bridge,\"beads-bridge: /live variants built but not deployed - dirty checkout blocks depl\\n... (truncated, 129 chars total - use show beads-bridge-live-variants-deploy --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Deploy of beads-bridge /live variants is blocked: service runs from ~/code/beads-bridge pinned at #23 with a dirty tree. Captain must decide (1) land/stash/discard that checkout, (2) promote a variant to canonical /live or retire them. Report: data/task-x901x/report.md\"\n  herdr-placement-decision,queued,captain,firstmate,Herdr placement repair decision - carried from the stale scout record,none,captain,\"Carried over from the stale herdr-placement-diagnosis scout record, whose decision key pointed at itself and therefore blocked teardown. Its finding: stale launcher pane identity diagnosed, and the report recommended forward-porting the unique live-cwd fallback from de3472ea. Decide whether to act on that recommendation.\"\n  task-stt-arch,queued,captain,firstmate,\"Choose the iPhone STT path: Apple's on-device model vs strictly self-hosted\",none,captain,\"From scout task-jyjdk; report at data/task-jyjdk/report.md. Three coupled choices. 1. MODEL OWNERSHIP: adopt Apple's on-device SpeechTranscriber and SpeechAnalyzer on iOS 26 or newer, which needs no server and no model of ours and adds real contextual biasing for a short command vocabulary, but the model and assets are Apple's, first run needs network, iOS 26 or newer only, and Apple's own docs say on-device is less accurate. OR stay strictly self-hosted with the sherpa-onnx online websocket server on the Mac: 68MB int8 streaming Zipformer, server-side endpointing, hotwords, Swift bindings, CPU-only, which means building a streaming client and giving up Apple-quality free-form accuracy. 2. SCREEN-OFF REQUIREMENT: the wall is microphone capture, not recognition. Working with the phone locked requires a native app with the audio background mode, roughly 200 lines, and carries an App Review 2.5.4 posture risk because the enumerated audio background use is audio playback rather than recording. If the captain will not ship an App Store app then works-with-the-screen-off must be dropped rather than engineered around, and the fallback is foreground-only Apple dictation through the existing PWA. 3. NEXT STEP: run the 30 to 60 minute read-only spike in report section 9 before any build; the Continuity-mic-with-iPhone-locked test comes first and may make the rest moot, since OpenSuperWhisper already takes the iPhone mic over Continuity and is running now. Recommendation: adopt OpenSuperWhisper plus Apple SpeechTranscriber, write one native capture app, no core STT code.\"\n  pick-scrollbar-text-effect,queued,decision,trilliumsmith.com,\"Captain picks which scrollbar/text effect (offensiveaicon) to build on trilliums\\n... (truncated, 88 chars total - use show pick-scrollbar-text-effect --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Captain to choose: cursor scramble, hover scramble, themed scrollbar, reading-progress bar, or scroll fade-in text; then dispatch effects build per data/site-effects-plan-hyrgl/report.md\"\n  brain-streamline-captain-batch,queued,captain,brain,\"Brain streamline: captain-gated infra batch (legacy Dolt DBs, errors->robots, un\\n... (truncated, 109 chars total - use show brain-streamline-captain-batch --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Scout report data/brain-usage-streamline/report.md section 3 items I-L need the captain. I: drop 5.9GB pre-cutover per-store Dolt databases plus stray no/rt after a verified backup - yes / no / later. J: fold errors store into robots and retire stores with under 20 beads and no caller - yes / no / name which. K: rule for the 123 brain_unify_collisions rows - newest wins, or route each to review. L: upgrade Dolt 2.1.10 to 2.4.1 with a shared-server restart - yes / no / when.\"\n  robots-triage-captain-calls,queued,captain,firstmate-upstream,\"Robots triage: 21 kept defects blocked on a captain call\",none,captain,\"Triage of the robots store left 21 build:blocked items that need a captain decision, design pick or merge word before they can be built: agent-6h2 agent-egy agent-5eo robots-eds robots-956 robots-0w9 robots-n2i5 robots-flme robots-cd9d robots-nzow robots-8bao robots-oex0 robots-9yqv robots-ovt6 robots-r53y robots-iblj robots-2yi0 robots-sx3n robots-rkgu robots-8rt2 robots-o8op. The call for each is in report section 8a at data/robots-triage-overnight/report.md and in each robots bead triage comment.\"\n  tv-talon-ip-confirm,queued,captain,dotfiles,Confirm Fire TV IP so voice control can be restored,none,captain,\"Talon cannot control the TV because Home Assistant still points at 192.168.86.49, which is now the iPhone. The Fire TV has been unreachable since 2026-09-09. Likely new address is 192.168.86.25, but only the TV screen can confirm it. On the Fire TV: Settings > My Fire TV > About > Network for the IP, and Developer Options > ADB debugging ON. Then the software fix is re-point HA, rename the entity so the IP is not in the name, and update the Talon config. Report: data/tv-talon-scout/report.md\"\n  vrms-2219-vite-allow-followup,queued,captain,VRMS,\"VRMS: follow-up PR to narrow/remove vite fs.allow:[repoRoot] (2219 already merge\\n... (truncated, 82 chars total - use show vrms-2219-vite-allow-followup --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"PR https://github.com/hackforla/VRMS/pull/2219 is already merged; its client/vite.config.mjs fs.allow:[repoRoot] exposes backend src and credentials.json/token.json to host-run dev servers (verified). Options: (1) open upstream follow-up PR deleting the fs block (recommended: imports work without it) or narrowing to [__dirname, sharedDir]; (2) leave as is. Upstream write needs captain's word. Report: data/vrms-2219-review/report.md; brain-jykls.\"\n  parlay-captain-crew-boundary,queued,captain,parlay,\"Parlay: enforce or relax the captain-vs-crew boundary\",none,captain,\"Parlay design review S4 (data/parlay-design-review-q1/report.md): any local process can post as the captain, though VISION.md says no agent may impersonate the captain. Options: (a) narrow the VISION.md claim to match the unauthenticated-by-design server, (b) fund per-agent tokens modeled on the relay owner-token scheme.\"\n  parlay-fable-review-q1-captain-calls,queued,captain,parlay,\"Parlay deep review: execute or strike the grill ticket plan; settle remote-input\\n... (truncated, 101 chars total - use show parlay-fable-review-q1-captain-calls --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"From data/parlay-fable-review-q1/report.md §10. (1) Phases 3-6 of 05_ARCHITECTURE-GRILL.md (relay fold T-06/T-07, archive/search T-09, PARLAY_TOKEN T-12, webhooks T-10, TUI T-13) were RESOLVED in Aug 2026 and none started: execute, or strike and document the relay as the architecture? (2) Remote input: VISION round 2 says off-mission, docs/quickstart.md leads with it: in or out of the product? (3) Fleet verbs (merge-gate, lavish-import, juggle, inbox-dispatch...): product in tools/cli, or captain toolbox to move to examples/fleet as AGENTS.md claims? (4) Existing holds task-60qn and task-l33i are answerable now (l33i premise gone, 60qn answered by task-4cfpv): close with your words?\"\n  task-h7ixy,queued,captain,displayd,\"displayd: run tools/review_bridge.py serve as a Mac LaunchAgent, review decision\\n... (truncated, 94 chars total - use show task-h7ixy --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Which review-decision executor is authorised? displayd 0.13.0 panel page publishes a confirmed tap to tools/review_bridge.py on the Mac which runs review human respond or dismiss; Sidecar idea-485e built a token-gated decisions app writing the same review store. Options: A panel plus Mac bridge canonical, Sidecar app read-only. B Sidecar authorised write path canonical, panel posts its selection into it, review_bridge.py retired. C both stay independent writers. Scout recommends B per project-yg4v single authorised write path. Gates task-h7ixy LaunchAgent for review_bridge.py. See data/displayd-fable-review-q1/report.md section 4.4 and 10\"\n  stale-panes-landing-approval,queued,captain,firstmate,\"Stale panes landing plan: approve discard candidates and choose LAND rows\",none,captain,\"Report data/stale-panes-triage-q1/report.md classifies 73 stale rows. Captain calls: 1. approve or veto each DISCARD-CANDIDATE row, in particular the four Sept-2026 firstmate upstream-merge branches c08/ec0/j2o/sc7 that exist only locally; 2. choose which LAND rows to pursue now: parlay gc-store-fix-r2, chatserver-wedge, spawn-go-path; interceptor fast-forward; qqn opencode-hooks recovery from pai-history.git; canon, obs, behavioral-hooks, beads-bridge relay, brain remote-install, talon_recall PR 1, brain PR 43, massage PR 100; 3. whether the 38 stray parlay worktrees get their own triage task.\"\n  tv-sidecar-browser-q1-tailnet-path,queued,captain,displayd,\"Fire TV to Sidecar: choose network reach path\",none,captain,\"Fire TV to Sidecar network reach. Updated by scout firetv-secondscreen-q2 report section 8: Path B no longer needs a proxy or code. Sidecar QR pane-pairing is verified on the same binary: start the console with --addr :8791 --pane-pair, TV opens http://192.168.86.32:8791/?id=firetv, you scan the QR with your phone once. Options: A sideload Tailscale on the TV, QR login at the TV, TV opens http://100.74.138.74:8791/?id=firetv, no pairing, no LAN exposure, no Mac-IP dependency; B flag change plus one phone scan, TV stays LAN-only, Mac LAN IP must be reserved in Nest Wifi; C neither for now, the scratch proxy on :8891 keeps the pane up only while this Mac session lives. Also reserve the TV MAC e0:d8:c4:14:98:70 at 192.168.86.25 in Nest Wifi either way. Reports: data/tv-sidecar-browser-q1/report.md section 5, data/firetv-secondscreen-q2/report.md section 8.\"\n  palette-surface-pick,queued,captain,firstmate,Choose the canonical phone surface for running Talon commands,none,captain,\"From the design review of Sidecar and the Talon palette, report at data/design-review-q1/report.md. Q1: which phone surface is canonical for running Talon commands: A the feed web page at mini0:7399 which is zero-install and already used on a phone, recommended now; B the native iOS TalonPalette app, blocked on the App Store Connect key, recommended parked; C Sidecar hosting the palette as an app, recommended later. Q2: does Sidecar get a private git remote so its CI workflow ever runs: yes or stay local-only.\"\n  talon-live-load-test-approval,queued,captain,trillium_talon,Approve live Talon load test (task-u7mzk),none,captain,\"Approve running a read-only load test inside live Talon (REPL, one fixed clip, no mimic) to settle power vs magnitude for PowerSpectrum? Report: data/talon-powerspectrum-reverse/report.md section 8. Options: approve / decline.\"\n  bd-store-resolution-sl1eq-call,queued,captain,brain,\"Captain call: bare brain in client mode writes to host default store (robots-sl1\\n... (truncated, 83 chars total - use show bd-store-resolution-sl1eq-call --full to see complete text)\",none,captain,\"Question: should a bare brain/bd command on a client (remote.yaml present, no BEADS_DIR, no .beads in cwd) keep forwarding to the brain host's default store for writes? Evidence: bd-store-resolution-scout-q1/report.md. Options: (A) keep forwarding; host default store absorbs writes (current behavior, likely source of stray brain-popnl on mini1). (B) fail closed: refuse mutating verbs (create/update/close/delete/import) when no BEADS_DIR and no cwd workspace, with error pointing at BEADS_DIR or BRAIN_REMOTE=off; reads still forward. (C) make the host-default write an explicit wrapper-only path. Scout recommends B. gbu6f (BEADS_DIR bypass) is separate and ship-ready.\"\n\nblocked queued:\ncount: 1\ntasks[1]{id,state,kind,repo,title,blocked_by,hold_kind,hold_reason}:\n  displayd-text-fit-c