{"parentUuid":"f76665e7-1d76-487a-8e37-167be20b259c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBUAth3apbtHKWTY8EHC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Logged to status-kdv, captain. The `BEADS_DIR` fix (robots-gbu6f) is still validating after I approved the dedupe finding. Nothing new needs you.\n\n**Usage and speed:**\n- **Claude:** 45% left, Fable 40%, on a seven-day window that resets at 23:59 UTC tonight.\n- **Codex:** 100% idle. **agy:** 92–95% idle. Both are underspent.\n- **Grok:** 75% left, but its credentials have expired.\n- **opencode:** 43%.\n- **Since last poke:** no PRs landed, one ship in flight, two wake notices handled.\n\nI'm holding the Codex/agy batch until you say \"go\". Top candidates for it are robots-7iaq (the validation test step that died silently) and the duplicate-record conflicts agent-l7p and agent-0bq.\n\nWaiting on you:\n1. **Brain PR 44:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44 is green; say \"merge\" to land it.\n2. **Codex/agy batch:** \"go\" to dispatch it.\n3. **forefront-backend PR 6:** https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/6 has a failing `typecheck-and-test` check. Say so if you want it waived.\n4. **robots-sl1eq:** should `brain` refuse writes when no `BEADS_DIR` is set and no local `.beads` exists? I recommend refusing.\n5. **Hold fix:** which branch to land. I recommend `fm/robots-bii4o-hold-q1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":90923,"output_tokens":525,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":546,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":525,"cache_read_input_tokens":90923,"cache_creation_input_tokens