{"parentUuid":"d20f17da-d3d3-45fc-8720-acdb6fc62b15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBVU1Uuktb8ZywEMXV9z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, I need your merge word on the two brain PRs. Both are green and the workers are done.\n\n1. **Brain PR 44:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44. This fixes `--file` and `--body-file` for remote `bd` commands. Land it first.\n2. **Brain PR 45:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45. This makes an explicit local `BEADS_DIR` win over remote forwarding (robots-gbu6f). It edits the same file as PR 44, so it goes second.\n\nThe repeated idle-worker alerts were just the PR 44 worker waiting for you. I told it to stop polling.\n\nOther decisions waiting on you:\n1. **Codex/agy batch:** \"go\" to dispatch it.\n2. **forefront-backend PR 6:** https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/6 has a failing `typecheck-and-test` check. Say so if you want it waived.\n3. **robots-sl1eq:** should `brain` refuse writes when no `BEADS_DIR` is set and no local `.beads` exists? I recommend refusing.\n4. **Hold fix:** which branch to land. I recommend `fm/robots-bii4o-hold-q1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":222,"cache_read_input_tokens":105058,"output_tokens":413,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":105058,"cache_creation_input_tokens":222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBloc