{"parentUuid":"6f75f0dc-a7f9-4daa-8cda-69149a941b09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBaGeHEFg4mvqJTFrsR9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, I found why GitHub Actions checks keep failing in 2 seconds, and only you can fix it. GitHub's own message on the failed run reads: \"The job was not started because recent account payments have failed or your spending limit needs to be increased.\"\n\n1. **Fix:** open github.com/settings/billing and check the payment method and the Actions spending limit.\n\nThis is what has been turning forefront-backend PR 6 and PR 7 red, and voicefirst-landing PR 86. The code is fine: PR 7 passes the typecheck and all 78 tests in a clean export. I recorded the cause on task-wh6t9 and task-calfm and flagged task-wh6t9 for your review. Once billing is fixed, the checks can simply be re-run, so no waiver would be needed.\n\nUsage hasn't moved: Claude has 45% left and Fable 40%, and Codex is idle. No PRs have landed.\n\nDecisions waiting on you:\n1. **Brain PR 44:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44 is green. Land it first.\n2. **Brain PR 45:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45 is green (fixes robots-gbu6f). It goes second.\n3. **Forefront-backend PR 7:** https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/7. Waive the red check, or fix billing and re-run it. I recommend fixing billing.\n4. **Codex/agy batch:** \"go\" to dispatch it.\n5. **robots-sl1eq:** should `brain` refuse writes when no `BEADS_DIR` is set and no local `.beads` exists? I recommend refusing.\n6. **Hold fix:** which branch to land. I recommend `fm/robots-bii4o-hold-q1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":655,"cache_read_input_tokens":131450,"output_tokens":588,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},