{"parentUuid":"599c469a-b466-4b7e-872f-147dda22b71e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBbpVAZNYqm5k9RgoBKn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, I triaged robots-wajev (the git hook that breaks worktree tests). I did not dispatch a fix, because the hook is part of the firstmate repo itself (`bin/fm-git-strip-ai-trailers.sh`) and this home is not allowed to publish to that repo on its own. I noted that on the bead.\n\nA fix needs your one-time consent to contribute it upstream. The same applies to robots-q22c (the turn-end guard repair loop). Say \"consent\" for either and I'll dispatch it.\n\n**Usage:** Claude has 45% left and Fable 40% (resets at midnight UTC tonight). Codex is idle. Nothing has landed since the last poke, and no workers are running.\n\nDecisions waiting on you:\n1. **Brain PR 44:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44 is green. Land it first.\n2. **Brain PR 45:** https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45 is green (fixes robots-gbu6f). It goes second.\n3. **GitHub billing:** check github.com/settings/billing. A failed payment or spending limit is stopping Actions jobs from starting, which is why forefront-backend PR 7 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/7) and PR 6 show red.\n4. **Firstmate-repo fixes:** consent for robots-wajev and robots-q22c, as above.\n5. **Codex/agy batch:** \"go\" to dispatch it.\n6. **robots-sl1eq:** should `brain` refuse writes when no `BEADS_DIR` is set and no local `.beads` exists? I recommend refusing.\n7. **Hold fix:** which branch to land. I recommend `fm/robots-bii4o-hold-q1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":138230,"output_tokens":588,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_c