{"parentUuid":"3892eb09-7b54-4916-a2c7-fa381aa2855a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c7d8279e-f259-4e9e-8405-0a99877662ff","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user repeatedly sends a standing nudge (items 1-12) asking me to:\n     - Log every action in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked).\n     - Put durable work into the right beads.\n     - Produce real work every turn. A turn with no work is a violation.\n     - Pull from the stores (robots, task, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review, projects).\n     - Keep Sidecar (project-yg4v, status-vkr, runbooks-5vr) and the Talon palette moving.\n     - Take open robots items: diagnose or dispatch a fix, and close with evidence.\n     - Check quota-axi and speed metrics every poke, and spend underused quota (prefer Fable for planning and building).\n     - Keep the queue deep and review open PRs and reports.\n   - Automated \"continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes also arrive. The text says each turn must produce real work, and not to take hands-only, destructive or still-open-choice steps.\n   - Standing rules:\n     - Inbox beads are captain messages: comment in the bead first.\n     - Scout reports go in full to the brain bead named by the inbox feed.\n     - Never merge without explicit word unless the project's yolo posture allows it, and never merge red or unreported required checks without a waiver.\n     - Never tear down unlanded work.\n     - Address the user as \"captain\" and don't expose internal terms.\n     - Output shaping for an ADHD reader.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling:\n     - `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, then `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`.\n     - `bin/fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N`.\n     - `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`.\n     - Export `FM_HOME=$PWD` for `fm-send`.\n   - Delivery flow:\n     - `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M`, then fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} via python3 -I.\n     - `fm-tasks-axi.sh add`, then `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> <project-dir> --mode M --yolo on|off --harness claude`.\n     - `fm-pr-check.sh`, `fm-pr-merge.sh`, `fm-teardown.sh`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`, `fm-crew-state.sh`.\n     - `fm-control.sh <id> relaunch --note ...`.\n     - `fm-send.sh <id> [--resolve-key KEY] 'text'`, with no `--yes`.\n   - ask-user-authority: decide in-scope findings; escalate expansions.\n   - GitHub Actions jobs fail in 2s because of an account billing problem (failed payments or spending limit). This is a captain-only fix at github.com/settings/billing.\n   - firstmate-self-repo: this home is a user/operator, so fixes in the firstmate repo's own bin/ need captain consent or a maintainer opt-in before publishing.\n   - Memory notes that applied:\n     - PAI scripts/TOOLS are deprecated.\n     - Device changes go in nix.\n     - fm-hooks and behavioral-hooks merges are mine.\n   - Quota: claude 45% / fable 40% (seven-day, resets 2026-10-20T00:00Z); codex 100% idle but the CLI is not installed on the macbook; agy ~92-95% idle; grok credentials expired; opencode 43%.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - data/brain-beadsdir-fwd-q1/nm-*-findings.txt: nm review/document findings that I decided.\n   - data/fb-green-q1/brief.md: forefront-backend repo-green brief (ship, no-mistakes, yolo off).\n   - data/bh-pai-link-q1/findings.md: the PAI/TOOLS findings (missing Inference, TranscriptParser and FailureCapture under ~/.claude/PAI/TOOLS).\n   - data/bh-pai-skip-q2/brief.md: the skip-when-absent brief.\n   - bin/fm-git-strip-ai-trailers.sh: firstmate-repo hook (robots-wajev). Not touched (gated).\n   - ~/.local/bin/fm-nudge and state/inbox-store-watch.check.sh: read-only context.\n   - Behavioral-hooks PR 30 changed tests/PromptProcessing.smoke.test.ts, tests/RestoreContext.smoke.test.ts, tests/SatisfactionCapture.smoke.test.ts, tests/e2e/SecurityPipeline.test.ts and added tests/helpers/pai-tools.ts (skip helper).\n\n4. Errors and fixes: see the analysis above (FM_HOME unset, persistent-cd hook, ScheduleWakeup denied, relaunch needing --note and failing on a dead pane, doorbell not ringing).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved and closed:\n     - robots-72p6x (fm-hooks clone clean).\n     - robots-pejry (behavioral-hooks PR 30 merged; follow-up robots-14w31).\n     - Root cause of the red Actions checks (billing), recorded on task-wh6t9, task-calfm, robots-936cm and task-ttugb.\n     - robots-xqffe diagnosed (codex CLI missing on the macbook; install task filed).\n   - Ready and awaiting the captain:\n     - Brain PR 45 (robots-gbu6f).\n     - Forefront-backend PR 7 (red only because of billing; local verify green).\n   - Ongoing: nothing actively running now (bh-pai-skip-q2 and bh-pai-link-q1 are torn down). The fb-green-q1 worker is parked at the CI gate.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Only the repeated standing nudge text (items 1-12), once including a pasted_content block. Examples: \"open robots items (robots ready/list), diagnose or dispatch a fix, and close with evidence. (11) USAGE + SPEED METRICS ... (12) MORE WORK, MORE REVIEW ...\"\n   - The earlier mid-turn question was \"what is the development plan dor tbis 5hr window? what needs vuilding or reviewing or gnhf - ing\".\n   - No \"go\", no merge, waive or land approvals, and no consent have been received. All other turns were automated notifications.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Drain the final `check: rearm-resurface` wake (needs `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, then its printed `--ack-through` command).\n   - Captain decisions pending:\n     - GitHub billing fix at github.com/settings/billing.\n     - Merge brain PR 44 (https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44), then PR 45 (https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45).\n     - Forefront-backend PR 7 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/7): waive the red check, or fix billing and re-run it (I recommend fixing billing). PR 6 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/6) has the same failure.\n     - Consent to publish firstmate-repo fixes (robots-wajev, robots-q22c, robots-d8dvl).\n     - \"go\" for the agy batch (Codex unavailable on the macbook until it is installed).\n     - robots-sl1eq design call (recommend refusing mutating verbs with no BEADS_DIR and no local .beads).\n     - Which hold-fix branch to land (recommend fm/robots-bii4o-hold-q1; discarding duplicate captain-hold-complete-q1 needs OK).\n     - inbox-cglf (which MCP tools to deactivate).\n     - Land dotfiles fm/dotfiles-nm-q1 and Share branch fm/firstmate-share-build-20261019.\n     - Many mini0-ops and macbook-ops holds.\n   - Follow-up work:\n     - Install the codex CLI via dotfiles nix (task filed).\n     - robots-14w31: remove hooks' dependency on deprecated PAI/TOOLS.\n     - task-calfm (Actions).\n     - Remaining robots candidates: robots-7iaq (upstream no-mistakes), agent-l7p and agent-0bq (duplicate-id conflicts), robots-ucj59, robots-5s8pw (firstmate repo).\n   - Keep logging each poke in status-kdv and keep the queue deep.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request, I had just merged behavioral-hooks PR 30 (robots-pejry fixed and closed), torn down worker bh-pai-skip-q2, run fleet-sync, acked outcomes through 2103 and logged to status-kdv. The final captain-facing message announced the merge and listed the pending decisions. The new Stop-hook wake `check: rearm-resurface` had not yet been drained.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Drain and acknowledge the pending `rearm-resurface` wake: run `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, handle it, then run the printed `WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED --ack-through` command. Then, on the next poke, run quota-axi, log to status-kdv, and pick another well-defined robots or task item to dispatch or diagnose (for example robots-ucj59 or the duplicate-id conflicts), re-presenting the pending captain decisions with full PR URLs.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"d6e5eee6-46e0-4bae-98dd-f39659cf5635","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:50:18.811Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":387,"turnIndex":744},"turnOrigin":"task_notification","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
