{"parentUuid":"4623bffe-ece8-49b1-aaa5-2e1db6ca2159","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a3dc1e2c-c65b-4ccd-a3ee-9aed602bce76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PFwG1sbYku9uogvjKThgRm","type":"tool_result","content":"○ agent-l7p · Unresolved duplicate-id conflict: agent-l7p (2 differing copies)   [● P1 · OPEN]\nOwner: brain-unify · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-06-21 · Updated: 2026-07-29\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  The id agent-l7p existed in 2 stores with different content. bd brain unify \n  did not pick one: it kept every copy as a bead of its own, and this bead is \n  what is left at the original id. Nothing was discarded. This conflict is    \n  unresolved.                                                                 \n                                                                              \n  Copies:                                                                     \n                                                                              \n  • brain-955cdf8f9f4b - from store brain (status closed, updated 2026-06-22  \n  19:53:27) \"cross-store links don't resolve — brain and robot are separate   \n  Dolt instances with no federation\"                                          \n  • agent-89a059e9d925 - from store robots (status closed, updated 2026-07-29 \n  16:35:08) \"cross-store links don't resolve — brain and robot are separate   \n  Dolt instances with no federation\"                                          \n                                                                              \n  Columns that differ between the copies: closed_at, notes, updated_at.       \n                                                                              \n  This bead tracks each copy (dependency type \"tracks\", which blocks nothing).\n  Links other beads hold to agent-l7p still point here, so they reach this    \n  conflict rather than either copy. Review the copies, keep what is true in   \n  one of them, close the other, then close this bead; bd brain unify has no   \n  command that does this for you. The merge record is brain_unify_collisions, \n  row agent-l7p.                                                              \n\n\n○ robots-2xsms · zsh shell snapshot defines nm as a function calling Talon mimic: nm -gU sent args to Talon speech input   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: zsh-shell-snapshot-defines-nm-as-a-function-calling-talon-mimic-nm-gu-sent-args-to-talon-speech-input\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 08:45 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Found by talon-ort-split-scout 2026-10-19: ~/.claude/shell-                 \n      snapshots/snapshot-zsh-1792399080093-gn0qgv.sh:1854 defines nm() as a Talon \n      mimic wrapper (probably a Talon voice alias leaking into shell). Running 'nm\n      -gU lib' sent '-gU' to Talon speech input (logged failed to parse phrase).  \n      Risk: arbitrary text injected as voice commands. Fix: find where nm is      \n      defined (zshrc/aliases), rename it, and keep snapshots from capturing it.   \n  2026-10-19 09:01 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Fixed in dotfiles branch fm/dotfiles-nm-q1 commit 950d67d: zshrc.pre-nix    \n      unfunctions nm after the bashrc_public chain. Verified: nm resolves to      \n      /usr/bin/nm. Build: darwin-rebuild build --flake .#macbookpro passed. Not   \n      live until rebuild.sh runs. Root fix (rename in bashrc_public","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3f0341e4-87b9-40d1-83cc-7b7b3d6d8be2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:52:10.402Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"○ agent-l7p · Unresolved duplicate-id conflict: agent-l7p (2 differing copies)   [● P1 · OPEN]\nOwner: brain-unify · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-06-21 · Updated: 2026-07-29\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  The id agent-l7p existed in 2 stores with different content. bd brain unify \n  did not pick one: it kept every copy as a bead of its own, and this bead is \n  what is left at