-ops [key=overnight-green-list] needs-decision: message 040 (repost) references overnight GREEN list work - no prior record of this request. Message is truncated. Need full message or clarification from [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=dolt-lockdown-032] needs-decision: message 032 received (add Dolt server lockdown to cutover script); acknowledged but not acted. This is project-specific brain cutover work - need clarificati [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=config-update] needs-decision: message 042 (repost) references Firstmate config/AGENTS.md update - no prior record. Need clarification or reissue from main firstmate.\nOPEN DECISIONS: 19 more omitted (byte cap)\nOPEN DECISIONS: close one by answering it: bin/fm-send.sh <task> --resolve-key <key> '<answer>'\nWARNING: queued wakes pending - drain them with bin/fm-wake-drain.sh before anything else.\nfm-inbox.sh - the captain's out-of-band capture surface.\n\nSolves three DIFFERENT problems with three different mechanisms, because they\nare not the same problem:\n\n  note    Queue an idea for firstmate while firstmate is mid-turn and cannot\n          answer. Writes a durable record and appends ONE `check` wake, so the\n          note survives a crash and is presented at firstmate's next drain.\n          `announce` may append that same wake for an already-saved note.\n          These two are the only subcommands that touch firstmate's wake queue.\n  say     Same as `note`, but the body comes from spoken audio on stdin.\n          Speech is an INPUT METHOD here, not an architecture: it transcribes\n          and then takes exactly the `note` path.\n  status  Answer \"what is happening\" from durable records ONLY. Reads no\n          network and appends NO wake, so it never interrupts work and is safe\n          to run in a loop.\n  ask     Answer a side question with a one-shot model call that never touches\n          firstmate, the backlog, or the wake queue. A side question is not\n          fleet work and must not become fleet work.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4fd959b5-4dd5-4535-aac6-f66bdafb884d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:59:13.775Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1792418334\t318416\tcheck\tinbox:1792418334-oYliF0\tcheck: captain inbox note 1792418334-oYliF0 - Continue the work already authorized. Triage open items in the task stores. If a task's next step is\nWAKE_ACK_REQUIRED: after handling completes run bin/fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 318416 --recovery-generation 96636.1792418334.Ple3Un\nOPEN DECISIONS (still open, folded from the durable status logs - not just the latest line):\ncaptain-hold-complete-q1 blocked: fix committed at 0db5dd53 on f650e380 lineage (same fix as sibling fm/robots-bii4o-hold-q1 fcb53f6d, duplicate task); cannot rebase onto main 3d2c80a4 because that line has  [truncated]\nmacbook-ops [key=vf-deck-dev-server] blocked: corr=589b856820d0e172 corr=b6e2ccebed6ee06b PR 72 MERGED https://github.com/trillium/voicefirst-landing/pull/72; dev server UP (200) https://macbook.hippo-tilapi [truncated]\nmacbook-ops needs-decision: inbox-cglf (Activate Apple Notes MCP, deactivate first MCP tools): Apple Notes part done (enabled, in chatgpt group, 51 tools live). Deactivate part needs the target: firstmate_mc [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=captain-hold-github-profile-improvements-1] needs-decision: captain hold github-profile-improvements: Which GitHub profile improvements to make (report: data/github-profile-review/report.md se [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=captain-hold-iphone-projects-reconcile-1] needs-decision: captain hold iphone-projects-reconcile: Which record clean-ups to apply in the brain project store (report: data/iphone-projects-statu [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=captain-hold-brain-beads-cleanup-1] needs-decision: captain hold brain-beads-cleanup: Apply the brain-bead clean-ups from data/brain-beads-report/report.md section 7? 1 update the brain projec [truncated]\nmini0-ops [key=captain-hold-brain-day-week-followup-1] needs-decision: captain hold brain-day-week-