{"parentUuid":"87b398eb-eb27-4d2d-a626-a76dddb2e804","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3f670c0-e74f-414a-847c-b1453f15f8f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Zhf5CLEwb9XEezcxkm5Wd","type":"tool_result","content":"○ robots-14w31 · Hooks still import deprecated PAI/TOOLS; remove the real dependency (robots-pejry follow-up)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: hooks-still-import-deprecated-pai-tools-remove-the-real-dependency-robots-pejry-follow-up\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 13:45 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Follow-up from robots-pejry (PR https://github.com/trillium/behavioral-     \n      hooks/pull/30). Tests now skip with a [skip] reason when PAI/TOOLS is       \n      absent, but the hooks still import the deprecated modules and fail to load  \n      without them. Files that import PAI/TOOLS:                                  \n      security/inspectors/RulesInspector.ts (Inference), events/session-          \n      end/RelationshipMemory.hook.ts and IntegrityCheck.hook.ts                   \n      (TranscriptParser), events/prompt/SatisfactionCapture.hook.ts (Inference,   \n      FailureCapture), events/prompt/PromptProcessing/dispatch.ts (Inference),    \n      handlers/SystemIntegrity.ts, handlers/TabState.ts (TranscriptParser type),  \n      handlers/DocCrossRefIntegrity.ts (Inference, TranscriptParser). Fix         \n      direction: remove the dependency from hooks (replace with lib/ equivalents, \n      as lib/transcript-parser.ts already does) and then drop the skip gate in    \n      tests/helpers/pai-tools.ts. Hook behavior change is out of scope for robots-\n      pejry.                                                                      \n\n- behavioral-hooks [direct-PR +yolo] - PAI lifecycle hooks: per-event dispatchers on a shared error-isolated core, incl. Stop BehaviorEnforcement modules; private origin trillium/behavioral-hooks, yolo on per captain 2026-10-17 (added 2026-10-17)\n# robots-pejry: PAI symlink in treehouse worktree\n\n## Reproduced\n- Baseline `./scripts/bun-test-safe tests/` in worktree: 909 pass, 24 fail (log: baseline.log).\n- Direct hook run fails at load: `Cannot find module '../../PAI/TOOLS/Inference.ts'`.\n\n## Why the symlink alone is not the fix\n- Tracked `PAI -> ../../.claude/PAI`. From a treehouse worktree this points to\n  `~/.treehouse/behavioral-hooks-ea2869/.claude/PAI` (nonexistent). Primary checkout's link is also dangling.\n- Fallback target `$HOME/.claude/PAI` exists but has only `MEMORY/` and `logs/`; no `TOOLS/`.\n- Modules the code imports from PAI/TOOLS: Inference, TranscriptParser, FailureCapture.\n- Copies of the full PAI tree exist only under `~/.claude/.worktrees/*/PAI` and\n  `~/.treehouse/.claude-9c6558/1/.claude/PAI`. Depending on them would couple tests to another slot.\n- No tracked file in this repo provides `TOOLS/Inference`.\n\n## Options for the captain/firstmate\n1. Restore the PAI/TOOLS tree at `~/.claude/PAI` on this machine. Then the symlink fallback or the existing link resolves everywhere.\n2. Make PAI/TOOLS imports optional in hooks (hook behavior change; out of scope per brief).\n3. Skip or stub the 24 tests when PAI/TOOLS is absent (weakens coverage).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e8ea6ea1-c0f7-42a1-993d-c6d3b9336511","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:59:17.561Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"○ robots-14w31 · Hooks still import deprecated PAI/TOOLS; remove the real dependency (robots-pejry follow-up)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: hooks-still-import-deprecated-pai-tools-remove-the-real-dependency-robots-pejry-follow-up\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 13:45 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Follow-up from robots-pejry (PR https://github.com/trillium/behavioral-     \n      hooks/pull/30). Tests now skip with a [skip] reason when PAI/TOOLS is       \n      absent, but the hooks still import the deprecated modules and fail to load  \n      without them. Files that import PAI/TOOLS:                                  \n      security/inspectors/RulesInspector.ts (Inference), events/session-          \n      end/RelationshipMemory.hook.ts and IntegrityCheck.hook.ts                   \n      (TranscriptParser), events/prompt/SatisfactionCapture.hook.ts (Inference,   \n      FailureCapture), events/prompt/PromptProcessing/dispatch.ts (Inference),    \n      handlers/SystemIntegrity.ts, handlers/TabState.ts (TranscriptParser type),  \n      handlers/DocCrossRefIntegrity.ts (Inference, TranscriptParser). Fix         \n      direction: remove the dependency from hooks (replace with lib/ equivalents, \n      as lib/transcript-parser.ts already does) and then drop the skip gate in    \n      tests/helpers/pai-tools.ts. Hook behavior change is out of scope for robots-\n      pejry.                                                                      \n\n- behavioral-hooks [direct-PR +yolo] - PAI lifecycle hooks: per-event dispatchers on a shared error-isolated core, incl. Stop BehaviorEnforcement modules; private origin trillium/behavioral-hooks, yolo on per captain 2026-10-17 (added 2026-10-17)\n# robots-pejry: PAI symlink in treehouse worktree\n\n## Reproduced\n- Baseline `./scripts/bun-test-safe tests/` in worktree: 909 pass, 24 fail (log: baseline.log).\n- Direct hook run fails at load: `Cannot find module '../../PAI/TOOLS/Inference.ts'`.\n\n## Why the symlink alone is not the fix\n- Tracked `PAI -> ../../.claude/PAI`. From a treehouse worktree this points to\n  `~/.treehouse/behavioral-hooks-ea2869/.claude/PAI` (nonexistent). Primary checkout's link is also dangling.\n- Fallback target `$HOME/.claude/PAI` exists but has only `MEMORY/` and `logs/`; no `TOOLS/`.\n- Modules the code imports from PAI/TOOLS: Inference, TranscriptParser, FailureCapture.\n- Copies of the full PAI tree exist only under `~/.claude/.worktrees/*/PAI` and\n  `~/.treehouse/.claude-9c6558/1/.claude/PAI`. Depending on them would couple tests to another slot.\n- No tracked file in this repo provides `TOOLS/Inference`.\n\n## Options for the captain/firstmate\n1. Restore the PAI/TOOLS tree at `~/.claude/PAI` on this machine. Then the symlink fallback or the existing link resolves everywhere.\n2. Make PAI/TOOLS imports optional in hooks (hook behavior change; out of scope per brief).\n3. Skip or stub the 24 tests when PAI/TOOLS is absent (weakens coverage).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"87b398eb-eb27-4d2d-a626-a76dddb2e804","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
