anch fm/robots-fy7f9-fix (ecf29e0): hermetic guard     \ndata/projects.md\n- iphone-contacts-sync [local-only] - local iPhone<->macOS contact sync/merge tool (Swift iOS app + Bun/TS cli/server/web), LAN + Tailscale, no cloud; union-merge + staleness detection (flagged 1920 s","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"92f3e40c-4004-4336-afea-1b53c8b125b8","timestamp":"2026-10-19T14:32:00.403Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"quota[9]{provider,scope,effectivePercentRemaining,spendPriority,runway,confidence,limitedBy,resetsAt}:\n  claude,all_models,45,7.2201,through_reset,established,seven_day,\"2026-10-20T00:00:00.453072+00:00\"\n  claude,\"model:fable\",40,6.8469,through_reset,established,\"model:fable\",\"2026-10-20T00:00:00.453239+00:00\"\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: iphone-contacts-sync-approve-job-test-read-the-real-mac-address-book-and-wrote-a-backup-under-backups\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 07:16 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Progress (branch fm/robots-fy7f9-fix, commit ecf29e0, local-only): the      \n      approve-job test is NOT on main. It lives on the unmerged fm/task-cemye     \n      lineage (ce78ca0), where it already injects backupSource.readMac and        \n      CONTACTSYNC_BACKUP_ROOT. On main I added the guard: bunfig [test] preload   \n      sets a temp backup root and CONTACTSYNC_HERMETIC=1 for the whole bun test   \n      run. Under it, findAddressBookDb / JXA read / backupRoot() on the real      \n      ~/Backups throw loudly. Only macos-sqlite integration test opts in (read-   \n      only). Production defaults unchanged when the guard is off. Suite: 96 pass. \n      Cleanup: listed ~/Backups/iphone-contacts-sync; deleted the two test        \n      artifacts apply-2026-10-18T19-52-52-340Z and apply-2026-10-18T19-54-00-724Z \n      (journal phone ids a/b/bad = approve-job fixtures, iPhone count 0, predate  \n      fix ce78ca0). Left toastmasters-purge-20261015 (real purge backup). Open:   \n      when fm/task-cemye lands, the approve-job test is covered by the preload; 