{"parentUuid":"ea7f9102-99bd-4053-b50b-0c7bc8af126f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBm17wiLuu8fXUaL4bhE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, a worker is now on robots-qi64x, the brain bug where `--file` and `--body-file` paths aren't rewritten when a command is forwarded to a remote host. It reproduces first, then fixes and adds a test. It ships through the full validation pipeline, and I'll tell you when the PR is up.\n\nAnother robots item, robots-fy7f9, has a fix ready on a local branch, but it needs your OK to land. The iphone-contacts-sync tests were reading the real Mac address book and writing a backup under `~/Backups`. The fix makes them hermetic, with 96 tests passing. Say \"land fm/robots-fy7f9-fix\" and I'll merge it.\n\nUsage is unchanged: Claude has 45% left and Fable 40%, resetting 2026-10-20 at 00:00 UTC. Everything is logged in status-kdv.\n\nStill waiting on you:\n1. Fix GitHub billing at github.com/settings/billing.\n2. Merge brain PR 44 (https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44), then PR 45 (https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45).\n3. Decide forefront-backend PR 7 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/7). Either waive the red check or fix billing and re-run it. I recommend fixing billing.\n4. Give consent to publish fixes in the firstmate repo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1162,"cache_read_input_tokens":121286,"output_tokens":466,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1162,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":121286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens