{"parentUuid":"6c315e74-3a74-4f9d-9114-46947a16cfa9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"22406f96-20cc-4cc6-9fc1-a6c126c23bbd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcSm18ZKDYkksz4p9YY7a7","type":"tool_result","content":"run: 01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4\nbranch: fm/brain-fwd-file-q2\npipeline head: 62a696a783587e9f469ef8244637e9bc6143cb2c\ngate: review (fix_review, risk medium)\nnote: the IDs from firstmate's decision for key REDACTED (intent-create-batch-comments-file-rejected, simplify-duplicate-local-file-flags) are NOT present in this gate. The gate now lists review-1..review-4 below.\n\nid: review-1\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: auto-fix (authorized: fix)\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"An explicit \"-\" value bypasses the one-stdin-per-command invariant. The \"-\" branch continues without claiming the single file slot, so `brain create t --body-file - --description-file plan.md` sends plan.md as stdin while the host also receives `--body-file -`. Both flags read the same stdin stream, so one of them gets the file and the other gets nothing, with no error. Remedy: count an explicit \"-\" as occupying the stdin slot, so combining it with a local file returns the existing \"only one of ...\" error.\"\n\nid: review-2\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"When a local file flag is present, the caller's piped stdin is silently discarded. `echo notes | brain update bd-1 --body-file plan.md` replaces stdin with plan.md and sets tty=false, so the piped data is dropped with no error. Remedy (an error for piped stdin plus a file flag) adds new behavior, so it needs authorization.\"\n\nid: review-3\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"The subcommand is taken as args[0], but maybeForwardRemote receives raw os.Args[1:] (main.go:1632), and root persistent flags such as --json, --actor and --db are accepted before the subcommand. `brain --json create t --body-file plan.md` sets command=\"--json\" and fails with the misleading \"--json --body-file is not supported when forwarded\", so the feature is unavailable for that invocation form. The fix needs to know which root flags take a value, which is a design decision, so it needs authorization.\"\n\nid: review-4\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"Intent conformance, recorded decision: the criterion \"make forwarded commands work with those flags (e.g. transfer the file content or inline it...)\" is REQUIRED. Lines 411-416 reject `--file` for `create`, `batch` and `comments add` client-side, and TestForwardRejectsLocalFileFlagsTheHostCannotRead asserts that rejection. This matches the Firstmate narrowing for nm-01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4 (full support tracked in task-tywam), so it is authorized. Confirm the rejection is accepted for those three commands and not full support.\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5d03e7ce-cf3f-4193-9be0-5f9f1cd223f0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:10:15.319Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"run: 01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4\nbranch: fm/brain-fwd-file-q2\npipeline head: 62a696a783587e9f469ef8244637e9bc6143cb2c\ngate: review (fix_review, risk medium)\nnote: the IDs from firstmate's decision for key REDACTED (intent-create-batch-comments-file-rejected, simplify-duplicate-local-file-flags) are NOT present in this gate. The gate now lists review-1..review-4 below.\n\nid: review-1\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: auto-fix (authorized: fix)\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"An explicit \"-\" value bypasses the one-stdin-per-command invariant. The \"-\" branch continues without claiming the single file slot, so `brain create t --body-file - --description-file plan.md` sends plan.md as stdin while the host also receives `--body-file -`. Both flags read the same stdin stream, so one of them gets the file and the other gets nothing, with no error. Remedy: count an explicit \"-\" as occupying the stdin slot, so combining it with a local file returns the existing \"only one of ...\" error.\"\n\nid: review-2\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"When a local file flag is present, the caller's piped stdin is silently discarded. `echo notes | brain update bd-1 --body-file plan.md` replaces stdin with plan.md and sets tty=false, so the piped data is dropped with no error. Remedy (an error for piped stdin plus a file flag) adds new behavior, so it needs authorization.\"\n\nid: review-3\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"The subcommand is taken as args[0], but maybeForwardRemote receives raw os.Args[1:] (main.go:1632), and root persistent flags such as --json, --actor and --db are accepted before the subcommand. `brain --json create t --body-file plan.md` sets command=\"--json\" and fails with the misleading \"--json --body-file is not supported when forwarded\", so the feature is unavailable for that invocation form. The fix needs to know which root flags take a value, which is a design decision, so it needs authorization.\"\n\nid: review-4\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"Intent conformance, recorded decision: the criterion \"make forwarded commands work with those flags (e.g. transfer the file content or inline it...)\" is REQUIRED. Lines 411-416 reject `--file` for `create`, `batch` and `comments add` client-side, and TestForwardRejectsLocalFileFlagsTheHostCannotRead asserts that rejection. This matches the Firstmate narrowing for nm-01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4 (full support tracked in task-tywam), so it is authorized. Confirm the rejection is accepted for those three commands and not full support.\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c315e74-3a74-4f9d-9114-46947a16