{"parentUuid":"3fad3f6b-2c75-476b-a76e-d1e7da2bff3c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9e449bb3-84a6-4eb3-97bb-d16823c2b4f9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUxbTZgCvpKpBh7MNYT2bR","type":"tool_result","content":"REDACTED.txt\nREDACTED.txt\nREDACTED.txt\npaused [at=1792422633]: review fix round applying review-1; waiting for next gate or outcome (reattach with axi run). Deferred review-2/3/4 recorded in task-tywam\nneeds-decision [at=1792422723] [REDACTED]: ask-user findings=dep-add-file-regression,intent-create-batch-comments-file-rejected,simplify-duplicate-local-file-flags file=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/brain-fwd-file-q2/REDACTED.txt ; dep-add-file-regression is NEW and is a regression I introduced (brain dep \nrun: 01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4\nbranch: fm/brain-fwd-file-q2\npipeline head: 8275089882040ef7bba1a788b171a005e0ba067a (fix rounds 1-3 applied)\ngate: review (fix_review, risk medium)\n\nid: dep-add-file-regression\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim as displayed by `no-mistakes axi status`; the CLI truncates at \"(truncated, 911 chars total)\" - the full text is not recoverable from the CLI):\n\"Regression beyond the recorded Firstmate narrowing. localFileFlags matches `--file` for every subcommand, and the check at line 415 rejects any command not in stdinFileFlags before the value is examined. `dep add --file` is not in the table, so it is now rejected client-side. Before this change it was forwarded unchanged. Its host command reads `--file` as JSONL and accepts `-` for stdin (cmd/bd/dep.go:1536, :538). Trace: `cat edges.jsonl | brain dep add bd-1 bd-2 --file -` worked by stdin passthrough and now fails with \"dep --file is not supported when forwarded\" before the `value == \"-\"` br\n\nid: intent-create-batch-comments-file-rejected\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"Intent conformance. The required criterion is \"make forwarded commands work with those flags (e.g. transfer the file content or inline it...)\". Lines 412-416 reject `--file` client-side for create, batch and comments add, and TestForwardRejectsLocalFileFlagsTheHostCannotRead asserts that rejection. This is the narrowing recorded as a Firstmate decision for nm-01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4, with full support tracked in task-tywam, so it is authorized. The required criterion is still not met for these three commands, so confirm rejection is the accepted outcome rather than full support.\"\nnote: same finding as review-4 in fix3; firstmate decided SKIP (004.msg).\n\nid: simplify-duplicate-local-file-flags\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"Unrequired component: localFileFlags (line 391) is a second definition of the flag set already held by stdinFileFlags (lines 376-385). The duplicate is the reason a new subcommand can be rejected without being listed in the table. Remove it and derive the flag set from stdinFileFlags, or keep only the table. Also, the `create` and `new` entries duplicate each other; canonicalizing the alias would remove that copy too. Removal is the smallest honest remedy and needs authorization.\"\nnote: firstmate decided FIX (003.msg: drop localFileFlags, keep stdinFileFlags only). Not yet applied.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"513c3ca7-63ec-4626-a7a0-70ffec16a463","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:12:23.008Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"REDACTED.txt\nREDACTED.txt\nREDACTED.txt\npaused [at=1792422633]: review fix round applying review-1; waiting for next gate or outcome (reattach with axi run). Deferred review-2/3/4 recorded in task-tywam\nneeds-decision [at=1792422723] [REDACTED]: ask-user findings=dep-add-file-regression,intent-create-batch-comments-file-rejected,simplify-duplicate-local-file-flags file=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/brain-fwd-file-q2/REDACTED.txt ; dep-add-file-regression is NEW and is a regression I introduced (brain dep \nrun: 01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4\nbranch: fm/brain-fwd-file-q2\npipeline head: 8275089882040ef7bba1a788b171a005e0ba067a (fix rounds 1-3 applied)\ngate: review (fix_review, risk medium)\n\nid: dep-add-file-regression\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim as displayed by `no-mistakes axi status`; the CLI truncates at \"(truncated, 911 chars total)\" - the full text is not recoverable from the CLI):\n\"Regression beyond the recorded Firstmate narrowing. localFileFlags matches `--file` for every subcommand, and the check at line 415 rejects any command not in stdinFileFlags before the value is examined. `dep add --file` is not in the table, so it is now rejected client-side. Before this change it was forwarded unchanged. Its host command reads `--file` as JSONL and accepts `-` for stdin (cmd/bd/dep.go:1536, :538). Trace: `cat edges.jsonl | brain dep add bd-1 bd-2 --file -` worked by stdin passthrough and now fails with \"dep --file is not supported when forwarded\" before the `value == \"-\"` br\n\nid: intent-create-batch-comments-file-rejected\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"Intent conformance. The required criterion is \"make forwarded commands work with those flags (e.g. transfer the file content or inline it...)\". Lines 412-416 reject `--file` client-side for create, batch and comments add, and TestForwardRejectsLocalFileFlagsTheHostCannotRead asserts that rejection. This is the narrowing recorded as a Firstmate decision for nm-01M5AAW7MWP1X1WHWAFV0PEBP4, with full support tracked in task-tywam, so it is authorized. The required criterion is still not met for these three commands, so confirm rejection is the accepted outcome rather than full support.\"\nnote: same finding as review-4 in fix3; firstmate decided SKIP (004.msg).\n\nid: simplify-duplicate-local-file-flags\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\naction: ask-user\ndescription (verbatim):\n\"Unrequired component: localFileFlags (line 391) is a second definition of the flag set already held by stdinFileFlags (lines 376-385). The duplicate is the reason a new subcommand can be rejected without being listed in the table. Remove it and derive the flag set from stdinFileFlags, or keep only the table. Also, the `create` and `new` entries duplicate each other; canonicalizing the alias would remove that copy too. Removal is the smallest honest remedy and needs authorization.\"\nnote: firstmate decided FIX (003.msg: drop localFileFlags, keep stdinFileFlags only). Not yet applied.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3fad3f6b-2c75-476b-a76e-d1e7da2bff3c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
