{"parentUuid":"11dc9b9c-f32f-43ea-9966-357f1eb685df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBp2YopqBgZbCjX6HuAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, the brain worker for robots-qi64x is on its fourth review round, and I answered it.\n\n1. **`dep add --file -` regression:** fixed. The new rejection broke piping a file into it, so the worker restores the old behavior and adds a test.\n2. **Duplicate flag list:** fixed, as decided earlier.\n3. **`create`, `batch` and `comments add` with `--file`:** skipped. The clear-error narrowing stays, and full support is tracked in task-tywam.\n\nThe worker keeps going and I'll bring you the PR link.\n\n**Usage:** Claude has 44% left and Fable 40%, with the window resetting 2026-10-20 at 00:00 UTC. One worker is busy and nothing else is running. That's still underspent, but the queue is thin on safe, well-defined work.\n\nStill waiting on you:\n1. Fix GitHub billing at github.com/settings/billing.\n2. Merge brain PR 44 (https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/44), then PR 45 (https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45).\n3. Decide forefront-backend PR 7 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/7). Either waive the red check or fix billing and re-run it. I recommend fixing billing.\n4. Decide Barterboo PR 2 (https://github.com/trillium/barter/pull/2). Merge it despite the red checks, or hold until billing is fixed.\n5. Say \"land fm/robots-fy7f9-fix\" to merge the iphone-contacts-sync test fix.\n6. Give consent to publish fixes in the firstmate repo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":144135,"output_tokens":546,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":612,"ephemeral_5m_i