{"parentUuid":"ed7f6901-c38e-4f11-9811-a40f8838fe41","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0ba5edb2-a768-403d-a9b0-27e23d57a0e2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VjzcPincWbBowrgefW3EC5","type":"tool_result","content":"Run: 01M5ADTD1Y6NH82Q5ZKF42ZGTZ  step: review (fix round 1)  pipeline head: 0b8b09deeb77c93cd753025ee47173457ddc2b23\nVerbatim from `no-mistakes axi status --run 01M5ADTD1Y6NH82Q5ZKF42ZGTZ` (tool truncates finding text at 641 chars)\n\nreview-1 | severity=warning | file=cmd/bd/bootstrap.go | action=ask-user\ndescription: \"The new executeBootstrapPlan guard refuses every non-sync action when bootstrap resolves server mode. For a fresh server-mode store with no server database, init/restore/jsonl-import now fail with a message telling the operator to 'connect to its dolt server', but bootstrap has no path to create that database: executeInitAction, executeRestoreAction and executeJSONLImportAction build a dolt.Config without ServerMode, so they would have taken the embedded path. The result is a dead end with no in-tool way forward. Routing those actions through the server store would be new behavior beyond the i… (truncated)\"\n\nreview-2 | severity=info | file=cmd/bd/bootstrap_server_mode_guard_test.go | action=auto-fix (pipeline applying)\ndescription: \"The case named 'server-mode config inherited from parent workspace' does not exercise findParentConfig. It builds an in-memory config with DoltMode=server and never writes metadata or a parent workspace. The name overstates coverage of the parent-config path that the author called out in the comment.\"\nREDACTED","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"561ffe0d-c196-4da8-b8e5-a32a040993a0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:02:03.279Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Run: 01M5ADTD1Y6NH82Q5ZKF42ZGTZ  step: review (fix round 1)  pipeline head: 0b8b09deeb77c93cd753025ee47173457ddc2b23\nVerbatim from `no-mistakes axi status --run 01M5ADTD1Y6NH82Q5ZKF42ZGTZ` (tool truncates finding text at 641 chars)\n\nreview-1 | severity=warning | file=cmd/bd/bootstrap.go | action=ask-user\ndescription: \"The new executeBootstrapPlan guard refuses every non-sync action when bootstrap resolves server mode. For a fresh server-mode store with no server database, init/restore/jsonl-import now fail with a message telling the operator to 'connect to its dolt server', but bootstrap has no path to create that database: executeInitAction, executeRestoreAction and executeJSONLImportAction build a dolt.Config without ServerMode, so they would have taken the embedded path. The result is a dead end with no in-tool way forward. Routing those actions through the server store would be new behavior beyond the i… (truncated)\"\n\nreview-2 | severity=info | file=cmd/bd/bootstrap_server_mode_guard_test.go | action=auto-fix (pipeline applying)\ndescription: \"The case named 'server-mode config inherited from parent workspace' does not exercise findParentConfig. It builds an in-memory config with DoltMode=server and never writes metadata or a parent workspace. The name overstates coverage of the parent-config path that the author called out in the comment.\"\nREDACTED","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed7f6901-c38e-4f11-9811-a40f8838fe41","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
