usually use this for PRs): main\n\nGit user: Trillium Smith\n\nStatus:\nM .claude/settings.json\n M .codex/hooks.json\n M .cursor/hooks.json\n M CHANGELOG.md\n?? .agents/hooks.json\n?? .entire/\n?? .opencode/plugins/entire.ts\n\nRecent commits:\nf650e380 fix(hooks): restore FM_GIT_HOOK_ACTIVE re-entrancy sentinel in generated wrappers\n58d4b73d chore: commit stray local working files so main is clean for local-only landing\n653d7cdb Merge remote-tracking branch 'upstream/main'\n9b1ada04 fix(bin): let a backlog captain hold bound the watcher's wedge escalation (#7338)\n4f77bb37 fix(bin): retry transient contribution forge reads once before waking (#7302)\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"33694ea7-ac82-4580-b7b1-17e35bb1f28c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"date","date":"2026-10-19"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3b90f29d-a780-4a93-8494-33d1f4b0dba6","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:10:41.298Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nToday's date is 2026-10-19.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"3b90f29d-a780-4a93-8494-33d1f4b0dba6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f2b7f3b3-ffc3-418c-8a3b-3ba7a3ca2589","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user repeatedly sends a standing nudge (items 1-12). It asks me to:\n     - Log every action in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked).\n     - Put durable work in the right beads.\n     - Produce real work every turn. A turn with no work is a violation.\n     - Pull from the stores (robots, task, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review, projects).\n     - Keep Sidecar (project-yg4v, status-vkr, runbooks-5vr) and the Talon palette (project-7u7w, idea-7d0b) moving.\n     - Take open robots items: diagnose or dispatch a fix, and close with evidence.\n     - Check quota-axi and speed metrics every poke, and take on more work if usage is underspent (prefer Fable).\n     - Keep the queue deep and review PRs and reports.\n   - Automated \"Continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes also arrive. They say each turn must produce real work, and not to take hands-only, destructive or still-open-choice steps.\n   - Standing rules:\n     - Inbox beads are captain messages: comment in the bead first.\n     - Never merge without explicit word unless the project's yolo posture allows it, and never merge red or unreported required checks without a waiver.\n     - Never tear down unlanded work.\n     - Address the user as \"captain\", and don't expose internal terms.\n     - Output shaping for an ADHD reader: lead with the action, numbered steps, state the win, and give a full PR URL with each PR mention.\n     - File tooling defects in `robots`.\n     - firstmate-repo fixes need captain consent before publishing.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling:\n     - `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, then `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`.\n     - `bin/fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N` (it errors if the seq isn't an unprocessed captain outcome).\n     - `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`.\n     - Export `FM_HOME=$PWD`.\n   - Delivery flow:\n     - `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M`, then fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} via python3 -I. Read the file before opening it for write.\n     - `fm-tasks-axi.sh add <id> '<title>' --kind ship`.\n     - `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> projects/<p> --mode M --yolo on|off --harness claude`.\n     - `fm-pr-check.sh <id> <PR url>`.\n     - `fm-pr-merge.sh <id> <PR url>`.\n     - `fm-teardown.sh`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`, `fm-crew-state.sh <id>`.\n     - `fm-send.sh <id> [--resolve-key KEY] 'text'`, no `--yes`.\n   - ask-user-authority: decide in-scope or unambiguous findings, skip contract expansions, and record deferrals in a follow-up bead (task-tywam).\n   - GitHub Actions jobs fail in about 2s because of an account billing problem. This is a captain-only fix at github.com/settings/billing.\n   - Project postures:\n     - behavioral-hooks and fm-hooks (firstmate_hooks): direct-PR +yolo, so I merge.\n     - brain: no-mistakes, yolo off, captain merges.\n     - barter: no-mistakes-prod-only, yolo off.\n     - iphone-contacts-sync: local-only.\n   - Memory notes that applied:\n     - Device changes go in nix (dotfiles).\n     - fm-hooks and behavioral-hooks merges are mine.\n     - PAI TOOLS are deprecated.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - data/bh-pai-drop-q3, data/fh-ledger-fp-q1, data/brain-fwd-file-q2, data/brain-bootstrap-q3 (brief.md and nm-*-findings.txt): worker briefs and review findings I decided.\n   - state/operational-inbox/handled/: created as a local workaround for robots-5s8pw. The root fix (the ack step should `mkdir -p`) is in firstmate bin/ and is gated.\n   - ~/.fm-hooks/queue/events/a934f44e...-fm-fleet-ledger.sh.json: evidence for the fm-hooks false positive.\n   - The brain worker's code (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go, internal/configfile/configfile.go with CheckEmbeddedCreateAllowed, cmd/bd/bootstrap.go with executeBootstrapPlan, cmd/bd/bootstrap_server_mode_guard_test.go) is in the brain worktrees, and I have not edited it myself.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `fm-pr-merge.sh bh-pai-drop-q3` alone gave \"invalid PR merge request\". Fix: pass the PR URL as the second arg.\n   - A python `open(p,'w')` before the read emptied the brief. I deleted and rescaffolded it.\n   - `fm-spawn` refused until the backlog item was added (`fm-tasks-axi.sh add ... --kind ship`).\n   - `mark-processed --through 2107` and `--through 2110` were refused because the seq wasn't a captain outcome. That's harmless.\n   - The `fm-tasks-axi add` flags `--project` and `--note` are invalid.\n   - A persistent-cd hook denied a `cd` into projects/fm-hooks. I used absolute paths.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved and closed:\n     - behavioral-hooks PR 31 merged (https://github.com/trillium/behavioral-hooks/pull/31): robots-14w31 closed.\n     - firstmate_hooks PR 7 merged (https://github.com/trillium/firstmate_hooks/pull/7): task-37b80163 closed.\n     - Duplicate-id conflicts agent-l7p and agent-0bq closed.\n     - robots-k7rob closed as a duplicate of robots-2xsms.\n     - robots-6izjm closed as a misplaced comment.\n   - Ready and awaiting the captain:\n     - brain PR 46 (robots-qi64x): https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/46.\n     - Brain PRs 44 and 45.\n     - Barterboo PR 2.\n     - Forefront-backend PR 7.\n   - Ongoing: brain-bootstrap-q3 is parked at a test-step ask-user finding.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Only the repeated standing nudge text (items 1-12, once including a pasted_content block), plus automated system notifications saying no human input was received.\n   - No \"go\", merge, waive or land approvals, and no consent, have been received.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Answer the brain-bootstrap-q3 test-gate decision (key REDACTED) and ack wake 318469. The ack command is `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 318469 --recovery-generation 26328.1792426131.agP1fG`.\n   - Record the mini1 finding. A stray `/Users/mini1/data/brain/.beads/embeddeddolt` exists, created Oct 19 09:04. It is likely a side effect of the worker's un-isolated live runs (BRAIN_REMOTE not off). File a robots/task bead for cleanup. Move it to `~/data/_retired/embeddeddolt-<date>` per the precedent from robots-ucj59, and don't delete it without a recorded decision. Tell the worker to run any further live tests with BRAIN_REMOTE=off or isolated.\n   - Captain decisions pending:\n     - Fix GitHub billing.\n     - Merge brain PR 44, then 45, then 46.\n     - Forefront-backend PR 7: waive the red check, or fix billing and re-run it. I recommend fixing billing.\n     - Barterboo PR 2 (https://github.com/trillium/barter/pull/2): merge it despite the red checks, or hold.\n     - \"land fm/robots-fy7f9-fix\" for the iphone-contacts-sync test fix.\n     - Consent to publish firstmate-repo fixes (robots-q22c, robots-wajev, robots-5s8pw root, robots-d8dvl).\n     - Reply in inbox-kv6b with the product-judgment claim.\n     - Codex install via dotfiles nix.\n     - robots-sl1eq design call.\n     - The hold-fix branch choice.\n     - Many mini0-ops and macbook-ops holds.\n   - Follow-ups: task-tywam (full `--file`/`-f` support), the mini1 fwd.py bind task (idea-dko0), the Sidecar and palette tasks (task-eykz1, task-rge87, task-oahqr, task-myaks), and robots-7iaq.\n   - Keep logging each poke in status-kdv and keep the queue deep.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The brain-bootstrap-q3 ship (robots-ucj59, brain, no-mistakes, yolo off, commit 052207f06 plus pipeline fixes) is parked at the test step with finding test-2 (ask-user). The worker's early live bootstrap runs weren't BRAIN_REMOTE=off, so the wrapper forwarded them over ssh to mini1, and a remote fresh-database attempt may have happened. I ran a read-only ssh check of mini1. It found `/Users/mini1/data/brain/.beads/embeddeddolt` (created Oct 19 09:04, `last-touched` 09:09), which confirms a stray embedded dolt dir inside the server-mode brain store. I had not yet replied to the gate or recorded the finding.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Answer the gate with `bin/fm-send.sh brain-bootstrap-q3 --resolve-key REDACTED '<decision>'`. The decision:\n   - Acknowledge test-2.\n   - Forbid further un-isolated live runs; require BRAIN_REMOTE=off.\n   - State that firstmate handles the mini1 cleanup.\n   - Tell the worker to continue to the PR.\n\n   Then:\n   1. File a robots/task bead for the stray `~/data/brain/.beads/embeddeddolt` on mini1, and move it to `_retired` via ssh after confirming it holds only bootstrap files.\n   2. Run `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 318469 --recovery-generation 26328.1792426131.agP1fG`.\n   3. Log in status-kdv.\n   4. Re-present the pending captain decisions with full PR URLs.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"d9b597cf-252c-4a16-ade2-73641789211e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:10:23.072Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":394,"turnIndex":767},"turnOrigin":"task_notification","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":