{"parentUuid":"dcf7c109-44cf-40c6-b17a-b0834b918a80","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8d72f6b7-7ce0-4ad4-bebf-53581fc7c9f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QiHSw7ABcjqnhc6ppp9iKh","type":"tool_result","content":"○ robots-gbu6f · bd ignores BEADS_DIR when HOME points at the real home: store resolves to ~/data/brain   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: bd-ignores-beads-dir-when-home-points-at-the-real-home-store-resolves-to-data-brain\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 10:28 Trillium Smith\n    \n      firstmate: dispatching diagnosis scout bd-store-resolution-scout-q1 (brain  \n      project, read-only); report data/bd-store-resolution-scout-q1/report.md.    \n  2026-10-19 10:35 Trillium Smith\n    \n      # bd store-resolution scout (robots-gbu6f, robots-sl1eq)                    \n                                                                                  \n      **Verdict:** Both defects reproduce, and they share one root cause: client- \n      mode forwarding in brain runs before any BEADS_DIR logic and depends only on\n      $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. gbu6f (BEADS_DIR ignored) is a one-guard   \n      fix. sl1eq (foreign store absorbs writes) needs a design call on what bare  \n      brain means in client mode.                                                 \n                                                                                  \n      Workaround today: BRAIN_REMOTE=off <command> runs locally and honors        \n      BEADS_DIR.                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n      ## What I did                                                               \n                                                                                  \n----\n○ robots-3ov0r · edge.sh apply hardcodes mode 644 on Caddy site files and would re-expose rotated secrets (follow-up from task-3nuud)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: edge-sh-apply-hardcodes-mode-644-on-caddy-site-files-and-would-re-expose-rotated-secrets-follow-up-from-task-3nuud\n\n\n- federated-markdown-bridge [local-only] - Store-backed Markdown bridge for Firstmate customizations (added 2026-09-27)\n- forefront-backend [no-mistakes] - Forefront backend (Next.js/Bun) agent comms platform (added 2026-07-12)\n- brain [no-mistakes] - brain v0.3 Go knowledge store (bd fork) (added 2026-07-12)\n- forefront [no-mistakes] - Forefront iOS native app (Swift/SwiftUI) (added 2026-07-12)\n- gnhf [direct-PR] - ralph-style overnight autonomous-agent orchestrator (TS/pnpm npm CLI); upstream repo kunchenguid/gnhf, contribute via fork (added 2026-07-12)\n- cursorless [direct-PR] - Cursorless VS Code extension (pnpm monorepo); fork at trillium/cursorless, upstream cursorless-dev/cursorless; clone at ~/code/cursorless (symlinked) (added 2026-07-27)\n- interceptor [no-mistakes] - Interceptor browser control CLI; origin at trillium/Interceptor; clone at ~/code/interceptor (symlinked) (added 2026-07-27)\n- TinyKeyboard [no-mistakes] - Near-invisible iOS keyboard extension (Swift/Xcode); origin at trillium/TinyKeyboard; clone at ~/code/TinyKeyboard (symlinked) (added 2026-07-28)\n- herdr-web [direct-PR +yolo] - Browser UI for herdr workspaces and agent panes (React + Rust bridge); fork-shaped: origin at trillium/herdr-web, upstream at kcosr/herdr-web - PRs land on the fork, never upstream (corrected 2026-08-14); clone at ~/code/herdr-web (symlinked); SHIP-FAST posture (captain 2026-08-11): no external-reviewer gate — merge on green alone, autonomous under yolo, clean up post-ship toward ideal state (added 2026-07-28)\n- commitment-triage [local-only] - Apple Notes → commitment-triage pipeline (Bun/TS, two-stage daemon); lo