l. gbu6f (BEADS_DIR ignored) is a one-guard   \n      fix. sl1eq (foreign store absorbs writes) needs a design call on what bare  \n      brain means in client mode.                                                 \n                                                                                  \n      Workaround today: BRAIN_REMOTE=off <command> runs locally and honors        \n      BEADS_DIR.                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n      ## What I did                                                               \n                                                                                  \n----\n○ robots-3ov0r · edge.sh apply hardcodes mode 644 on Caddy site files and would re-expose rotated secrets (follow-up from task-3nuud)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: edge-sh-apply-hardcodes-mode-644-on-caddy-site-files-and-would-re-expose-rotated-secrets-follow-up-from-task-3nuud\n\n\n- federated-markdown-bridge [local-only] - Store-backed Markdown bridge for Firstmate customizations (added 2026-09-27)\n- forefront-backend [no-mistakes] - Forefront backend (Next.js/Bun) agent comms platform (added 2026-07-12)\n- brain [no-mistakes] - brain v0.3 Go knowledge store (bd fork) (added 2026-07-12)\n- forefront [no-mistakes] - Forefront iOS native app (Swift/SwiftUI) (added 2026-07-12)\n- gnhf [direct-PR] - ralph-style overnight autonomous-agent orchestrator (TS/pnpm npm CLI); upstream repo kunchenguid/gnhf, contribute via fork (added 2026-07-12)\n- cursorless [direct-PR] - Cursorless VS Code extension (pnpm monorepo); fork at trillium/cursorless, upstream cursorless-dev/cursorless; clone at ~/code/cursorless (symlinked) (added 2026-07-27)\n- interceptor [no-mistakes] - Interceptor browser control CLI; origin at trillium/Interceptor; clone at ~/cod