{"parentUuid":"75b6e897-55c0-4ce0-9ef3-fe70aadfd0fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBtdCiXkYmf1QtRjEV9g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q2vvhLWqJCut4AHRnftxRD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr view 45 -R trillium/brain --json title,body 2>&1 | head -12; robots show robots-gbu6f 2>&1 </dev/null | sed -n 30,70p"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":95116,"output_tokens":110,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":110,"cache_read_input_tokens":95116,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q2vvhLWqJCut4AHRnftxRD":{"command":"gh pr view 45 -R trillium/brain --json title,body 2>&1 | head -12; robots show robots-gbu6f 2>&1 </dev/null | sed -n 30,70p"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBtdCQvTjRdBHzgJRXoD","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4bb2992-7d5e-4c8f-a8eb-c16a3c239fe2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:12:51.052Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"d4bb2992-7d5e-4c8f-a8eb-c16a3c239fe2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8d72f6b7-7ce0-4ad4-bebf-53581fc7c9f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q2vvhLWqJCut4AHRnftxRD","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"body\":\"## Intent\\n\\nFix robots-gbu6f: bd ignores BEADS_DIR because client-mode remote forwarding runs first and depends only on HOME's remote config. Per the scout report (attached as a comment on robots-gbu6f): in remoteForwardingActive (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go), before loading the remote config, return inactive when BEADS_DIR is set and the canonical BEADS_DIR has local beads project files. Add a regression test.\\n\\n## What Changed\\n- `remoteForwardingActive` in `cmd/bd/brain_remote.go` now returns inactive when `BEADS_DIR` names an existing local beads project, before the HOME remote config is loaded, so the store is opened locally instead of forwarded to the host.\\n- `internal/beads/beads.go` adds `ExplicitBeadsDir()`, which holds the existing `BEADS_DIR` check from `FindBeadsDir` step 1; `FindBeadsDir` now calls it.\\n- Adds `TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir`, covering unset `BEADS_DIR` (still forwards), a directory without project files (still forwards), and a local project (does not forward). Help text, `docs/brain/REMOTE.md`, `docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md`, the website remote reference, and divergence 0034 describe the new precedence.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n\\n✅ Low: The change adds one early-return gate in remoteForwardingActive that reuses the same local-project check FindBeadsDir already applies, and the new test exercises the public function for the set, unset, and non-project cases, so the behavior change is narrow and matches the stated criterion.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nDrove the built `bd` binary live in an isolated HOME with a fake ssh host. Client mode with a configured remote and BEADS_DIR naming a local beads project now runs locally (no ssh call), where the base build forwards. Every guard and boundary case still forwards: no BEADS_DIR, a directory without project files, a missing path, and a regular file. A redirect file resolving to a local project runs locally, and the store-wrapper path (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE set) behaves the same way. The regression unit test fails on base and passes on the fix, and the internal/beads FindBeadsDir tests pass, but both of those were run as Go unit tests in scratch copies and are not counted as live results. Overall: pass on the live scenarios. The live driving used `bd version`, which exercises the forwarding decision but not a full store read or write against a real database.\\n\\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 9 of 11 scenarios driven live against the product\\n\\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Client with remote configured + BEADS_DIR naming a local beads project: `bd version` runs locally, no ssh forward | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-local-project: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Base build reproduces the bug: same setup forwards to the brain host | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (base-local-project: FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| No BEADS_DIR set: client config still forwards to the host (unchanged behavior) | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-no-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR set to an empty directory with no project files: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-empty-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR set to a nonexistent path: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-missing-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a regular file (not a store directory): still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-beads-dir-is-file run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a redirect file pointing to a local project: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-redirect-to-local: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with a local BEADS_DIR: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-store-wrapper-local: ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with no BEADS_DIR: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-store-wrapper-no-dir run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| Regression test TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir fails on base and passes on fix | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is a Go unit test run in scratch copies with cgo-only helpers stubbed, not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. Would… |\\n| FindBeadsDir / ExplicitBeadsDir refactor: existing FindBeadsDir behavior preserved | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is Go unit tests only (`go test ./internal/beads` on a scratch copy), not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. |\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Evidence: Live CLI transcript (base vs fixed, guard and boundary cases)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n=== base-local-project | binary=bd-base | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/store/.beads\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-local-project | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/store/.beads\\nbd version 1.1.0-rc.1+brain.0.5.1 (dev)\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 0\\n\\n=== fixed-no-beads-dir | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=-\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-empty-beads-dir | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/nofiles/.beads\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-missing-beads-dir | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/does-not-exist/.beads\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-redirect-to-local | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/redir/.beads\\nbd version 1.1.0-rc.1+brain.0.5.1 (dev)\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 0\\n\\n=== fixed-store-wrapper-local | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/store/.beads\\nbd version 1.1.0-rc.1+brain.0.5.1 (dev)\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 0\\n```\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Evidence: Regression test on fixed commit (PASS, scratch copy)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n--- PASS: TestRemoteForwardingActive (0.00s)\\n--- PASS: TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir (0.06s)\\nPASS\\nok  \\tgithub.com/steveyegge/beads/cmd/bd\\t1.051s\\n```\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Evidence: Regression test on base commit with new test (FAIL, scratch copy)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n--- PASS: TestRemoteForwardingActive (0.00s)\\n    brain_remote_test.go:230: BEADS_DIR with a local project must not forward: active=true err=<nil>\\n--- FAIL: TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir (0.00s)\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/steveyegge/beads/cmd/bd\\t0.948s\\nFAIL\\n```\\n</details>\\n- Outcome: ⚠️ 1 warning across 1 run (4m0s)\\n\\n## Pipeline\\n\\nUpdates from [git push no-mistakes](https://github.com/kunchenguid/no-mistakes)\\n\\n<!-- no-mistakes-pipeline-attestation:v1 {\\\"head_sha\\\":\\\"23b4f1d8e72c5bf7a7c6c02454f83809c6b50ed4\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[{\\\"step\\\":\\\"intent\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"rebase\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"review\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"test\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"document\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"lint\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"push\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"pr\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"running\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"ci\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\"}]} -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **intent** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **Rebase** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>🔧 **Review** - 2 issues found → auto-fixed ✅</summary>\\n\\n- ⚠️ `internal/beads/beads.go:676` - Simplification: `ExplicitBeadsDir` (internal/beads/beads.go:676) re-implements FindBeadsDir step 1 (beads.go ~line 688: canonicalizeBeadsDirPath, FollowRedirect, os.Stat IsDir, hasBeadsProjectFiles) as a second copy of the same rule. The only caller (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:267) consumes just whether the result is non-empty, so the returned path is unused. The required behavior is the check itself; the narrower form is to have FindBeadsDir step 1 call one shared helper (returning bool or the dir) so the BEADS_DIR-is-a-local-project rule is defined once.\\n- ℹ️ `cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:267` - Behavior consequence of the intended fix, not a contradiction: the store wrappers export BEADS_DIR=$HOME/data/&lt;store&gt;/.beads unconditionally. On any client machine where that local store directory exists with project files, every wrapper invocation now runs locally and never forwards, even when a remote host is configured. Writes then land in the local store without a warning. This follows directly from the stated criterion, so no change is requested.\\n\\n🔧 Fix applied.\\n✅ Re-checked - no issues remain.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>⚠️ **Test** - 1 warning</summary>\\n\\n- ⚠️ `cmd/bd/brain_host_e2e_test.go:87` - The cmd/bd test package does not compile in this environment: brain_host_e2e_test.go (untagged) calls buildBDUnderTest, which is defined only in cgo-gated files, and freePort is undefined. The cgo build itself fails on the missing ICU headers (go-icu-regex). This predates the change (same error at base 24ea97b25), so the regression test could only be run in a scratch copy with those helpers stubbed. Needs a human decision on tagging or fixing the test helpers and installing ICU for CI.\\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 9 of 11 scenarios driven live against the product\\n\\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Client with remote configured + BEADS_DIR naming a local beads project: `bd version` runs locally, no ssh forward | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-local-project: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Base build reproduces the bug: same setup forwards to the brain host | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (base-local-project: FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| No BEADS_DIR set: client config still forwards to the host (unchanged behavior) | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-no-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR set to an empty directory with no project files: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-empty-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR set to a nonexistent path: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-missing-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a regular file (not a store directory): still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-beads-dir-is-file run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a redirect file pointing to a local project: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-redirect-to-local: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with a local BEADS_DIR: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-store-wrapper-local: ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with no BEADS_DIR: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-store-wrapper-no-dir run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| Regression test TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir fails on base and passes on fix | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is a Go unit test run in scratch copies with cgo-only helpers stubbed, not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. Would… |\\n| FindBeadsDir / ExplicitBeadsDir refactor: existing FindBeadsDir behavior preserved | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is Go unit tests only (`go test ./internal/beads` on a scratch copy), not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. |\\n\\n- <code>Built fixed binary from worktree (`go build ./cmd/bd`) and base binary from `git archive 24ea97b25` into the evidence dir</code>\\n- <code>Isolated HOME with `~/.config/brain/remote.yaml` host set; fake ssh via BRAIN_REMOTE_SSH logging every invocation; driven with `bd version` (runs the forwarding decision before any DB work)</code>\\n- `Live CLI cases: base+local project, fixed+local project, fixed+no BEADS_DIR, fixed+empty .beads dir, fixed+missing path, fixed+redirect to local project, BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task+local project, BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task+no BEADS_DIR, fixed+BEADS_DIR pointing at a regular file`\\n- <code>`go test ./cmd/bd -run TestRemoteForwarding -v` on a scratch copy of the fixed commit (only the cgo-blocked helpers stubbed out there; the repo itself was not modified)</code>\\n- `Same test on a scratch copy of the base commit with the new test file: TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir fails with 'BEADS_DIR with a local project must not forward: active=true'`\\n- <code>`go test ./internal/beads -run &#39;FindBeadsDir|ExplicitBeadsDir|BeadsDir&#39;` on the fixed scratch copy (all pass)</code>\\n- `Transcript saved at evidence transcript.txt; test outputs at regression-fixed.txt and regression-base.txt`\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>⚠️ **Document** - 1 info</summary>\\n\\n- ℹ️ `cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:40` - The `bd remote` help text (Go Long string, mirrored in docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md and the generated website/docs/cli-reference/remote.md) does not mention that a local BEADS_DIR now bypasses forwarding. I updated the authoritative user doc, docs/brain/REMOTE.md, and left the help text unchanged because it is generated from the Go source and changing it means editing the help string and regenerating the website copy.\\n\\n🔧 Fix applied.\\n1 info still open:\\n\\n- ℹ️ `docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md:8512` - Generated CLI reference was already out of sync with live help at base 24ea97b25 (docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md missing bd stores rewrite-wrappers and other stores entries; website/docs/cli-reference/brain.md and stores.md drifted). scripts/generate-cli-docs.sh regenerates them all, so this change&#39;s remote-only update was applied by hand to docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md and the unrelated drift was not regenerated, to keep scope. Follow-up: run scripts/generate-cli-docs.sh in a dedicated docs-sync change.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **Lint** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **Push** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\",\"title\":\"fix(bd): honor an explicit local BEADS_DIR over remote forwarding\"}\n                                                                                  \n      • Read-only diagnosis. Nothing in the live stores or the shared Dolt server \n      (127.0.0.1:3307) was touched.                                               \n      • Built a throwaway sandbox under the scratchpad (bd-sandbox/) with an      \n      overridden HOME (bd-sandbox/realhome), so ~/.config/brain/remote.yaml and   \n      ~/data/brain live only in the sandbox.                                      \n      • Used the installed binary ~/.local/bin/bd.real (bd version 1.1.0-rc.1+    \n      brain.0.5.1 (3a63e7914)), with env -i so no live env leaked in.             \n      • Replaced the ssh transport with a fake (BRAIN_REMOTE_SSH pointing at a    \n      script that appends argv to a log and exits 0). It never connects.          \n      • Read the source in this worktree (HEAD 24ea97b25).                        \n                                                                                  \n      ## Resolution order (as the code runs)                                      \n                                                                                  \n      cmd/bd/main.go startup, in order:                                           \n                                                                                  \n      1. hostGateEarly(os.Args[1:]) (main.go near 1628).                          \n      2. maybeForwardRemote(os.Args[1:]) at cmd/bd/main.go:1632. If it returns    \n      handled, bd exits here. **No **BEADS_DIR** check happens before this point. \n      **                                                                          \n      3. Only if not forwarded: BD_NAME, then loadEnvironment → beads.            \n      FindBeadsDir().                                                             \n                                                                                  \n      maybeForwardRemote → remoteForwardingActive (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:254-    \n      282):                                                                       \n                                                                                  \n      • :255 BRAIN_REMOTE=off disables forwarding. This is the only escape.       \n      • :258 name comes from BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE (set by store wrappers); empty    \n      means brain.                                                                \n      • :264 loadRemoteConfig() (:132-147) reads remoteConfigFile() (:83-89),     \n      which is $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. **This is the HOME dependency.**  \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_HOST can override the host.                                    \n      • :268 cfg.Host == \"\" means not a client. Any non-empty host means forward. \n                                                                                  \n      brain_remote.go contains zero references to BEADS_DIR (grep -c BEADS_DIR    \n      returned 0). The remote script (:179-181) sets PATH, BRAIN_REMOTE=off,      \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1 and execs the host's wrapper with the store name.  \n      Neither the client's BEADS_DIR nor its cwd is sent.                         \n                                                                                  \n      For comparison, the local resolver internal/beads/beads.go:689              \n      (FindBeadsDir) honors BEADS_DIR at step 1 (:690). It is never reached when","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bbaf82dc-ea52-4582-8d0c-991f589e8cb5","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:12:52.421Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"body\":\"## Intent\\n\\nFix robots-gbu6f: bd ignores BEADS_DIR because client-mode remote forwarding runs first and depends only on HOME's remote config. Per the scout report (attached as a comment on robots-gbu6f): in remoteForwardingActive (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go), before loading the remote config, return inactive when BEADS_DIR is set and the canonical BEADS_DIR has local beads project files. Add a regression test.\\n\\n## What Changed\\n- `remoteForwardingActive` in `cmd/bd/brain_remote.go` now returns inactive when `BEADS_DIR` names an existing local beads project, before the HOME remote config is loaded, so the store is opened locally instead of forwarded to the host.\\n- `internal/beads/beads.go` adds `ExplicitBeadsDir()`, which holds the existing `BEADS_DIR` check from `FindBeadsDir` step 1; `FindBeadsDir` now calls it.\\n- Adds `TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir`, covering unset `BEADS_DIR` (still forwards), a directory without project files (still forwards), and a local project (does not forward). Help text, `docs/brain/REMOTE.md`, `docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md`, the website remote reference, and divergence 0034 describe the new precedence.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n\\n✅ Low: The change adds one early-return gate in remoteForwardingActive that reuses the same local-project check FindBeadsDir already applies, and the new test exercises the public function for the set, unset, and non-project cases, so the behavior change is narrow and matches the stated criterion.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\nDrove the built `bd` binary live in an isolated HOME with a fake ssh host. Client mode with a configured remote and BEADS_DIR naming a local beads project now runs locally (no ssh call), where the base build forwards. Every guard and boundary case still forwards: no BEADS_DIR, a directory without project files, a missing path, and a regular file. A redirect file resolving to a local project runs locally, and the store-wrapper path (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE set) behaves the same way. The regression unit test fails on base and passes on the fix, and the internal/beads FindBeadsDir tests pass, but both of those were run as Go unit tests in scratch copies and are not counted as live results. Overall: pass on the live scenarios. The live driving used `bd version`, which exercises the forwarding decision but not a full store read or write against a real database.\\n\\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 9 of 11 scenarios driven live against the product\\n\\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Client with remote configured + BEADS_DIR naming a local beads project: `bd version` runs locally, no ssh forward | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-local-project: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Base build reproduces the bug: same setup forwards to the brain host | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (base-local-project: FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| No BEADS_DIR set: client config still forwards to the host (unchanged behavior) | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-no-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR set to an empty directory with no project files: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-empty-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR set to a nonexistent path: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-missing-beads-dir: ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a regular file (not a store directory): still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-beads-dir-is-file run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a redirect file pointing to a local project: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-redirect-to-local: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with a local BEADS_DIR: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-store-wrapper-local: ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with no BEADS_DIR: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-store-wrapper-no-dir run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| Regression test TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir fails on base and passes on fix | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is a Go unit test run in scratch copies with cgo-only helpers stubbed, not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. Would… |\\n| FindBeadsDir / ExplicitBeadsDir refactor: existing FindBeadsDir behavior preserved | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is Go unit tests only (`go test ./internal/beads` on a scratch copy), not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. |\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Evidence: Live CLI transcript (base vs fixed, guard and boundary cases)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n=== base-local-project | binary=bd-base | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/store/.beads\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-local-project | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/store/.beads\\nbd version 1.1.0-rc.1+brain.0.5.1 (dev)\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 0\\n\\n=== fixed-no-beads-dir | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=-\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-empty-beads-dir | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/nofiles/.beads\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-missing-beads-dir | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/does-not-exist/.beads\\nFORWARDED-TO-HOST\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 1\\nSSH-INVOKED: -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPath=/tmp/brain-ssh-501/%C -o ControlPersist=10m -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 -o LogLevel=ERROR -T me@brainhost -- exec /bin/sh -c 'd=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"; PATH=\\\"$d:$PATH\\\"; BRAIN_REMOTE=off; BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1; export PATH BRAIN_REMOTE BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED; exec \\\"$d/$0\\\" \\\"$@\\\"' 'brain' 'version'\\n\\n=== fixed-redirect-to-local | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/redir/.beads\\nbd version 1.1.0-rc.1+brain.0.5.1 (dev)\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 0\\n\\n=== fixed-store-wrapper-local | binary=bd-fixed | BEADS_DIR=<EV>/fake/store/.beads\\nbd version 1.1.0-rc.1+brain.0.5.1 (dev)\\nexit=0\\nssh calls: 0\\n```\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Evidence: Regression test on fixed commit (PASS, scratch copy)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n--- PASS: TestRemoteForwardingActive (0.00s)\\n--- PASS: TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir (0.06s)\\nPASS\\nok  \\tgithub.com/steveyegge/beads/cmd/bd\\t1.051s\\n```\\n</details>\\n<details>\\n<summary>Evidence: Regression test on base commit with new test (FAIL, scratch copy)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n--- PASS: TestRemoteForwardingActive (0.00s)\\n    brain_remote_test.go:230: BEADS_DIR with a local project must not forward: active=true err=<nil>\\n--- FAIL: TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir (0.00s)\\nFAIL\\nFAIL\\tgithub.com/steveyegge/beads/cmd/bd\\t0.948s\\nFAIL\\n```\\n</details>\\n- Outcome: ⚠️ 1 warning across 1 run (4m0s)\\n\\n## Pipeline\\n\\nUpdates from [git push no-mistakes](https://github.com/kunchenguid/no-mistakes)\\n\\n<!-- no-mistakes-pipeline-attestation:v1 {\\\"head_sha\\\":\\\"23b4f1d8e72c5bf7a7c6c02454f83809c6b50ed4\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[{\\\"step\\\":\\\"intent\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"rebase\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"review\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"test\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"document\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"lint\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"push\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"pr\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"running\\\"},{\\\"step\\\":\\\"ci\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\"}]} -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **intent** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **Rebase** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>🔧 **Review** - 2 issues found → auto-fixed ✅</summary>\\n\\n- ⚠️ `internal/beads/beads.go:676` - Simplification: `ExplicitBeadsDir` (internal/beads/beads.go:676) re-implements FindBeadsDir step 1 (beads.go ~line 688: canonicalizeBeadsDirPath, FollowRedirect, os.Stat IsDir, hasBeadsProjectFiles) as a second copy of the same rule. The only caller (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:267) consumes just whether the result is non-empty, so the returned path is unused. The required behavior is the check itself; the narrower form is to have FindBeadsDir step 1 call one shared helper (returning bool or the dir) so the BEADS_DIR-is-a-local-project rule is defined once.\\n- ℹ️ `cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:267` - Behavior consequence of the intended fix, not a contradiction: the store wrappers export BEADS_DIR=$HOME/data/&lt;store&gt;/.beads unconditionally. On any 