forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-beads-dir-is-file run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| BEADS_DIR is a redirect file pointing to a local project: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-redirect-to-local: &#39;bd version ...&#39;, ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with a local BEADS_DIR: runs locally | ✅ pass | live | transcript.txt (fixed-store-wrapper-local: ssh calls: 0) |\\n| Store wrapper (BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task) with no BEADS_DIR: still forwards | ✅ pass | live | fixed-store-wrapper-no-dir run in session (FORWARDED-TO-HOST, ssh calls: 1) |\\n| Regression test TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir fails on base and passes on fix | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is a Go unit test run in scratch copies with cgo-only helpers stubbed, not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. Would… |\\n| FindBeadsDir / ExplicitBeadsDir refactor: existing FindBeadsDir behavior preserved | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload recorded this as a pass, but it is Go unit tests only (`go test ./internal/beads` on a scratch copy), not a live product run, so it does not meet the live-validation contract. |\\n\\n- <code>Built fixed binary from worktree (`go build ./cmd/bd`) and base binary from `git archive 24ea97b25` into the evidence dir</code>\\n- <code>Isolated HOME with `~/.config/brain/remote.yaml` host set; fake ssh via BRAIN_REMOTE_SSH logging every invocation; driven with `bd version` (runs the forwarding decision before any DB work)</code>\\n- `Live CLI cases: base+local project, fixed+local project, fixed+no BEADS_DIR, fixed+empty .beads dir, fixed+missing path, fixed+redirect to local project, BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task+local project, BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE=task+no BEADS_DIR, fixed+BEADS_DIR pointing at a regular file`\\n- <code>`go test ./cmd/bd -run TestRemoteForwarding -v` on a scratch copy of the fixed commit (only the cgo-blocked helpers stubbed out there; the repo itself was not modified)</code>\\n- `Same test on a scratch copy of the base commit with the new test file: TestRemoteForwardingYieldsToLocalBeadsDir fails with 'BEADS_DIR with a local project must not forward: active=true'`\\n- <code>`go test ./internal/beads -run &#39;FindBeadsDir|ExplicitBeadsDir|BeadsDir&#39;` on the fixed scratch copy (all pass)</code>\\n- `Transcript saved at evidence transcript.txt; test outputs at regression-fixed.txt and regression-base.txt`\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>⚠️ **Document** - 1 info</summary>\\n\\n- ℹ️ `cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:40` - The `bd remote` help text (Go Long string, mirrored in docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md and the generated website/docs/cli-reference/remote.md) does not mention that a local BEADS_DIR now bypasses forwarding. I updated the authoritative user doc, docs/brain/REMOTE.md, and left the help text unchanged because it is generated from the Go source and changing it means editing the help string and regenerating the website copy.\\n\\n🔧 Fix applied.\\n1 info still open:\\n\\n- ℹ️ `docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md:8512` - Generated CLI reference was already out of sync with live help at base 24ea97b25 (docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md missing bd stores rewrite-wrappers and other stores entries; website/docs/cli-reference/brain.md and stores.md drifted). scripts/generate-cli-docs.sh regenerates them all, so this change&#39;s remote-only update was applied by hand to docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md and the unrelated drift was not regenerated, to keep scope. Follow-up: run scripts/generate-cli-docs.sh in a dedicated docs-sync change.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **Lint** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>✅ **Push** - passed</summary>\\n\\n✅ No issues found.\\n</details>\\n\",\"title\":\"fix(bd): honor an explicit local BEADS_DIR over remote forwarding\"}\n                                                                                  \n      • Read-only diagnosis. Nothing in the live stores or the shared Dolt server \n      (127.0.0.1:3307) was touched.                                               \n      • Built a throwaway sandbox under the scratchpad (bd-sandbox/) with an      \n      overridden HOME (bd-sandbox/realhome), so ~/.config/brain/remote.yaml and   \n      ~/data/brain live only in the sandbox.                                      \n      • Used the installed binary ~/.local/bin/bd.real (bd version 1.1.0-rc.1+    \n      brain.0.5.1 (3a63e7914)), with env -i so no live env leaked in.             \n      • Replaced the ssh transport with a fake (BRAIN_REMOTE_SSH pointing at a    \n      script that appends argv to a log and exits 0). It never connects.          \n      • Read the source in this worktree (HEAD 24ea97b25).                        \n                                                                                  \n      ## Resolution order (as the code runs)                                      \n                                                                                  \n      cmd/bd/main.go startup, in order:                                           \n                                                                                  \n      1. hostGateEarly(os.Args[1:]) (main.go near 1628).                          \n      2. maybeForwardRemote(os.Args[1:]) at cmd/bd/main.go:1632. If it returns    \n      handled, bd exits here. **No **BEADS_DIR** check happens before this point. \n      **                                                                          \n      3. Only if not forwarded: BD_NAME, then loadEnvironment → beads.            \n      FindBeadsDir().                                                             \n                                                                                  \n      maybeForwardRemote → remoteForwardingActive (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:254-    \n      282):                                                                       \n                                                                                  \n      • :255 BRAIN_REMOTE=off disables forwarding. This is the only escape.       \n      • :258 name comes from BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE (set by store wrappers); empty    \n      means brain.                                                                \n      • :264 loadRemoteConfig() (:132-147) reads remoteConfigFile() (:83-89),     \n      which is $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. **This is the HOME dependency.**  \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_HOST can override the host.                                    \n      • :268 cfg.Host == \"\" means not a client. Any non-empty host means forward. \n                                                                                  \n      brain_remote.go contains zero references to BEADS_DIR (grep -c BEADS_DIR    \n      returned 0). The remote script (:179-181) sets PATH, BRAIN_REMOTE=off,      \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1 and execs the host's wrapper with the store name.  \n      Neither the client's BEADS_DIR nor its cwd is sent.                         \n                                                                                  \n      For comparison, the local resolver internal/beads/beads.go:689              \n      (FindBeadsDir) honors BEADS_DIR at step 1 (:690). It is never reached when","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4bb2992-7d5e-4c8f-a8eb-c16a3c239fe2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
