{"parentUuid":"2cf1a57f-9fa4-4772-b230-4b054850ad41","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"160a7f52-c471-45ec-8e1b-d99b3eca05c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uit5SQFV8tbLwsEDiJxfVm","type":"tool_result","content":"verified: https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/5 is open and mergeable, with every unwaived required check reported and every unwaived check green at head 410ecccc4f8f0b0bdc08bf3ae70302771119cb36\nverified: https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/5 is merged (state=MERGED, merged=true, isInMergeQueue=false)\nfilled in. Ship and scout `# Task` sections have two subsections Firstmate\n       fm-brief.sh <task-id> <repo-name> --scout [--base-branch <branch>] [--herdr-lab]\n  --scout writes the scout contract instead: the deliverable is a report at\nand passes the explicit flag. Refused on --scout and --secondmate: a scout\nthe same way. Ship-only: a scout publishes nothing and a charter is not a\nUsage: fm-spawn.sh <task-id> <project-dir> --mode <no-mistakes|direct-PR|local-only> --yolo <on|off> [--branch-prefix <prefix>] [--base-branch <branch>] [--harness <name>|harness|launch-command] [--model <name>] [--effort <level>] [--backend <name>] [--herdr-resume-lock-wait]\n       fm-spawn.sh <task-id> <project-dir> --scout [--base-branch <branch>] [--harness <name>|harness|launch-command] [--model <name>] [--effort <level>] [--backend <name>] [--herdr-resume-lock-wait]\n       fm-spawn.sh <task-id> [<firstmate-home>] [--harness <name>|harness|launch-command] [--model <name>] [--effort <level>] [--backend <name>] --secondmate\n  spawn and refused on --scout and --secondmate spawns. Firstmate resolves both\n  ship or scout spawn also refuses leftover `{TASK}` / `{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}`\n  Every ship or scout spawn renders `launch-brief.md`; for a no-mistakes ship\nbrief.md\nlaunch-brief.md\nreport.md\n143\n# Scout: can Talon's speech layer move to the iPhone?\n\n**Short answer:** Not as a port. Talon's recognizer is a Mac-only Conformer (wav2letter-format) engine with a native decoder dylib, and there is no iOS build of it in the install. What *can* move to the phone is the transcription step itself: an on-device Whisper-class or Apple SpeechAnalyzer model \n\nScope: report only. No code, grammar, or Talon voice commands were changed. The only scratch activity was read-only inspection of `~/.talon`, the Talon app bundle, and this worktree, plus web searches. Nothing was pushed and no PR was opened.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Talon's speech engine is\n\n**Engine family.** The repo README says Talon's recommended engine is its \"built-in Conformer (wav2letter) speech recognition engine\" (`README.md:21`). The running engine is the w2l engine: the Talon watchdog log repeatedly reports stacks through `talon/engines/w2l.py:730` and `talon/scripting/dispa\n\n**Models on disk.** Talon's blob store is `~/.talon/.sys/blob/`, and its keyval DB (`~/.talon/.sys/user.db`, table `keyval`) records which models are registered:\n\n- `sys.w2l.models` lists three model ids: `19a05637…`, `2285dbfb…`, `f7e58e5a…`.\n- `sys.speech.engine-mru` orders the engines as `wav2letter` (most recent, 2026-03-08) then `wav2letter-conformer` (2026-03-07).\n\nThe manifests, read directly from the blob store:\n\n| Manifest (`blob/…`) | Name | Blobs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `19/19a05637…` | **Conformer D (2025-01-06)**, en_US, most recently used | `acoustic.onnx` 111.4 MB (ONNX, PyTorch-exported; header is `pytorch`), `lexicon.txt` 4.35 MB, `lexicon_flat.bin` 12.1 MB |\n| `f7/f7e58e5a…` | Conformer D (2023-05-20) + Whisper, not public | `acoustic.b2l` 111 MB (`BW2L` format), `ort.patch` 164 KB, lexicon files, `whisper-tiny.bin` 78 MB, `whisper-base.bin` 148 MB, `whisper-small.bin` 488 MB (ggml, `lmgg` magic), `measure.flac` 129 KB |\n| `6d/6d4da3d8…` | Conformer D (2023-05-20) | `acoustic.b2l`, `ort.patch`, lexicon files |\n\nWhich manifest is live is inferred from the MRU timestamps, not confirmed by a live query. Verify with `settings.get` or the REPL if it matters.\n\n**Key takeaways about the engine:**\n\n- The acoustic model is an ONNX graph run through ONNX Runtime (`~/.talon/documentation/engines/w2l/W2lOrtEncoder.md:5`, `W2lModelInfo` fields `model_format`, `am_path`, `ort_patch`, `whisper_paths`, `measure_path`: `W2lModelInfo.md:5`).\n- Decoding uses a native library, `/Applications/Talon.app/Contents/Frameworks/libw2ldecode.dylib`, which contains `w2l::` symbols (TrieNode, FlatTrie, LM, ZeroLM). It exists only in the Mac app bundle, and `Talon 2.app` has its own copy. Nothing in the bundle or on disk is an iOS build.\n- The Whisper `.bin` files are bundled in Talon's own manifest. The w2l model config has a `whisper_paths` field, which suggests Whisper is used inside the Talon engine (perhaps for rescoring). I did **not** verify how Talon uses them at runtime.\n- `sys.speech.record_all` is `true` (`user.db`). Talon is saving every utterance: `~/.talon/recordings/` holds 329,247 FLAC files (8.0 GB), with the phrase in each filename. This is a large local audio corpus. It is the captain's voice and must stay local; do not publish or ship it.\n\nNote: `~/.talon/documentation` is auto-generated API stubs. Most method pages have `None` for their description, so the source of truth is the bundled API docs plus the repo's own usage.\n\n## 2. What Talon exposes for external recognition input\n\nThe `speech_system` API (`~/.talon/documentation_clean/talon_complete_api_docs_clean.md`, section `speech_system`, from line 9222):","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"efb8ae05-0504-40af-ad87-a9b5e4bcf208","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:53:16.097Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"verified: https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/5 is open and mergeable, with every unwaived required check reported and every unwaived check green at head 410ecccc4f8f0b0bdc08bf3ae70302771119cb36\nverified: https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/5 is merged (state=MERGED, merged=true, isInMergeQueue=false)\nfilled in. Ship and scout `# Task` sections have two subsections Firstmate\n       fm-brief.sh <task-id> <repo-name> --scout [--base-branch <branch>] [--herdr-lab]\n  --scout writes the scout contract instead: the deliverable is a report at\nand passes the explicit flag. Refused on --scout and --secondmate: a scout\nthe same way. Ship-only: a scout publishes nothing and a charter is not a\nUsage: fm-spawn.sh <task-id> <project-dir> --mode <no-mistakes|direct-PR|local-only> --yolo <on|off> [--branch-prefix <prefix>] [--base-branch <branch>] [--harness <name>|harness|launch-command] [--model <name>] [--effort <level>] [--backend <name>] [--herdr-resume-lock-wait]\n       fm-spawn.sh <task-id> <project-dir> --scout [--base-branch <branch>] [--harness <name>|harness|launch-command] [--model <name>] [--effort <level>] [--backend <name>] [--herdr-resume-lock-wait]\n       fm-spawn.sh <task-id> [<firstmate-home>] [--harness <name>|harness|launch-command] [--model <name>] [--effort <level>] [--backend <name>] --secondmate\n  spawn and refused on --scout and --secondmate spawns. Firstmate resolves both\n  ship or scout spawn also refuses leftover `{TASK}` / `{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}`\n  Every ship or scout spawn renders `launch-brief.md`; for a no-mistakes ship\nbrief.md\nlaunch-brief.md\nreport.md\n143\n# Scout: can Talon's speech layer move to the iPhone?\n\n**Short answer:** Not as a port. Talon's recognizer is a Mac-only Conformer (wav2letter-format) engine with a native decoder dylib, and there is no iOS build of it in the install. What *can* move to the phone is the transcription step itself: an on-device Whisper-class or Apple SpeechAnalyzer model \n\nScope: report only. No code, grammar, or Talon voice commands were changed. The only scratch activity was read-only inspection of `~/.talon`, the Talon app bundle, and this worktree, plus web searches. Nothing was pushed and no PR was opened.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Talon's speech engine is\n\n**Engine family.** The repo README says Talon's recommended engine is its \"built-in Conformer (wav2letter) speech recognition engine\" (`README.md:21`). The running engine is the w2l engine: the Talon watchdog log repeatedly reports stacks through `talon/engines/w2l.py:730` and `talon/scripting/dispa\n\n**Models on disk.** Talon's blob store is `~/.talon/.sys/blob/`, and its keyval DB (`~/.talon/.sys/user.db`, table `keyval`) records which models are registered:\n\n- `sys.w2l.models` lists three model ids: `19a05637…`, `2285dbfb…`, `f7e58e5a…`.\n- `sys.speech.engine-mru` orders the engines as `wav2letter` (most recent, 2026-03-08) then `wav2letter-conformer` (2026-03-07).\n\nThe manifests, read directly from the blob store:\n\n| Manifest (`blob/…`) | Name | Blobs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `19/19a05637…` | **Conformer D (2025-01-06)**, en_US, most recently used | `acoustic.onnx` 111.4 MB (ONNX, PyTorch-exported; header is `pytorch`), `lexicon.txt` 4.35 MB, `lexicon_flat.bin` 12.1 MB |\n| `f7/f7e58e5a…` | Conformer D (2023-05-20) + Whisper, not public | `acoustic.b2l` 111 MB (`BW2L` format), `ort.patch` 164 KB, lexicon files, `whisper-tiny.bin` 78 MB, `whisper-base.bin` 148 MB, `whisper-small.bin` 488 MB (ggml, `lmgg` magic), `measure.flac` 129 KB |\n| `6d/6d4da3d8…` | Conformer D (2023-05-20) | `acoustic.b2l`, `ort.patch`, lexicon files |\n\nWhich manifest is live is inferred from the MRU timestamps, not confirmed by a live query. Verify with `settings.get` or the REPL if it matters.\n\n**Key takeaways about the engine:**\n\n- The acoustic model is an ONNX graph run through ONNX Runtime (`~/.talon/documentation/engines/w2l/W2lOrtEncoder.md:5`, `W2lModelInfo` fields `model_format`, `am_path`, `ort_patch`, `whisper_paths`, `measure_path`: `W2lModelInfo.md:5`).\n- Decoding uses a native library, `/Applications/Talon.app/Contents/Frameworks/libw2ldecode.dylib`, which contains `w2l::` symbols (TrieNode, FlatTrie, LM, ZeroLM). It exists only in the Mac app bundle, and `Talon 2.app` has its own copy. Nothing in the bundle or on disk is an iOS build.\n- The Whisper `.bin` files are bundled in Talon's own manifest. The w2l model config has a `whisper_paths` field, which suggests Whisper is used inside the Talon engine (perhaps for rescoring). I did **not** verify how Talon uses them at runtime.\n- `sys.speech.record_all` is `true` (`user.db`). Talon is saving every utterance: `~/.talon/recordings/` holds 329,247 FLAC files (8.0 GB), with the phrase in each filename. This is a large local audio corpus. It is the captain's voice and must stay local; do not publish or ship it.\n\nNote: `~/.talon/documentation` is auto-generated API stubs. Most method pages have `None` for their description, so the source of truth is the bundled API docs plus the repo's own usage.\n\n## 2. What Talon exposes for external recognition input\n\nThe `speech_system` API (`~/.talon/documentation_clean/talon_complete_api_docs_clean.md`, section `speech_system`, from line 9222):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2cf1a57f-9fa4-4772-b230-4b054850ad41","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
