{"parentUuid":"5354129d-b8cc-4049-8ef1-983da3aa2b49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBwiAgjVcxcKJEDvXj6u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PRs #44, #45, #47 and forefront-backend #5 are merged. Launching a Fable scout to dig into the phone-side Talon question, building on the existing finding that Talon's recognizer can't port to the phone but Whisper-class transcription can.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2843,"cache_read_input_tokens":132532,"output_tokens":1029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":235},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":132532,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3,"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgBwiAProMTdd9De4i4SW","type":"assistant","uuid":"3959fbfe-03c7-4a00-984e-463c6430a8f9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:53:21.472Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"3959fbfe-03c7-4a00-984e-463c6430a8f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBwiAgjVcxcKJEDvXj6u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P9Sf5WPpKp9PFqNPGCULsc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; id=talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2\n$B/fm-brief.sh $id trillium_talon --scout 2>&1 | tail -1\npython3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/brief.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('{TASK}',\"Captain's ask: improve the Talon story. Can the Talon model be brought to the phone so the phone handles the speech part in a Talon-like way (fast command-grammar recognition, not just free dictation)? Documentation partly exists: read data/scout-talon-phone-asr/report.md first (it concludes Talon's Conformer engine is Mac-only, but on-device Whisper-class or Apple SpeechAnalyzer transcription can move to the phone). Also see idea-v0fz (on-device Whisper feeding the mimic inject endpoint), question-bl4 (Apple vocab biasing on the iPhone mic path), and the palette feed/inject work in trillium_talon.\")\ns=s.replace('{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}',\"Deliver data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/report.md: (1) what is possible today, with the strongest options ranked for a Talon-like feel (grammar-constrained decoding, vocab/contextual biasing, hot-word command mode vs dictation mode, latency budget), (2) a concrete architecture where the phone recognizes and sends text or commands to the Mac via the existing inject/mimic endpoint, with what stays in Talon, (3) a staged build plan with a first small spike, and (4) gaps in existing documentation to fix. Report only: write no code, do not write Talon voice commands or grammar (those are captain-only), and do not touch the recordings corpus.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nHERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 $B/fm-spawn.sh $id projects/trillium_talon --scout --harness