{"parentUuid":"d2159fe1-949c-44fd-b22e-e6087d95c40f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBxCLTPL9ECbiU3uR3Hs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NqumPJVAX3gfxSVXWc8DLc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; id=talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2\npython3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/brief.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd='\\n\"Talon\\'s recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - this is a cop out, that is the whole point. yes we can do this\"\\n'\ni=s.find('## Firstmate spec')\ns=s[:i].rstrip('\\n')+'\\n'+add+'\\n'+s[i:] if i>0 else s+add\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n$B/fm-send.sh $id 'Correction to the premise: \"Talon\\'s recognizer is Mac-only and cannot be ported\" is NOT an acceptable conclusion. Porting it to the phone is the whole point, so the captain wants a plan that makes it work. Treat feasibility as given and find the how. Known levers: acoustic.onnx (111 MB, PyTorch-exported ONNX) runs on iOS via ONNX Runtime or CoreML conversion; the w2l/flashlight decoder, lexicon.txt and lexicon_flat.bin are open formats we can reimplement or cross-compile for arm64 (libw2ldecode.dylib is only a Mac build, not the only possible build); the Whisper ggml models run in whisper.cpp on iOS. Rewrite the report: (1) the concrete porting path for the Conformer AM + decoder + lexicon/grammar biasing, with effort and risks per piece, (2) a first spike that gets acoustic.onnx emitting tokens on an iPhone, (3) what from the Mac install must be copied (this is the captain\\'s own licensed install; list any license check as a risk item, not a blocker), (4) fallback only if a specific piece proves impossible, with evidence. Report only, no Talon voice commands or grammar.' 2>&1 | tail -1\nstatus comment status-kdv \"Captain pushback: 'Talon recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - cop out, that is the point. yes we can do this.' Steered talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2 (Fable) to treat porting AM+decoder to iPhone as given and plan the how (ONNX/CoreML, flashlight decoder cross-compile, spike plan).\" 2>&1 | tail -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":139241,"output_tokens":1082,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":189},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1082,"cache_read_input_tokens":139241,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NqumPJVAX3gfxSVXWc8DLc":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; id=talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2\npython3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/brief.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd='\\n\"Talon\\'s recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - this is a cop out, that is the whole point. yes we can do this\"\\n'\ni=s.find('## Firstmate spec')\ns=s[:i].rstrip('\\n')+'\\n'+add+'\\n'+s[i:] if i>0 else s+add\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n$B/fm-send.sh $id 'Correction to the premise: \"Talon\\'s recognizer is Mac-only and cannot be ported\" is NOT an acceptable conclusion. Porting it to the phone is the whole point, so the captain wants a plan that makes it work. Treat feasibility as given and find the how. Known levers: acoustic.onnx (111 MB, PyTorch-exported ONNX) runs on iOS via ONNX Runtime or CoreML conversion; the w2l/flashlight de