{"parentUuid":"f26a0872-b2df-48e0-a9db-15bf2adf8bda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBxCyoSCLKU1ME5MtxEP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JWa3Rynj8wVV6jopSMBxyM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; id=talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2\npython3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/brief.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd='\\n\"Talon\\'s recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - this is a cop out, that is the whole point. yes we can do this\"\\n'\ni=s.find('## Firstmate spec')\ns=s[:i].rstrip('\\n')+'\\n'+add+'\\n'+s[i:] if i>0 else s+add\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/$id/steer-port.txt <<'EOF'\nCorrection to the premise: \"Talon's recognizer is Mac-only and cannot be ported\" is NOT an acceptable conclusion. Porting it to the phone is the whole point, so the plan must make it work. Treat feasibility as given and find the how. Known levers: acoustic.onnx (111 MB, PyTorch-exported ONNX) runs on iOS via ONNX Runtime or CoreML conversion; the w2l/flashlight decoder, lexicon.txt and lexicon_flat.bin are open formats we can reimplement or cross-compile for arm64 (libw2ldecode.dylib is only the Mac build); the Whisper ggml models run in whisper.cpp on iOS. Rewrite the report: (1) the concrete porting path for the Conformer AM + decoder + lexicon/grammar biasing, with effort and risk per piece, (2) a first spike that gets acoustic.onnx emitting tokens on an iPhone, (3) what must be copied from the Mac install (it is the captain's own licensed install; list any license check as a risk item, not a blocker), (4) a fallback only if a specific piece proves impossible, with evidence. Report only, no Talon voice commands or grammar.\nEOF\n$B/fm-send.sh $id \"$(cat $FM_HOME/data/$id/steer-port.txt)\" 2>&1 | tail -1\nstatus comment status-