 runs on iOS via ONNX Runtime or CoreML conversion; the w2l/flashlight decoder, lexicon.txt and lexicon_flat.bin are open formats we can reimplement or cross-compile for arm64 (libw2ldecode.dylib is only the Mac build); the Whisper ggml models run in whisper.cpp on iOS. Rewrite the report: (1) the concrete porting path for the Conformer AM + decoder + lexicon/grammar biasing, with effort and risk per piece, (2) a first spike that gets acoustic.onnx emitting tokens on an iPhone, (3) what must be copied from the Mac install (it is the captain's own licensed install; list any license check as a risk item, not a blocker), (4) a fallback only if a specific piece proves impossible, with evidence. Report only, no Talon voice commands or grammar.\nEOF\n$B/fm-send.sh $id \"$(cat $FM_HOME/data/$id/steer-port.txt)\" 2>&1 | tail -1\nstatus comment status-kdv \"Captain pushback: Talon recognizer mac-only/cant be ported is a cop out, that is the point, yes we can do this. Steered talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2 (Fable) to plan the port of AM+decoder to iPhone (ONNX/CoreML, decoder cross-compile, spike).\" 2>&1 | tail -1"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgBxCyXZvkTRKgs24HtgY","type":"assistant","uuid":"8c212da2-3ce2-4e05-b20e-e8ab5c84f8cc","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:59:52.682Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
