usually use this for PRs): main\n\nGit user: Trillium Smith\n\nStatus:\nM .claude/settings.json\n M .codex/hooks.json\n M .cursor/hooks.json\n M CHANGELOG.md\n?? .agents/hooks.json\n?? .entire/\n?? .opencode/plugins/entire.ts\n\nRecent commits:\nf650e380 fix(hooks): restore FM_GIT_HOOK_ACTIVE re-entrancy sentinel in generated wrappers\n58d4b73d chore: commit stray local working files so main is clean for local-only landing\n653d7cdb Merge remote-tracking branch 'upstream/main'\n9b1ada04 fix(bin): let a backlog captain hold bound the watcher's wedge escalation (#7338)\n4f77bb37 fix(bin): retry transient contribution forge reads once before waking (#7302)\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"d901d3a5-7dde-4cd4-b258-2113ff86f51b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"date","date":"2026-10-19"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"be1b7afc-2b04-4637-9ed9-cedec39546c9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T17:27:23.938Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nToday's date is 2026-10-19.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"be1b7afc-2b04-4637-9ed9-cedec39546c9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0e9a4794-85a0-4a94-a04d-81f92a0b9529","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Standing nudge, repeated: log every action in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked). Pull from the stores (robots, task, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review, projects). Take open robots items: diagnose or dispatch a fix, and close with evidence. Check quota-axi and speed metrics every poke. If usage is underspent, dispatch more work, preferring Fable. Keep the queue deep and review PRs and reports. Keep Sidecar and the Talon palette moving.\n   - Automated \"Continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes also arrive. Handle them, then ack with `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`.\n   - New captain instructions this segment (verbatim):\n     - \"brain gorefront varterboo all yolo\" (done: yolo ON for brain, forefront, forefront-backend, barter).\n     - \"we have 2 cycles left, use fable to improve the talon story - what is the avility yo get thr talon model to the phone so thr phone handles the speedh part in a talon-like way? we should have documentation on this partially\"\n     - \"Talon's recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - this is a cop out, that is the whole point. yes we can do this\"\n   - Standing rules:\n     - Inbox beads are captain messages: comment in the bead first.\n     - Never merge red or unreported required checks without an explicit waiver.\n     - Never tear down unlanded work.\n     - Address the user as \"captain\" and don't expose internal terms.\n     - Output shaping for an ADHD reader: lead with the action, numbered steps, state the win, and give a full PR URL with each PR mention.\n     - File tooling defects in `robots`.\n     - firstmate-repo fixes need captain consent before publishing.\n     - Never write Talon voice commands or grammar (captain-only).\n     - Never touch the Talon recordings corpus.\n     - No SMS sends without consent.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling:\n     - `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, then `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`. The ack prints a \"queued wakes pending\" warning that I never confirmed cleared.\n     - `bin/fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N`.\n     - `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`.\n     - Export `FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate`.\n     - Never use a persistent top-level `cd` (the hook denies it).\n   - Delivery flow:\n     - `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M` or `--scout`.\n     - Fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} with `python3 -I`. Intent must be the captain's words with no \"Captain\" label.\n     - `fm-tasks-axi.sh add <id> '<title>' --kind ship|scout`.\n     - `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> projects/<p> --mode M --yolo on|off --harness claude [--model fable --effort xhigh]`, or `--scout`.\n     - `fm-pr-merge.sh <id> <PR url>`.\n     - `fm-teardown.sh`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`.\n     - `fm-send.sh <id> [--resolve-key KEY] 'text'`, with no `--yes`. For text with apostrophes, write it to a file and use `\"$(cat file)\"`.\n     - `fm-crew-state.sh`, `fm-peek.sh`.\n   - ask-user-authority: decide in-scope findings, skip contract expansions.\n   - no-mistakes caveat: skipping both review and test gates makes push fail for lack of a durably recorded review-approved head. Approve past findings instead of skipping when the push step needs an approved head.\n   - GitHub Actions jobs fail in about 2s because of an account billing problem. Fixing it is a captain-only task at github.com/settings/billing.\n   - Project postures now:\n     - brain: [no-mistakes +yolo].\n     - forefront: [no-mistakes +yolo].\n     - forefront-backend: [no-mistakes +yolo].\n     - barter: [no-mistakes-prod-only +yolo].\n     - dotfiles: local-only, yolo off.\n     - behavioral-hooks and fm-hooks: direct-PR +yolo.\n   - Talon facts from the existing report (data/scout-talon-phone-asr/report.md):\n     - Talon's engine is a Conformer (wav2letter) with `acoustic.onnx` (111MB, PyTorch-exported ONNX).\n     - It uses lexicon.txt and lexicon_flat.bin.\n     - The native decoder is the Mac-only libw2ldecode.dylib.\n     - Whisper ggml models are bundled.\n     - Recordings are in ~/.talon/recordings, 329k FLAC files, which must stay local.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - data/projects.md: edited with sed. brain, forefront, forefront-backend and barter now carry +yolo. barter's note changed to \"yolo ON (captain 2026-10-19): green-PR merges autonomous\".\n   - data/dotfiles-codex-q1/brief.md: ship brief that adds the codex CLI to the macbook nix config. The branch fm/dotfiles-codex-q1 (f94f69c) is ready, built without a switch, and local-only, so it needs the captain's word to land.\n   - data/fb-commitments-inject-q1/brief.md: ship brief that makes runCommitments injectable (idea-pag9). The commit defbff5 adds setCommitmentsRunner, 9 route tests with a fake runner, and 71 lib tests pass.\n   - data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/brief.md and steer-port.txt: Fable scout (claude, model fable, effort xhigh). The deliverable is report.md with a porting path for the Conformer AM, decoder and lexicon/grammar biasing, a first iPhone spike for acoustic.onnx, a licence check as a risk item, and a fallback only with evidence. The report is not yet written.\n   - data/brain-fwd-file-q2/steer-dup.txt: steer used for the PR 46 supersession check.\n   - ~/.fm-nudge.text and ~/.local/bin/fm-nudge: nudge text and script (context only, not edited).\n   - mini1 `~/data/_retired/embeddeddolt-20261019-bootstrap-stray`: quarantined stray database.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - See the analysis section above. Key ones: the persistent-cd denial, zsh variable mangling, fm-send quoting, the operator-address intent refusal, the backlog-add requirement, and the push failure after skipping both gates.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Merged: brain PRs 44, 45 and 47, and forefront-backend PR 5.\n   - Closed: brain PR 46 (superseded by 44) and forefront-backend PRs 2 and 3 (superseded by 5).\n   - Torn down: brain-fwd-file-q2.\n   - Closed beads with evidence: robots-gbu6f, robots-ucj59, robots-qi64x, robots-shos9, task-4smbc.\n   - Still open: robots-xqffe (codex; the fix is on a branch awaiting landing) and the robots-q22c, 7iaq, wajev, sl1eq, 4ayi4, 2xsms, lc225, 5s8pw, fy7f9, d8dvl items.\n   - Usage at last check: Claude 43% and Fable 38% remaining, weekly reset 2026-10-20 00:00Z. Underspent.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The repeated standing nudge text (items 1-12; items 11 and 12 about usage metrics and more work/review were shown most recently).\n   - \"brain gorefront varterboo all yolo\"\n   - \"we have 2 cycles left, use fable to improve the talon story - what is the avility yo get thr talon model to the phone so thr phone handles the speedh part in a talon-like way? we should have documentation on this partially\"\n   - \"Talon's recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - this is a cop out, that is the whole point. yes we can do this\"\n   - Automated system notifications saying no human input was received (Stop-hook wakes) are not user messages.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Drain and handle the current \"check: inactive-outcome\" wake, then run its WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED command.\n   - Wait for fb-commitments-inject-q1 to reach checks-passed. If the PR is green, merge it with `fm-pr-merge.sh fb-commitments-inject-q1 <url>`. Then close idea-pag9 with evidence and run fm-fleet-sync.\n   - Read the talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2 report when it lands, relay findings, and promote to a ship if the captain wants one.\n   - Barter PRs 2 (https://github.com/trillium/barter/pull/2) and 7 and forefront-backend PR 7 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/7) have red checks from billing. Merge only after billing is fixed or the captain names a specific waiver.\n   - After billing is fixed, run the forefront-backend consolidation task for PRs 4, 6 and 7.\n   - Captain decisions still pending:\n     - Fix GitHub billing.\n     - Land fm/dotfiles-codex-q1, then log in to codex.\n     - Consent to publish firstmate-repo fixes (robots-q22c, wajev, 5s8pw root, d8dvl).\n     - The robots-sl1eq design call.\n     - The inbox-kv6b product-judgment reply.\n     - Many review-store and mini0-ops/macbook-ops holds.\n     - Credential rotations (review-2p3, 3a3, 7s2).\n   - Follow-ups: task-tywam, idea-dko0, the Sidecar and palette tasks (task-eykz1, rge87, oahqr, myaks; talon-palette-ios is not a registered project), and robots-7iaq.\n   - Keep logging each poke in status-kdv and keep the queue deep.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Handling the automated Stop-hook wake \"check: inactive-outcome\". It had not yet been drained when the summary was requested. In flight: fb-commitments-inject-q1 is validating again after the rerun with the review and test gates approved, and talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2 is working. My last captain-facing message said the inbox note was only bookkeeping and that nothing needed the captain.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh` to read the \"inactive-outcome\" wake, handle it (likely a worker or scout that went inactive with an outcome to reconcile; check `fm-crew-state.sh` for fb-commitments-inject-q1 and talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2), then run the exact `--ack-through` command it prints. Then continue: merge fb-commitments-inject-q1 once its PR is green, and read the Talon scout report when it lands.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"049adbe4-ebbd-4c0a-a497-70deb19c1f66","timestamp":"2026-10-19T17:26:50.103Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":399,"turnIndex":783},"turnOrigin":"task_notification","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
