{"parentUuid":"b42938e0-648a-4802-9b34-bb8863e397e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC1pnLyZy3xYP25EHYHE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the flow, step by step, from what the project record says (I haven't read the code itself):\n\n1. **Share sheet:** on the phone you tap Share in Safari, Photos, Instagram or any other app, then pick Firstmate Share. This opens the Share Extension, a small piece bundled with the app.\n2. **Extension reads the item:** it pulls out the URL, text, image or PDF you shared. The URL and text handling comes from the MIT-licensed readeck-ios code, and the image and PDF handling from swift-paperless.\n3. **Extension sends it:** it makes an HTTPS POST to `https://macbook.hippo-tilapia.ts.net:8771/share`. The request carries a shared secret in a header. The secret is kept in the iOS keychain, and the host app and the extension both read it.\n4. **Tailnet only:** that address works only on your tailnet. Funnel (public exposure) was refused, so nothing outside it can reach the receiver.\n5. **Receiver checks it:** a small launchd service on the MacBook listens on 127.0.0.1:8770 behind that tailnet address. It rejects a missing or wrong secret with 401, and anything over about 2MB with 413.\n6. **Receiver files a bead:** it files an inbox bead with the shared content, the same as `inbox q`. Images and files are saved to `~/data/inbox-attachments`, and the bead points to them. It replies 201 with the bead id.\n7. **The poke:** a watcher already watches the inbox store for new beads. A new one wakes me, and I read it under the rule that inbox beads are your messages.\n\n**Known gap:** when two shares land in one batch, the watcher dropped the wake for the second one (robots-xcay2). The bead was still filed, but I wasn't poked.\n\n**Not working yet:** I only verified steps 5 to 7 with simulated posts from the MacBook. No share from the phone has been sent, because the app can't be installed until Xcode has an Apple ID for signing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_read_input_tokens":104655,"output_tokens":699,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":40},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":104655,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgC1pn6Lz5nkWrABiGt7T","type":"assistant","uuid":"80aef8b0-e861-428d-b89f-9addfcf9c017","timestamp":"2026-10-19T17:47:22.637Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
