{"parentUuid":"5311988e-eb0a-4438-8e64-2a240b6ea820","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC1w12Ntb9SDs8Ysh6Xy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, I need to correct my last two answers. The note field and chips are already built. I read the code this time. I told you they weren't built, which was wrong, and I've closed the duplicate task I filed (task-hx0p9).\n\nBetween picking Firstmate and the send, there is a compose step:\n1. **You pick Firstmate in the share sheet.** The extension loads what you shared (URL, text, image or file) and shows a short summary of it.\n2. **Compose screen appears.** It has four optional chips, Person, Task, Idea and Later, and a free-text note box. Both are optional.\n3. **You tap Send.** Nothing goes out before this.\n4. **Text and URL shares** go as an immediate POST. **Images and files** go as an upload that can finish after the sheet closes. The screen then shows the bead id and closes after about a second.\n5. **On the MacBook,** the receiver turns your chips and note into an `Ask:` line in the inbox bead body, next to the item.\n6. **Follow-up note:** the app remembers the last bead you sent. From the host app you can add a note to it, and the receiver stores that as a comment on the same bead.\n\nSo an Instagram screenshot can go with \"Person\" ticked and \"we want to contact them for barter\" in the note.\n\nThe setup changed since my earlier summary. The app comes prefilled with the receiver address and needs no secret typed in. It uses plain http over the tailnet on :8774, and signing now uses team 85PWBA3B59.\n\n**Still blocked:** none of this runs on your phone until the branch lands and the app is installed, and I haven't confirmed the signing blocker is cleared. I haven't run it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_