{"parentUuid":"de10b415-2854-437b-9283-6daded84e14f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"133fbfba-db7c-42ef-b2fa-f8b4759e7408","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WGzWpFMaABRqxkUvP3qQZD","type":"tool_result","content":"metadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nCaptain works from his phone and cannot type long URLs. Explainer/report pages go in `~/fm_home/firstmate/.lavish/site/` (HTML file + a new `<a class=\"p\">` entry in `index.html`), served by launchd `com.firstmate.pages` at http://macbook:4380/ (tailnet IP 100.74.138.74:4380). He asked for lavish/self-hosted, not claude.ai artifacts.\n\n**Why:** 2026-10-14 he said \"lavish, self hosted\" and \"i can't type that in\".\n**How to apply:** for any new \"give me a link\" page, write the HTML into that site dir, add it to index.html, and give him `http://macbook:4380/` (plus the direct page link). Do not rely on a lavish-axi session URL; it dies when idle. See [[status-kvo-channel]].\nbin: ~/.local/state/fnm_multishells/26542_1792052127658/bin/lavish-axi\ndescription: \"Lavish Editor helps agents turn rich HTML artifacts into collaborative human review surfaces. Whenever you are about to give user a complex response that will be easier to understand via\nvisual_guidance[5]: \"Use visual hierarchy to make the most important decisions, risks, tradeoffs, and next actions obvious at a glance\",\"Show, don't tell: explain concepts, flows, relationships, and c\nplaybooks[8]{id,use_when}:\n  diagram,\"Explain relationships, flows, state, architecture, and concepts with illustrations\"\n  table,Turn dense records into scan-friendly review surfaces\n  comparison,\"Show options, tradeoffs, and current vs target behavior\"\n  plan,Explain a product or technical plan before implementation\n  code,\"Render source code, code files, patches, PR diffs, and before/after code inside Lavish artifacts\"\n  input,\"Must be used when the agent needs to collect user input on decisions, choices, preferences, triage, scope, or other structured feedback from within the artifact\"\n  explanation,\"Explain an existing system, PR, incident, or decision to a reader who was not there - when the goal is understanding what is and why, not choosing a direction or inspecting a plan befor\n  slides,Create a deliberate presentation when slides are requested\nhelp[13]: \"Run `lavish-axi <html-file>` to open or resume a Lavish Editor session. If the user explicitly ended the session from the browser, this refuses to reopen it and explains why instead of reop\nactivity-2026-10-16.html\ncalendar-status.html\ndental-proposal.pdf\nindex.html\nmassage-flyer-v2.pdf\nmassage-flyer-v2.png\nmassage-flyer-v2b.pdf\nmassage-flyer-v2b.png\nmassage-flyer-v3.pdf\nmassage-flyer-v3.png","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4601aaad-d4ac-499b-8b96-91ad21c5418b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T17:57:31.159Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"metadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nCaptain works from his phone and cannot type long URLs. Explainer/report pages go in `~/fm_home/firstmate/.lavish/site/` (HTML file + a new `<a class=\"p\">` entry in `index.html`), served by launchd `com.firstmate.pages` at http://macbook:4380/ (tailnet IP 100.74.138.74:4380). He asked for lavish/self-hosted, not claude.ai artifacts.\n\n**Why:** 2026-10-14 he said \"lavish, self hosted\" and \"i can't type that in\".\n**How to apply:** for any new \"give me a link\" page, write the HTML into that site dir, add it to index.html, and give him `http://macbook:4380/` (plus the direct page link). Do not rely on a lavish-axi session URL; it dies when idle. See [[status-kvo-channel]].\nbin: ~/.local/state/fnm_multishells/26542_1792052127658/bin/lavish-axi\ndescription: \"Lavish Editor helps agents turn rich HTML artifacts into collaborative human review surfaces. Whenever you are about to give user a complex response that will be easier to understand via\nvisual_guidance[5]: \"Use visual hierarchy to make the most important decisions, risks, tradeoffs, and next actions obvious at a glance\",\"Show, don't tell: explain concepts, flows, relationships, and c\nplaybooks[8]{id,use_when}:\n  diagram,\"Explain relationships, flows, state, architecture, and concepts with illustrations\"\n  table,Turn dense records into scan-friendly review surfaces\n  comparison,\"Show options, tradeoffs, and current vs target behavior\"\n  plan,Explain a product or technical plan before implementation\n  code,\"Render source code, code files, patches, PR diffs, and before/after code inside Lavish artifacts\"\n  input,\"Must be used when the agent needs to collect user input on decisions, choices, preferences, triage, scope, or other structured feedback from within the artifact\"\n  explanation,\"Explain an existing system, PR, incident, or decision to a reader who was not there - when the goal is understanding what is and why, not choosing a direction or inspecting a plan befor\n  slides,Create a deliberate presentation when slides are requested\nhelp[13]: \"Run `lavish-axi <html-file>` to open or resume a Lavish Editor session. If the user explicitly ended the session from the browser, this refuses to reopen it and explains why instead of reop\nactivity-2026-10-16.html\ncalendar-status.html\ndental-proposal.pdf\nindex.html\nmassage-flyer-v2.pdf\nmassage-flyer-v2.png\nmassage-flyer-v2b.pdf\nmassage-flyer-v2b.png\nmassage-flyer-v3.pdf\nmassage-flyer-v3.png","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"de10b415-2854-437b-9283-6daded84e14f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
