{"parentUuid":"03279286-e57d-4442-9d9a-b74aef0b4a8d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC2uqC8J45oCu6LT9fPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, the move into brain is only partly working. fm-hooks did log the scout in the fleet store, but it did not file the report in brain.\n\n- **What worked:** the hook recorded the scout's progress and its finished status in `fleet-talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2`.\n- **What failed:** it made no brain bead for the report. I think the hook missed the scout's finished line, but I haven't reproduced it. That left brain-key50 as the Talon verdict, and it was wrong. It said a full iPhone port wasn't reasonable.\n- **What I did:**\n  1. I filed the full report in brain as brain-r1ccu.\n  2. I marked brain-key50 as superseded by it.\n  3. I filed robots-fkb70 for the hook to be fixed.\n- **My own slip:** my first comment on robots-fkb70 landed on robots-7iaq by mistake. I added a note there saying to ignore it.\n\nYour Parlay question is not answered yet. The line \"Start by enrolling in Parlay...\" comes from `bin/fm-brief.sh`, the script that writes every worker's instructions. I haven't yet checked whether anything uses the enrollment. Want me to finish that check and then lay out what removing it or enforcing it would look like?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":137693,"output_tokens":416,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":428,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":137693,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens