{"parentUuid":"9e0ecd0e-5bbe-4c39-9a97-074418f665e8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14986450 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"538cffa5-a8b0-472c-8041-2f3ab9189f30","timestamp":"2026-10-19T18:05:17.171Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14986450 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"538cffa5-a8b0-472c-8041-2f3ab9189f30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC3Cj7y5swuw8xBG7kyF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, I can't yet say whether the Parlay enrollment line gets used, and I found no sign that firstmate is what puts it on your prompts.\n\n**What I found:**\n1. **Not in the current code:** today's `bin/fm-brief.sh` (the script that writes every worker's instructions) has no \"Start by enrolling in Parlay\" line. Only stale copies in old worktrees (`~/code/_wt/*`, `firstmate-gnhf-worktrees`) still have it.\n2. **Where it shows up:** it appears as typed input in your herdr pane history, wrapped in triple quotes. That points to a prefix added by something on your side, such as a launcher, alias or prompt template.\n3. **Some Parlay use is real:** there's a Parlay listener record for macbook-ops, and a worker named `rode-parlay-q2` is on Parlay project work. That says Parlay is used. It doesn't say sessions follow the enrollment line.\n\n**What I haven't measured:** how many sessions actually enroll versus just see the line.\n\n**Removing it:** find the one launcher or template that adds it and delete the line. Nothing else depends on it that I found.\n\n**Enforcing it:**\n1. Make the session start check that the session is enrolled.\n2. Refuse to start work, or warn loudly, if it isn't.\n3. Fix the stale copies in the old worktrees.\n\nEnforcing is more work, and it's only worth it if you want firstmate to always be able to reach workers through Parlay.\n\nI filed the decision as idea-7jmo. Which way do you lean?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":142504,"output_tokens":516,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache