{"parentUuid":"6087ed70-768e-4e58-b4ed-4d29c87e3947","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC3WbbHpwGMDSDSK6Dge","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, you're right that it was in worker briefs, but only in old ones. New briefs no longer have it.\n\n- **Where it appeared:** 6 of the 409 saved briefs contain the \"FIRST ACTION: enroll in Parlay\" block. They include task-2hl6a, task-ik1l6 and talon-iphone-research. All six were written on 2026-09-27 or earlier.\n- **Current briefs:** the brief for the Talon phone scout, written today, doesn't have it. The current `bin/fm-brief.sh` and its git history don't contain the line either. That script wrote the old briefs from a variant it no longer has.\n- **Stale copies:** old worktrees under `~/code/_wt/*` still carry the line in their copies of `fm-brief.sh`. Workers started from those would still get it.\n- **Actual use:** the line told workers to run `parlay listen --agent <id>` as a background listener. Today only one listener record exists, for macbook-ops. So almost no workers are enrolled, even though the briefs asked every one to be.\n\n**Removing it:** it's already gone from the live generator. The remaining step is deleting the stale worktrees, or at least not launching from them.\n\n**Enforcing it:**\n1. Put the block back into `bin/fm-brief.sh`.\n2. Have `fm-spawn.sh` check that the worker's listener record exists after launch.\n3. Refuse to count the worker as live until it does.\n\nThat makes Parlay the guaranteed way to reach workers. It only pays off if you want that. Right now status files and the steering inbox already carry that traffic, which is probably why almost nothing enrolled. I lean toward leaving it removed. Say so and I'll close idea-7jmo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":144968,"output_tokens":666,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":98},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":802,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":144968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":802},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgC3WbJg9iheA8gwm3qHK","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e7c31e1-d850-44c7-a2f3-5e614cc45e2c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T18:09:26.845Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
