{"parentUuid":"49a4ac9c-5543-48fa-940c-a6d53d11ed1c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC3iF2NjSvxiUAZXxmn5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pe8vAjaHms7LN3tZFP5smt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; ID=fmh-scout-capture-q1\n$B/fm-brief.sh $ID fm-hooks --mode direct-PR 2>&1 | tail -2\npython3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/fmh-scout-capture-q1/brief.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('{TASK}',\"The goal is for finished scout reports to flow into brain automatically through fm-hooks. Scout talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2 finished on 2026-10-19 with its report at data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/report.md in the firstmate home. fm-hooks wrote its fleet-store status comments, but src/scout-capture.ts did not file a brain bead, so a stale wrong brain bead stayed the Talon verdict. The failure is tracked as robots-fkb70.\")\ns=s.replace('{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}',\"Reproduce why scout-capture did not fire for that scout (check the done-line shape against DONE_LINE and the fm-fleet-ledger appended signal; the scout's done status text was: report written at data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/report.md; Talon AM+decoder+lexicon shown portable on Mac with real blobs). Fix the root cause with a regression test using that done line. Also make capture fire when the fleet bead reaches state done and the task's data/<id>/report.md exists, idempotently (deterministic id, no duplicates). Out of scope: other hook behavior, backfilling old scouts. Comment the evidence on robots-fkb70 when the PR is up.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n$B/fm-tasks-axi.sh add $ID 'fm-hooks: scout-capture misses finished scouts (robots-fkb70)' --kind ship 2>&1 | tail -1\nHERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 $B/fm-spawn.sh $ID projects/fm-hooks --mode direct-PR --yolo on --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-200"},"c