{"parentUuid":"a75bff05-f860-434d-a31b-500663fc78bf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"47bf71f7-2a17-4b53-a8e5-4ae6ff37a00e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Standing nudge (repeated every poke, 12 items): log every action in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked); put durable work into the right bead; never have a no-work turn; pull from projects, task ready, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review; keep Sidecar (project-yg4v, runbooks-5vr) and Talon palette (project-7u7w, idea-7d0b) moving; overnight usability/onboarding plans; idle design review (runbooks-b6e); take top open robots items, diagnose/dispatch fix and close with evidence; check quota-axi + speed metrics each poke and spend underused usage (prefer Fable); keep queue deep and review PRs/reports.\n   - Automated \"Continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes: handle, ack with `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`.\n   - Captain asks this segment: (a) Firstmate Share iPhone app: how notes/text work, how the flow works, chips must be single-select, \"later\" unclear, wants lavish-page mockups of flow; likes the idea as an agent tool; (b) \"did that fable agent land?\" (Talon scout); (c) why the \"Start by enrolling in Parlay…\" text appears, whether it's used, what removing/enforcing would look like, clarified it's in the briefs; (d) are we using fm-hooks to move scout content into brain (the goal); (e) is the hook worker an always-running daemon; (f) latest message \"how are\" + pasted nudge text (treated as a poke; the \"how are\" question was cut off). Earlier standing instruction: Talon recognizer on phone is the whole point (\"yes we can do this\").\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling: `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, then exact `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`; `bin/fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N`; `fm-inbox.sh drain --ack`; export `FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate`; never top-level `cd`.\n   - Delivery flow: `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M`, fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} with `python3 -I`, `fm-tasks-axi.sh add <id> '<title>' --kind ship`, `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> projects/<p> --mode M --yolo on --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh`, `fm-pr-merge.sh <id> <url>`, `fm-teardown.sh`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`, `fm-send.sh <id> 'text'` (use file + `$(cat)` for apostrophes; prints nothing on success/uncertain).\n   - Project postures: brain/forefront/forefront-backend [no-mistakes +yolo]; barter [no-mistakes-prod-only +yolo]; fm-hooks and behavioral-hooks [direct-PR +yolo]; dotfiles local-only yolo off; GitHub Actions fail ~2s from account billing (captain-only fix at github.com/settings/billing).\n   - Firstmate Share: iOS Share Extension → compose view (chips ShareIntent person/task/idea/later multi-select currently, note) → POST to tailnet receiver (launchd com.firstmateshare.receiver on 127.0.0.1:8770, tailscale https :8771, plain http :8774) → inbox bead with Ask line; follow-up note as bead comment; inbox-store-watch wakes firstmate. Branch fm/firstmate-share-build-20261019 (macbook-ops/projects/firstmate-share, local-only) awaits landing; OTA install blocked on Xcode Apple ID signing.\n   - Talon-on-iPhone: Conformer acoustic.onnx on CoreML, w2ldecode (BSD) built for iOS arm64, lexicon.txt/lexicon_flat.bin, hand-built command DFA, grammar compiler is the largest remaining piece; Talon stays authority on Mac, phone sends phrases to existing /execute endpoint.\n   - fm-hooks: harness hooks only observe/enqueue to ~/.fm-hooks/queue; daemons com.fm-hooks.worker and com.fm-hooks.bead-poller (launchd) drain queue and apply rules from projects/fm-hooks/config/fm-hooks.rules.json; code changes need a restart (`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/<label>`); scout-capture.ts (DONE_LINE regex, fm-fleet-ledger appended signal) files brain bead for finished scouts.\n   - Lavish pages: write HTML to ~/fm_home/firstmate/.lavish/site/, add `<a class=\"p\">` entry to index.html, served at http://macbook:4380/.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/.lavish/site/firstmate-share-mockups.html (created): three phone mockups (A single-select plain verbs: Add a person/Make a task/Save an idea/Just keep it; B note-only; C chips fill note), flow diagram, questions for captain. Entry added to .lavish/site/index.html (line 6 via python insert).\n   - data/talon-phone-grammar-scout-q2/report.md: Fable scout report (345 lines), sections 1a-1g port pieces, section 2 spike plan, risk register (EULA, CoreML first-launch compile), effort 13-20 days.\n   - data/fmh-scout-capture-q1/brief.md: ship brief for fm-hooks scout-capture fix (done/merged/torn down).\n   - /private/tmp/claude-501/ms.txt, ms2.txt: fm-send messages routing spike 1 and spike 2 to macbook-ops.\n   - macbook-ops/projects/firstmate-share/ShareExtension/Sources/ShareViewController.swift and Shared/ShareIntent.swift (read): compose step with `model.intents` (Set) and `model.note`, `payload.ask = ShareAsk(intents:note:)`; ShareIntent enum cases person/task/idea/later; ShareAsk.fields emits `intents` comma-joined and `note`.\n   - projects/fm-hooks/src/scout-capture.ts (read), README.md line ~137 rule `fm-scout-report-capture`; config/fm-hooks.rules.json line ~106 has that rule.\n   - ~/.fm-hooks/queue/failed/*.json and *.json.error: 672 files; sample rule fm-ledger-timeline (operation fm-wake-drain.sh, action `fm-hooks-bead-action ledger {operation} {correlationId} {ruleId}`), error \"action exited 1\".\n   - data/*/brief.md: 6 old briefs contain \"# FIRST ACTION: enroll in Parlay … `parlay listen --agent <id>`\".\n   - Beads created/changed: task-hx0p9 (closed dup), task-gj3l7 (Talon spike 1), task-6qvs7 (Talon spike 2), brain-r1ccu (Talon report), brain-key50 (marked superseded), robots-fkb70 (closed), idea-7jmo (Parlay enrollment decision), idea-pag9 (closed).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - persistent-cd denial on `cd` → use absolute paths.\n   - mark-processed refused (beyond read cursor 2116) → later marks succeeded after cursor advanced.\n   - sed -i insert failed on macOS → used python3 -I.\n   - Wrongly told captain the share note field wasn't built → read code, found e03d800/d81718f, closed task-hx0p9, corrected.\n   - Comment landed on robots-7iaq by mistake → recommented on robots-fkb70, added ignore note on 7iaq.\n   - fm-send gave no confirmation (possible double send to macbook-ops).\n   - fleet-sync: forefront-backend clone STUCK (uncommitted changes, behind origin) — left untouched, not yet filed.\n   - A Python loop over failed hook jobs timed out (120s) and went to background; abandoned.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Merged: forefront-backend PR 8 (https://github.com/trillium/forefront-backend/pull/8), firstmate_hooks PR 8 (https://github.com/trillium/firstmate_hooks/pull/8).\n   - Talon on iPhone proven feasible on device (spikes 1 and 2 passed).\n   - fm-hooks scout-capture fixed and worker/poller restarted; not yet confirmed with a new scout.\n   - Ongoing: why 672 hook jobs failed (rule fm-ledger-timeline \"action exited 1\" seen; need breakdown by rule and root cause).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Repeated standing nudge text (12 items, as given in the pasted blocks), including the latest preceded by \"how are\".\n   - \"share with firstmate - did we ever end up with the abiltiy to add notes and stuff? how would that work anyway?\"\n   - \"not notes, the iphone app share with firstmate, might just be called firstmate\"\n   - \"what I mean is if i send firstamte a piece of text or content, if it is an image, how do I add text?\"\n   - \"how does the share actually flow through the application?\"\n   - \"is there more internals between 2 and 3 that are hidden? I share / some app interaction / send?\"\n   - \"I see that the buttons allow for multiples to be selected, that is not right. I also do not know what `later` means here. I think what I'd like is for the agent to make some mockups of what I want and waht flow I want in a lavish page, so that we can get a better idea of where to go. This is infinitely better than it was before, and I thikn that this idea has a lot of promise as an agent tool\"\n   - \"did that fable agent land?\"\n   - \"\"\"Start by enrolling in Parlay so firstmate can reach you and you can report back\"\"\" I see this at the beginning of every prompt, but I am not sure we actually use this feature, can you check? What would it look like to remove it? what would it look like to enforce usage within the workflows?\n   - \"No what I am trying to say is that it makes it into the briefs we use\"\n   - \"Are we successfully using fm_hooks to move this type of content into brain? that is the goal\" (about the Fable Talon scout reply)\n   - \"whewn you say hook worker, are you impmplying that the hook system has some sort of daemon that is always runngin?\"\n   - \"how are\" + pasted nudge text.\n   - Earlier (carried): \"brain gorefront varterboo all yolo\"; \"we have 2 cycles left, use fable to improve the talon story…\"; \"Talon's recognizer is mac-only and cant be ported - this is a cop out, that is the whole point. yes we can do this\".\n   - Automated system notifications (Stop-hook wakes, \"no human input\") are not user messages.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish the hook-failure diagnosis (672 failed jobs; group by ruleId/error, find root cause of fm-ledger-timeline \"action exited 1\"); file robots bead/dispatch fix if a real defect; log the poke in status-kdv (this poke not yet logged).\n   - Captain decisions pending: pick Firstmate Share compose option A/B/C (http://macbook:4380/firstmate-share-mockups.html) and the choice set; land branches fm/talon-phone-asr-spike1-20261019 (930c183), fm/dotfiles-codex-q1, fm/dotfiles-nm-q1, fm/firstmate-share-build-20261019; go for Talon grammar compiler spike (not started); Parlay enrollment remove vs enforce (idea-7jmo; I lean leave removed); GitHub billing fix; consent to publish firstmate-repo fixes (robots-q22c, wajev, 5s8pw root, d8dvl); robots-sl1eq design call; inbox-kv6b reply; review-store/macbook-ops/mini0-ops holds; credential rotations (review-2p3, 3a3, 7s2); inbox-cglf deactivate target; Talon licence/EULA check.\n   - Barter PRs (rls fix task-03lms, socials task-ho60f) and forefront-backend PRs 4, 6, 7 red from billing: merge only after billing fixed or explicit waiver; then forefront-backend consolidation.\n   - forefront-backend clone stuck in fleet-sync (uncommitted changes, behind origin) — needs investigation/tracking bead.\n   - Verify fm-send route to macbook-ops (possible double send); verify scout-capture works on next finished scout; other follow-ups: task-tywam, idea-dko0, Sidecar/palette tasks (task-eykz1, rge87, oahqr, myaks), robots-7iaq (upstream no-mistakes defect), robots-lqep3 (flaky fm-hooks test), robots-xqffe (codex).\n   - Keep usage spent: last quota claude 38%, fable 30% remaining, reset 2026-10-20 00:00Z (underspent).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Handling the latest nudge poke (message began \"how are\" then pasted the standing nudge). I was diagnosing why 672 fm-hooks queue jobs failed (offered to captain earlier). Last observations: `~/.fm-hooks/queue/failed` holds 672 `.json` jobs with `.json.error` files (\"Error: action exited 1\"); the newest sample was ruleId `fm-ledger-timeline`, operation `fm-wake-drain.sh`, action command `fm-hooks-bead-action` args `[\"ledger\",\"{operation}\",\"{correlationId}\",\"{ruleId}\"]`, created 2026-10-18T06:57:56Z. A heavy python loop timed out and I abandoned it. No poke log written yet for this cycle.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the poke: tally failed hook jobs by `ruleId` with a cheap command (e.g. `grep -ho '\"ruleId\":\"[^\"]*\"' ~/.fm-hooks/queue/failed/*.json | sort | uniq -c`) and inspect the `fm-hooks-bead-action ledger` exit-1 cause, then file/dispatch a fix in robots and log to status-kdv. Quote of where I left off: \"Error: action exited 1\" / `{\"id\":\"49b8…\",\"ruleId\":\"fm-ledger-timeline\",\"operation\":\"fm-wake-drain.sh\",…}`. Also answer the captain's cut-off \"how are\" if they clarify; do not start the grammar compiler or land any local-only branch without their word.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"6bb7134d-c5af-4efa-bd1a-ee434146f68e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T18:55:02.438Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":412,"turnIndex":803},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["01757a18-b777-4050-9c30-547421ea3994"],"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
