{"parentUuid":"ee837fda-0f7d-4e64-a74a-addd53b30fc5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f54f52a6-8527-4b1b-8ab8-8b3235e282bc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TgrvoM8DtJxZEhtEBrz4un","type":"tool_result","content":"<p class=mut>After sending, the app can add a follow-up note to the same share.</p>\n\n<h2>Option A: one choice, plain verbs (single-select)</h2>\n<div class=row>\n<div class=phone><h3>Firstmate</h3><div class=thumb>Instagram screenshot</div>\n<div class=cap>What should I do with this?</div>\n<div class=chips><span class=\"chip on\">Add a person</span><span class=chip>Make a task</span><span class=chip>Save an idea</span><span class=chip>Just keep it</span></div>\n<div class=note>we want to contact them for barter</div><div class=send>Send</div>\n<div class=cap>Tap one; tapping another switches. \"Just keep it\" is the default.</div></div>\n<div><b>Good:</b> one decision, clear verbs, no ambiguity for me.<br><b>Cost:</b> can't say \"task AND person\" in one share; use the note.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Option B: no chips, note only, I decide</h2>\n<div class=row>\n<div class=phone><h3>Firstmate</h3><div class=thumb>Instagram screenshot</div>\n<div class=cap>Tell me what to do (optional)</div>\n<div class=note>add them to the person store, contact for barter</div><div class=send>Send</div>\n<div class=cap>Simplest screen. I read the note and route it.</div></div>\n<div><b>Good:</b> most flexible, handles combos.<br><b>Cost:</b> more typing on the phone; voice dictation helps.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Option C: chips as quick-fill for the note</h2>\n<div class=row>\n<div class=phone><h3>Firstmate</h3><div class=thumb>Instagram screenshot</div>\n<div class=chips><span class=chip>Add person</span><span class=chip>Task</span><span class=chip>Idea</span></div>\n<div class=note>Add person: <i>we want to contact them for barter</i></div><div class=send>Send</div>\n<div class=cap>Tapping a chip types its phrase into the note. You can edit or stack phrases. Everything sent is just text.</div></div>\n<div><b>Good:</b> fast taps plus free text, combos possible.<br><b>Cost:</b> chips aren't a strict choice, so it is less structured.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Your call</h2>\n<div class=q><b>1.</b> A, B or C?</div>\n<div class=\"q b\"><b>2.</b> If A: which four choices? My guess: Add a person, Make a task, Save an idea, Just keep it.</div>\n<div class=\"q b\"><b>3.</b> Anything missing, e.g. \"Reply to this\", \"Add to calendar\", \"Research this\"?</div>\n<p class=mut>Bigger idea you mentioned: shares as an agent tool. Agents could also share to you or each other through the same endpoint. Say the word and I'll mock that flow too.</p>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bb1cc0c0-dfe6-4191-bcf2-18cb66091ec8","timestamp":"2026-10-19T19:04:03.416Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"<p class=mut>After sending, the app can add a follow-up note to the same share.</p>\n\n<h2>Option A: one choice, plain verbs (single-select)</h2>\n<div class=row>\n<div class=phone><h3>Firstmate</h3><div class=thumb>Instagram screenshot</div>\n<div class=cap>What should I do with this?</div>\n<div class=chips><span class=\"chip on\">Add a person</span><span class=chip>Make a task</span><span class=chip>Save an idea</span><span class=chip>Just keep it</span></div>\n<div class=note>we want to contact them for barter</div><div class=send>Send</div>\n<div class=cap>Tap one; tapping another switches. \"Just keep it\" is the default.</div></div>\n<div><b>Good:</b> one decision, clear verbs, no ambiguity for me.<br><b>Cost:</b> can't say \"task AND person\" in one share; use the note.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Option B: no chips, note only, I decide</h2>\n<div class=row>\n<div class=phone><h3>Firstmate</h3><div class=thumb>Instagram screenshot</div>\n<div class=cap>Tell me what to do (optional)</div>\n<div class=note>add them to the person store, contact for barter</div><div class=send>Send</div>\n<div class=cap>Simplest screen. I read the note and route it.</div></div>\n<div><b>Good:</b> most flexible, handles combos.<br><b>Cost:</b> more typing on the phone; voice dictation helps.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Option C: chips as quick-fill for the note</h2>\n<div class=row>\n<div class=phone><h3>Firstmate</h3><div class=thumb>Instagram screenshot</div>\n<div class=chips><span class=chip>Add person</span><span class=chip>Task</span><span class=chip>Idea</span></div>\n<div class=note>Add person: <i>we want to contact them for barter</i></div><div class=send>Send</div>\n<div class=cap>Tapping a chip types its phrase into the note. You can edit or stack phrases. Everything sent is just text.</div></div>\n<div><b>Good:</b> fast taps plus free text, combos possible.<br><b>Cost:</b> chips aren't a strict choice, so it is less structured.</div>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Your call</h2>\n<div class=q><b>1.</b> A, B or C?</div>\n<div class=\"q b\"><b>2.</b> If A: which four choices? My guess: Add a person, Make a task, Save an idea, Just keep it.</div>\n<div class=\"q b\"><b>3.</b> Anything missing, e.g. \"Reply to this\", \"Add to calendar\", \"Research this\"?</div>\n<p class=mut>Bigger idea you mentioned: shares as an agent tool. Agents could also share to you or each other through the same endpoint. Say the word and I'll mock that flow too.</p>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee837fda-0f7d-4e64-a74a-addd53b30fc5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
