{"parentUuid":"0784edc9-50c5-42ff-8603-07e6e07dc701","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC7vVBxDhJwuMEdnMmKd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_read_input_tokens":97258,"output_tokens":436,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":99},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":97258,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":872,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgC7vUY23y9BgqeWNCPdn","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed47fa95-9d01-4994-b02f-6068c61d63aa","timestamp":"2026-10-19T19:07:14.550Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"ed47fa95-9d01-4994-b02f-6068c61d63aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC7vVBxDhJwuMEdnMmKd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Outbound only today, captain.\n\nThe app POSTs the share to the receiver, which creates the inbox bead. The app can also add a follow-up note as a bead comment. Nothing flows back to the phone. You'd find out how a share was handled by looking at the bead.\n\nA return path would be small to add, because the phone already reaches the receiver over the tailnet:\n\n1. **Status per share:** the app polls the receiver for each share's bead state (open, answered, closed) and shows my last comment. It's the simplest option, with no push infrastructure.\n2. **Push notification:** when I answer or close the bead, a push goes to the phone. It needs the Apple push setup, which is blocked on the same Xcode signing as the install.\n3. **Two-way thread:** the bead's comments show as a chat in the app, and you reply from the phone. This is the agent-tool idea you liked. I'd build it on top of option 1.\n\nI recommend option 1 now, and the thread view in the second round. Should I add a \"Sent\" list with status to the Option D mockup?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_read_input_tokens":97258,"output_tokens":436,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":99},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":97258,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":