{"parentUuid":"5015319d-3a5a-490f-9312-d6d00c469f1c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"02987af3-1181-466b-b45f-6be2d8e63e2f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Standing nudge, repeated each poke (12 items):\n     - Log all actions in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked).\n     - Put durable work in the right bead.\n     - Never have a no-work turn.\n     - Pull from projects, task ready, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review.\n     - Keep Sidecar (project-yg4v, runbooks-5vr) and the Talon palette (project-7u7w, idea-7d0b) moving.\n     - Overnight usability/onboarding plans.\n     - Idle design review (runbooks-b6e).\n     - Take the top open robots items, diagnose or dispatch a fix, and close with evidence.\n     - Check quota-axi and speed metrics each poke and spend underused usage (prefer Fable).\n     - Keep the queue deep and review PRs/reports.\n   - Automated \"Continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes: handle, then ack with `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`.\n   - Captain requests this segment:\n     - Firstmate Share iPhone app design (two boxes: original+notes with single-select store chips top3 + A–Z picker; instructions box with fixed inbox chip; mini preview; config object `top3` served by receiver with manual refresh; return channel via \"Sent\" list).\n     - Talon palette \"select the command\" input must strip all punctuation.\n     - \"make sure to close down old tabs … they hog cpu and memory that other processes need\".\n   - Captain approved the share design direction (\"Yes this is godo, for the instagram- doing great\"). I treated it as design approval only, not authorization to land the branch.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling: `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, exact `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`, `fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N`, `fm-inbox.sh drain --ack`. Export `FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate`. Never top-level `cd` (persistent-cd hook denies it); use absolute paths.\n   - Delivery flow: `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M`, fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} with `python3 -I`, `fm-tasks-axi.sh add <id> '<title>' --kind ship`, `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> projects/<p> --mode M --yolo on --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh`, `fm-pr-merge.sh <id> <url>` (refuses red/unreported checks), `fm-teardown.sh <id>`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`, `fm-send.sh <task> [--resolve-key K] 'text'` (use a file + `$(cat)`), `fm-control.sh <id> exit`, `fm-reap.sh scan --act` (slow, ~2 min+), `fm-pr-check.sh <id> <url>` (re-arms merge watch).\n   - Project postures: fm-hooks (firstmate_hooks repo) is direct-PR +yolo; brain/forefront/forefront-backend are no-mistakes +yolo; barter is no-mistakes-prod-only +yolo; dotfiles and macbook-ops projects such as firstmate-share, talon-phone-asr and talon-palette-ios are local-only (land needs the captain's word). GitHub Actions fail ~2s because of account billing (captain-only fix at github.com/settings/billing).\n   - fm-hooks: harness hooks enqueue to ~/.fm-hooks/queue; worker/poller daemons (launchd com.fm-hooks.worker, com.fm-hooks.bead-poller) apply rules; failed/ holds 672 historical jobs. Retry/backoff is already on main (PR #4).\n   - Firstmate Share architecture: iOS Share Extension → tailnet receiver (launchd com.firstmateshare.receiver, 127.0.0.1:8770, tailscale https :8771, http :8774) → inbox bead with Ask line. Planned GET /config for top3, store list, and recent-share status.\n   - Talon-on-iPhone: phone sends Conformer/CoreML emissions, Mac swaps only Talon's model call (private test engine), live-engine install default OFF, EULA question open.\n   - Lavish pages: HTML in ~/fm_home/firstmate/.lavish/site/, listed in index.html, served at http://macbook:4380/.\n   - Quota: quota-axi, claude/fable window resets 2026-10-20T00:00Z.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/.lavish/site/firstmate-share-mockups.html: rewritten with Option D v2 (two boxes, top3 chips + \"More stores\" A–Z picker, inbox chip, preview, settings note, and the open question hint-vs-file-directly). Edited via python3 -I string replacement.\n   - data/fmh-retry-q1, fmh-flaky-q1, fmh-tmp-q1, fmh-cursor-q1 /brief.md: ship briefs for fm-hooks fixes (all filled with {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}).\n   - /private/tmp/claude-501/ms3.txt, ms4.txt, fbg.txt: fm-send message bodies (palette punctuation ask, tab cleanup ask, ci-1 billing decision).\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/.fm-hooks/queue/failed/*.json(+.error): 672 historical failed jobs; bead-action script at projects/fm-hooks/bin/fm-hooks-bead-action.ts (usage `ledger|project-comment|captain-hold|fleet|scout-report <operation> <correlationId> [ruleId]`; needs events/<corr>-<operation>.json).\n   - state/fb-green-q1.check.sh: was rejected as untrusted (mode 0600); re-armed by fm-pr-check.sh.\n   - Read earlier (unchanged): ~/.claude/settings.json, data/cd-violations/cdextract.py, state/inbox-store-watch.check.sh, ~/.local/bin/fm-nudge.\n   - Beads touched: task-iydgi (Share on-device check + all design comments), project-7u7w (punctuation ask), robots-vs2bv (closed), robots-lqep3 (closed), robots-yhvym (closed), robots-59gm1 (fix in PR 12), robots-8swcz (macbook-ops filed), robots-q4lpu (reaper relaunches stopped workers), a task for auto-reaping finished panes, a task for the Talon EULA/tailscale call, status-kdv (poke logs).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - persistent-cd denial on `cd` → used absolute paths / no top-level cd.\n   - fm-send doorbell skipped because of stray \"xx\" in macbook-ops composer → sent a direct herdr `send-text` + `enter` (ctrl-u is unsupported by herdr send-keys).\n   - mark-processed refused for seq 2137 (not a captain outcome) → ignored, ack succeeded.\n   - fm-reap scan timed out at 120s → ran in background; it later relaunched stopped workers fb-green-q1 and task-ho60f, undoing tab cleanup → filed robots-q4lpu.\n   - fm-control exit on task-ho60f failed (\"could not be sent\") → reported; tracked under robots-8swcz.\n   - The check.sh for fb-green-q1 was rejected as untrusted → re-registered via fm-pr-check.sh.\n   - Retry fix assumption was wrong: retry/backoff already existed (PR #4); the ship became a regression-test-only PR 9.\n   - status comments land under the pre-existing header \"Poke log 2026-10-18\" (cosmetic).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: hook failure diagnosis (transient, replay succeeds), flaky test (timeout under load), heartbeat tmp-file leak, Share design iteration, palette punctuation delegated and delivered, Talon phone emission proven on device, tab cleanup partially done.\n   - Ongoing: live Talon injection test (needs Mac unlocked); fb-green-q1/task-ho60f relaunched by the reaper (robots-q4lpu); GitHub billing blocks red PRs.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Repeated standing nudge text (pasted blocks, items 1–12), several times.\n   - \"http://macbook:4380/firstmate-share-mockups.html I wnt two inputs one is the orgiinal thign I am sharing , with any notes I want the other is the inbox bead that will talk about how to process it having the mini view of the sahre if it is an image or whatever is good too\"\n   - \"first box should have 3 common chips person brain task then have the 4th one be a alphabetized selector of any of the stores the 3 suggested stores should be configurable in the app as the hint ones, only one can be selected at a time the 2nd box is the inbox, it should have an inbox chip as well so that we can know it si for the inbox\"\n   - \"do we have a way to communicate back in ? or is this outbound only\"\n   - \"what about a config object that the tool can cehck on when it posts, and also has the option to manually refresh\"\n   - \"yeah, and the abiltiy to serve top 3, I could change the top 3 and leave the rest being a pciker\"\n   - \"Yes this is godo, for the instagram- doing great\"\n   - \"inside the talon `select the command` app thing , the input bx needs to strip out all punctuation pleas\"\n   - \"make sure to close down old tabs\"\n   - \"they hog cpu and memory that other processes need\"\n   - Automated system notifications (Stop-hook wakes, task notifications) are not user messages.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Immediately: merge firstmate_hooks PR 12 (robots-59gm1) via `fm-pr-merge.sh fmh-cursor-q1 https://github.com/trillium/firstmate_hooks/pull/12`, mark seq 2139 processed, ack with `--ack-through 318614 --recovery-generation 47074.1792443903.WaWOPb`, close robots-59gm1 with evidence, teardown fmh-cursor-q1, fleet-sync, log in status-kdv.\n   - Captain decisions pending:\n     - \"land it\" for fm/firstmate-share-build-20261019 (then dispatch the Option D build: two boxes, preview, GET /config with top3, Sent list, hint-vs-direct-file question).\n     - Land the palette punctuation branch (builds on unmerged fm/talon-palette-ota-20261019).\n     - Merge OK for trillium_talon PR 30 and the branch fm/talon-phone-mvp3-emission-20261019.\n     - Unlock the Mac screen for the live Talon test.\n     - Talon EULA call plus one new tailscale serve mapping.\n     - Land fm/dotfiles-nm-q1 (closes robots-lc225); other branches fm/dotfiles-codex-q1, fm/talon-phone-asr-spike1-20261019.\n     - GitHub billing fix (blocks forefront-backend PRs 4, 6, 7, Barter PRs); then merge those. Barter PR 2 should win over task-ho60f's attempt.\n     - File beads/dispatch cleanup for stuck clones (trilliumsmith.com 23 behind with uncommitted changes; forefront-backend); stop fb-green-q1/task-ho60f again (asked, no answer); consent to publish firstmate-repo fixes (robots-q22c, wajev, 8swcz, q4lpu); other earlier holds (iPhone unlock for task-4afnn, inbox-cglf deactivate target, review-store holds, credential rotations).\n   - Robots queue items remaining: q22c, 7iaq, wsv8a, ek6rg, sl1eq, lc225, wajev, 8swcz, q4lpu. Keep Sidecar and palette moving; overnight usability plan; idle design review.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Handling a Stop-hook wake after a poke. The drain just printed BRANCH OUTCOME seq 2139: \"fmh-cursor-q1: The fix for stray temp files in the hook cursor writers (robots-59gm1) is ready for review: both cursor writers and the deploy install now share one safe-replace and cleanup routine. 156 tests pass and the type check is clean. PR: https://github.com/trillium/firstmate_hooks/pull/12. I haven't run the PR check, so MAIN should confirm checks are green before merging.\" WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED printed: `--ack-through 318614 --recovery-generation 47074.1792443903.WaWOPb`. Nothing has been done on it yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the handling of this wake: run `fm-pr-merge.sh fmh-cursor-q1 https://github.com/trillium/firstmate_hooks/pull/12` (merge only if it verifies green), then `fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through 2139`, then `fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 318614 --recovery-generation 47074.1792443903.WaWOPb`, close robots-59gm1 with evidence, teardown fmh-cursor-q1, fleet-sync, and log to status-kdv. Do not land any local-only branch or merge trillium_talon PR 30 without the captain's explicit word.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"33dafcc2-56f6-4f86-9c96-780f7b83bfff","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:06:56.667Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":425,"turnIndex":839},"turnOrigin":"task_notification","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
