{"parentUuid":"34ef7535-b1fa-4457-be40-395b2a2ee116","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCHT95uEHkSY8Xy2BwVD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012QtQqRfRG89K9wVUkvgeea","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; robots show robots-sl1eq | sed -n 1,40p | cut -c1-300; $B/fm-project-mode.sh beads 2>&1|head -3; $B/fm-project-mode.sh --branch-prefix beads"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_read_input_tokens":91643,"output_tokens":271,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":104},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":271,"cache_read_input_tokens":91643,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012QtQqRfRG89K9wVUkvgeea":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; robots show robots-sl1eq | sed -n 1,40p | cut -c1-300; $B/fm-project-mode.sh beads 2>&1|head -3; $B/fm-project-mode.sh --branch-prefix beads"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCHT8rVsSUtFSNeLLQV2","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8d99f0f-534f-4991-9ec0-4ca6e8aea9ea","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:12:13.465Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"e8d99f0f-534f-4991-9ec0-4ca6e8aea9ea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93187c72-b46f-468f-ae8a-aabe6a535219","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012QtQqRfRG89K9wVUkvgeea","type":"tool_result","content":"○ robots-sl1eq · bd in a fresh git dir with no .beads resolves to a foreign-home store and creates beads there (scout repro of robots-4ayi4)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: bd-in-a-fresh-git-dir-with-no-beads-resolves-to-a-foreign-home-store-and-creates-beads-there-scout-repro-of-robots-4ayi4\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 10:28 Trillium Smith\n    \n      firstmate: dispatching diagnosis scout bd-store-resolution-scout-q1 (brain  \n      project, read-only); report data/bd-store-resolution-scout-q1/report.md.    \n  2026-10-19 10:35 Trillium Smith\n    \n      # bd store-resolution scout (robots-gbu6f, robots-sl1eq)                    \n                                                                                  \n      **Verdict:** Both defects reproduce, and they share one root cause: client- \n      mode forwarding in brain runs before any BEADS_DIR logic and depends only on\n      $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. gbu6f (BEADS_DIR ignored) is a one-guard   \n      fix. sl1eq (foreign store absorbs writes) needs a design call on what bare  \n      brain means in client mode.                                                 \n                                                                                  \n      Workaround today: BRAIN_REMOTE=off <command> runs locally and honors        \n      BEADS_DIR.                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n      ## What I did                                                               \n                                                                                  \n      • Read-only diagnosis. Nothing in the live stores or the shared Dolt server \n      (127.0.0.1:3307) was touched.                                               \n      • Built a throwaway sandbox under the scratchpad (bd-sandbox/) with an      \n      overridden HOME (bd-sandbox/realhome), so ~/.config/brain/remote.yaml and   \n      ~/data/brain live only in the sandbox.                                      \n      • Used the installed binary ~/.local/bin/bd.real (bd version 1.1.0-rc.1+    \n      brain.0.5.1 (3a63e7914)), with env -i so no live env leaked in.             \n      • Replaced the ssh transport with a fake (BRAIN_REMOTE_SSH pointing at a    \n      script that appends argv to a log and exits 0). It never connects.          \n      • Read the source in this worktree (HEAD 24ea97b25).                        \ndirect-PR off\nfm/","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e361d7f3-6329-4cb1-85d0-7d6c6d420626","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:12:14.565Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"○ robots-sl1eq · bd in a fresh git dir with no .beads resolves to a foreign-home store and creates beads there (scout repro of robots-4ayi4)   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  (none)\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: bd-in-a-fresh-git-dir-with-no-beads-resolves-to-a-foreign-home-store-and-creates-beads-there-scout-repro-of-robots-4ayi4\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 10:28 Trillium Smith\n    \n      firstmate: dispatching diagnosis scout bd-store-resolution-scout-q1 (brain  \n      project, read-only); report data/bd-store-resolution-scout-q1/report.md.    \n  2026-10-19 10:35 Trillium Smith\n    \n      # bd store-resolution scout (robots-gbu6f, robots-sl1eq)                    \n                                                                                  \n      **Verdict:** Both defects reproduce, and they share one root cause: client- \n      mode forwarding in brain runs before any BEADS_DIR logic and depends only on\n      $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. gbu6f (BEADS_DIR ignored) is a one-guard   \n      fix. sl1eq (foreign store absorbs writes) needs a design call on what bare  \n      brain means in client mode.                                                 \n                                                                                  \n      Workaround today: BRAIN_REMOTE=off <command> runs locally and honors        \n      BEADS_DIR.                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n      ## What I did                                                               \n                                                                                  \n      • Read-only diagnosis. Nothing in the live stores or the shared Dolt server \n      (127.0.0.1:3307) was touched.                                               \n      • Built a throwaway sandbox under the scratchpad (bd-sandbox/) with an      \n      overridden HOME (bd-sandbox/realhome), so ~/.config/brain/remote.yaml and   \n      ~/data/brain live only in the sandbox.                                      \n      • Used the installed binary ~/.local/bin/bd.real (bd version 1.1.0-rc.1+    \n      brain.0.5.1 (3a63e7914)), with env -i so no live env leaked in.             \n      • Replaced the ssh transport with a fake (BRAIN_REMOTE_SSH pointing at a    \n      script that appends argv to a log and exits 0). It never connects.          \n      • Read the source in this worktree (HEAD 24ea97b25).                        \ndirect-PR off\nfm/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e8d99f0f-534f-4991-9ec0-4ca6e8aea9ea","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
