{"parentUuid":"76ba3ec1-a1e6-47ac-aa93-b91b91a1d611","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCHTaQAAYi98JGJFz4B5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017uhNBzc28SPF4rP4NhT9qB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; robots show robots-gbu6f | sed -n 1,6p | cut -c1-250; sed -n 40,80p <(robots show robots-sl1eq) | cut -c1-200; $B/fm-project-mode.sh brain; $B/fm-project-mode.sh --branch-prefix brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1213,"cache_read_input_tokens":95033,"output_tokens":254,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":64},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":95033,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017uhNBzc28SPF4rP4NhT9qB":{"command":"export FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate; B=$FM_HOME/bin; robots show robots-gbu6f | sed -n 1,6p | cut -c1-250; sed -n 40,80p <(robots show robots-sl1eq) | cut -c1-200; $B/fm-project-mode.sh brain; $B/fm-project-mode.sh --branch-prefix brain"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCHTaAGmfsNijauRJBYH","type":"assistant","uuid":"63208d10-88f7-4453-9fbc-1f7891074ca3","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:12:17.046Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"63208d10-88f7-4453-9fbc-1f7891074ca3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93187c72-b46f-468f-ae8a-aabe6a535219","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uhNBzc28SPF4rP4NhT9qB","type":"tool_result","content":"✓ robots-gbu6f · bd ignores BEADS_DIR when HOME points at the real home: store resolves to ~/data/brain   [● P2 · CLOSED]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\nClose reason: Fixed by merged brain PR 45 https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45\n\nDESCRIPTION\n      • Read the source in this worktree (HEAD 24ea97b25).                        \n                                                                                  \n      ## Resolution order (as the code runs)                                      \n                                                                                  \n      cmd/bd/main.go startup, in order:                                           \n                                                                                  \n      1. hostGateEarly(os.Args[1:]) (main.go near 1628).                          \n      2. maybeForwardRemote(os.Args[1:]) at cmd/bd/main.go:1632. If it returns    \n      handled, bd exits here. **No **BEADS_DIR** check happens before this point. \n      **                                                                          \n      3. Only if not forwarded: BD_NAME, then loadEnvironment → beads.            \n      FindBeadsDir().                                                             \n                                                                                  \n      maybeForwardRemote → remoteForwardingActive (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:254-    \n      282):                                                                       \n                                                                                  \n      • :255 BRAIN_REMOTE=off disables forwarding. This is the only escape.       \n      • :258 name comes from BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE (set by store wrappers); empty    \n      means brain.                                                                \n      • :264 loadRemoteConfig() (:132-147) reads remoteConfigFile() (:83-89),     \n      which is $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. **This is the HOME dependency.**  \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_HOST can override the host.                                    \n      • :268 cfg.Host == \"\" means not a client. Any non-empty host means forward. \n                                                                                  \n      brain_remote.go contains zero references to BEADS_DIR (grep -c BEADS_DIR    \n      returned 0). The remote script (:179-181) sets PATH, BRAIN_REMOTE=off,      \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1 and execs the host's wrapper with the store name.  \n      Neither the client's BEADS_DIR nor its cwd is sent.                         \n                                                                                  \n      For comparison, the local resolver internal/beads/beads.go:689              \n      (FindBeadsDir) honors BEADS_DIR at step 1 (:690). It is never reached when  \n      forwarding is active.                                                       \n                                                                                  \n      ## Evidence                                                                 \n                                                                                  \n      ### gbu6f: BEADS_DIR bypassed when remote.yaml is under HOME                \n                                                                                  \n      Fixture: realhome/.config/brain/remote.yaml with host: fake-brain-          \n      host.invalid. Explicit store at explicit/store/.beads.                      \n                                                                                  \n      G1 (bug): env -i HOME=realhome BEADS_DIR=explicit/store/.beads              \nno-mistakes on\nfm/","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"112e7c2c-f6d8-47b9-bf82-963b0469b81b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:12:18.978Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"✓ robots-gbu6f · bd ignores BEADS_DIR when HOME points at the real home: store resolves to ~/data/brain   [● P2 · CLOSED]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-19 · Updated: 2026-10-19\nClose reason: Fixed by merged brain PR 45 https://github.com/trillium/brain/pull/45\n\nDESCRIPTION\n      • Read the source in this worktree (HEAD 24ea97b25).                        \n                                                                                  \n      ## Resolution order (as the code runs)                                      \n                                                                                  \n      cmd/bd/main.go startup, in order:                                           \n                                                                                  \n      1. hostGateEarly(os.Args[1:]) (main.go near 1628).                          \n      2. maybeForwardRemote(os.Args[1:]) at cmd/bd/main.go:1632. If it returns    \n      handled, bd exits here. **No **BEADS_DIR** check happens before this point. \n      **                                                                          \n      3. Only if not forwarded: BD_NAME, then loadEnvironment → beads.            \n      FindBeadsDir().                                                             \n                                                                                  \n      maybeForwardRemote → remoteForwardingActive (cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:254-    \n      282):                                                                       \n                                                                                  \n      • :255 BRAIN_REMOTE=off disables forwarding. This is the only escape.       \n      • :258 name comes from BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE (set by store wrappers); empty    \n      means brain.                                                                \n      • :264 loadRemoteConfig() (:132-147) reads remoteConfigFile() (:83-89),     \n      which is $HOME/.config/brain/remote.yaml. **This is the HOME dependency.**  \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_HOST can override the host.                                    \n      • :268 cfg.Host == \"\" means not a client. Any non-empty host means forward. \n                                                                                  \n      brain_remote.go contains zero references to BEADS_DIR (grep -c BEADS_DIR    \n      returned 0). The remote script (:179-181) sets PATH, BRAIN_REMOTE=off,      \n      BRAIN_REMOTE_FORWARDED=1 and execs the host's wrapper with the store name.  \n      Neither the client's BEADS_DIR nor its cwd is sent.                         \n                                                                                  \n      For comparison, the local resolver internal/beads/beads.go:689              \n      (FindBeadsDir) honors BEADS_DIR at step 1 (:690). It is never reached when  \n      forwarding is active.                                                       \n                                                                                  \n      ## Evidence                                                                 \n                                                                                  \n      ### gbu6f: BEADS_DIR bypassed when remote.yaml is under HOME                \n                                                                                  \n      Fixture: realhome/.config/brain/remote.yaml with host: fake-brain-          \n      host.invalid. Explicit store at explicit/store/.beads.                      \n                                                                                  \n      G1 (bug): env -i HOME=realhome BEADS_DIR=explicit/store/.beads              \nno-mistakes on\nfm/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"so