{"parentUuid":"6915968d-0406-48b4-a6b6-a58d0200f0a5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"48402863-6427-4cbb-9150-848968a7e965","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n      PRODUCT SPEC (captain 2026-10-17) Q1: single user holds control; they have  \n      multiple screens in their viewing space and Sidecar serves useful info on   \n      them automatically, without fuss (zero-config). Q2: a device that joins with\n      no pane assigned displays its own status, sizing and config info (self-     \n      describing default pane).                                                   \n  2026-10-17 09:24 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Product answers (single user zero-config; unassigned-device pane) landed on \n      sidecar local main fcca1ae; make check green; worker torn down.             \n  2026-10-17 09:27 Trillium Smith\n    \n      PRODUCT SPEC Q3-Q9 (captain 2026-10-17) - EVERYTHING IS V1, OVERNIGHT BUILD \n      Q3 \"Drive a pane\": Sidecar serves visual UI on a pane by switching a        \n      predetermined MODE. A pane can swap its view into any of a WHITELISTED set  \n      of apps via a CLI command or API call. Architecture: server -> UI system;   \n      server sends COMMAND; UI system changes view to the command. Target format: \n      frame-within-a-frame (the UI is a wrapper/shell that embeds dedicated       \n      services we can display).                                                   \n      Q5 CLI feel: something like herdr.                                          \n      Q6 API: reachable over the tailnet; ALSO an exposed MCP server. Tools       \n      register to use it (e.g. fm_hooks actions become one of the user            \n      interfaces).                                                                \n      Q7 Writes: YES in v1 (supersedes scope.md \"writes later\"). A UI option the  \n      user selects must have a real effect in the user computer/agent layers, and \n      Sidecar must route the response intelligently (e.g. user answering a request\n      that came from herdr workspace 1 pane 3 -> response routes back there).     \n      Needs origin/reply-route tracking per request. Write path is explicit and   \n      authorised by this decision; keep guards (auth, bounded payloads, no loops).\n      Q8 Done: any device can enroll as a UI display and serve data; the system   \n      advertises which UIs are available with capabilities (touch or not).        \n      Q9: nothing deferred; all of it is v1.                                      \n      SUCCESS TEST: load two different browsers; two different UIs; both          \n      programmatically driven (CLI/API) to shift display content.                 \n  2026-10-17 09:29 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Overnight build started (msg 347). Stage 1: worker sidecar-core-20261017    \n      doing scope.md update, docs/api.md contract, Go core + serve + embedded     \n      browser UI shell. Stage 2 (parallel): CLI, MCP server, second UI,           \n      enroll/advertise polish. Stage 3: two-browser/two-UI success test with      \n      recorded evidence.                                                          \n  2026-10-17 10:03 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Overnight progress: stage 1 core (HTTP API, registry, bus, router,          \n      whitelist, embedded shell; docs/api.md contract) landed 9518d89; CLI landed \n      6894b63. MCP server and UI variants in progress; then two-browser success   \n      test with evidence.                                                         \n  2026-10-17 10:12 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Stage 2a: MCP server (internal/mcp, docs/mcp.md, 'sidecar mcp') landed on   \n      local main, make check green. UI branch still building; stage 3 two-browser \n      test next.                                                                  \n  2026-10-17 10:16 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Stage 2b: UI (shell variants glance/panel/full; apps                        \n      clock/status/ask/feed/devices) landed local main 03657bc, make check green. \n      Stage 3 two-browser e2e worker started.                                     \n  2026-10-17 10:28 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Stage 3 DONE: two-browser e2e (make e2e, test/e2e, zero-dep Go CDP driving  \n      two headless Chrome UIs) landed 728a522. Verified: per-pane app switching,  \n      ask/reply routed to correct pane only, unknown pane exit 3, /v1/uis matches \n      browsers. Evidence data/sidecar-e2e-20261017/evidence.txt. Next: review     \n      docs, optional remote/publish (MIT, local-only for now).                    \n  2026-10-17 10:49 Trillium Smith\n    \n      2026-10-17 macbook-ops: Sidecar v1 built overnight - core+CLI+MCP+UI+two-   \n      browser e2e on local main 728a522, make check + make e2e green, two headless\n      Chrome UIs driven via CLI/API. Next: verify evidence myself, then enrol-    \n      from-another-device test.                                                   \n  2026-10-17 10:52 Trillium Smith\n(eval):1: ===== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MFFcz1xcWq33C9kzakvgai"}]},"uuid":"1ad528bb-c403-413c-9826-7dc9ac669249","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:24:47.988Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n      PRODUCT SPEC (captain 2026-10-17) Q1: single user holds control; they have  \n      multiple screens in their viewing space and Sidecar serves useful info on   \n      them automatically, without fuss (zero-config). Q2: a device that joins with\n      no pane assigned displays its own status, sizing and config info (self-     \n      describing default pane).                                                   \n  2026-10-17 09:24 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Product answers (single user zero-config; unassigned-device pane) landed on \n      sidecar local main fcca1ae; make check green; worker torn down.             \n  2026-10-17 09:27 Trillium Smith\n    \n      PRODUCT SPEC Q3-Q9 (captain 2026-10-17) - EVERYTHING IS V1, OVERNIGHT B