{"parentUuid":"8f276f07-fa6a-4b73-8227-785003aff22c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"48402863-6427-4cbb-9150-848968a7e965","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BXDdeMW3UgYZ99eBXmptJ3","type":"tool_result","content":"  2026-10-18 05:51 Trillium Smith\n    \n      2026-10-17 poke: QR slice landed, errors fix-guide worker (task-u6ul8)      \n      running; open: phone scan, Chrome check task-7mfok. No new dispatch needed. \n  2026-10-18 06:52 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Poke: routed macbook-ops to redeploy live console with 8fb37a5 fix-guide    \n      errors (still old binary on :8791).                                         \n  2026-10-18 07:09 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Captain 2026-10-18 (verbatim): I really want to explore how to make sidecar \n      a fully functional control surface via talon too - iphone is a talon route  \n      controller, sidecar UI is hosted on macbook, iphone interacts with visuals  \n      from a sidecar pane anywhere out in the world (see task-7txy4)              \n  2026-10-18 20:06 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Captain 2026-10-18: Sidecar needs a way to force light/dark theme per       \n      pane/device. Fire TV is in light theme; captain prefers dark. Pages follow  \n      prefers-color-scheme, which the TV browser reports as light, so Sidecar     \n      needs an override (per-pane setting, driveable by agent via drive_pane/API).\n  2026-10-19 02:45 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Captain 2026-10-19 (verbatim): sidecar - shows qr code on non tailbet       \n      devices that has a qr code that has the token to the tailnet site so only   \n      tailnet devices authenticate. (Design: public Funnel :10000 page for an     \n      unauthenticated device shows a pairing QR; scanning it from a tailnet device\n      opens a tailnet-only approve URL, which authorizes that public session. Only\n      tailnet devices can mint access.)                                           \n  2026-10-19 03:09 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Captain 2026-10-19: no Funnel, vps01 as proxy -> task-k2354                 \n  2026-10-19 05:54 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Dedicated status bead: status-vkr (append-only; newest entry at bottom).    \n      Read it first for current Sidecar state.                                    \n  2026-10-19 06:03 Trillium Smith\n    \n      Promoted to foreground 2026-10-19T06:03:47.585Z — capture inbox-90re in     \n      inbox                                                                       \n\n\n○ project-lp7s [EPIC] · Firstmate hooks to beads — hooks own all bead lifecycle   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: epic\nCreated: 2026-10-11 · Updated: 2026-10-11\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  Hooks, not agents or firstmate, handle every bead interaction. Principle:   \n  any loop of captain -> beads -> agent -> beads is done by hooks with no     \n  manual bead steps. Requirements are child beads.                            \n\n\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: firstmate-hooks-to-beads-hooks-own-all-bead-lifecycle\n\nCHILDREN\n  ↳ ○ project-lp7s.2: REQ2: Agent-to-firstmate messages/reports are copied into beads by hook ● P2\n  ↳ ○ project-lp7s.3: REQ3: Needs-direction asks auto-filed to review store; decisions auto-notified back ● P2\n  ↳ ○ project-lp7s.1: REQ1: Spawn hook turns brief into a task bead claimed by the agent ● P2\n  ◐ 0/3 complete (0%)\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-11 02:11 Trillium Smith\n    \n      CONSTRAINT (captain): all of this must be achievable entirely via hooks,    \n      without editing any Firstmate code directly.                                \n  2026-10-11 08:08 Trillium Smith\n    \n      2026-10-11 macbook project audit: ~/code/firstmate: active, last activity   \n      2026-10-03 (7d); readiness READY (e.g. task-n4l9 \"Evaluate readiness of     \n○ project-73bi.5 · fm-hooks (firstmate_hooks) — add MIT LICENSE, tests, live view   [● P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: Trillium Smith · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-10-17 · Updated: 2026-10-17\n\nDESCRIPTION\