g was enabled. No vps01 file was edited. No Funnel was     \n      touched. This report holds no secret.                                       \n                                                                                  \n      ## 0. Bottom line                                                           \n                                                                                  \n\n\n\nLABELS: project:sidecar, sidecar-status\n\nMETADATA\n  brain_slug: sidecar-status-current-state-access-paths-open-items-append-only\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-10-19 06:06 Trillium Smith\n    \n      2026-10-19: sidecar.trilliumsmith.com serves the personal Vercel site only  \n      via wildcard DNS (*.trilliumsmith.com); name is free. Explicit A record to  \n      vps01 would override it. Still gated on review-jtwo. Answered in inbox-90re.\n  2026-10-19 06:07 Trillium Smith\n    \n      == 2026-10-19 (entry 2, captain) ==                                         \n      Captain approved review-jtwo (public exposure) after reading inbox-90re.    \n      inbox-90re closed with answer: Next.js site is personal portfolio on Vercel \n      via *.trilliumsmith.com wildcard; sidecar. name is free. Plan: explicit A   \n      record sidecar. -> vps01 overrides wildcard only; Caddy vhost proxies to    \n      tailnet macbook:8792; QR pairing stays as auth. Task filed for the DNS +    \n      Caddy write step. No live changes made from this chat yet.                  \n  2026-10-19 06:13 Trillium Smith\n    \n      2026-10-19: PUBLIC LIVE at https://sidecar.trilliumsmith.com (A record ->   \n      vps01 198.12.123.41 + Caddy vhost, by macbook-ops). Firstmate verified via  \n      1.1.1.1 / --resolve: healthz 200, /v1/devices 401, /pair 404. Some local    \n      resolvers still cache the old wildcard (Vercel) for a while.                \n\nbehavioral-hooks\nfm-hooks\n8c510e0 Remove a cursor's or rules file's temporary on any failed write and sweep dead writers' temporaries on every wri\nc660db3 Remove a heartbeat's temporary on any failed write and sweep dead writers' temporaries on every beat (robots-yhv\nd1367ec Give the pipeline end-to-end tests a budget sized to their process count (robots-lqep3) (#10)\n52f1d58 Pin the exit-1 retry path with resident-worker tests and report retried in status (robots-vs2bv) (#9)\ndee6f57 Capture a scout's report on any done-line stamp, and from the status tail (robots-fkb70) (#8)\n76094dc Ledger failure rule fires only when the ledger call itself demonstrably failed (#7)\n101d8bb Test: the ledger failure rule ignores a refused chain that never reached fm-fleet-ledger.sh (#6)\na5c9d02 Detect fm-* calls inside bash -c scripts and record every ship a spawn loop dispatched (robots-znjpz) (#5)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6bf4bc78-331e-4747-90af-8534812fc17b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
