{"parentUuid":"03417883-c424-48d7-bdc4-3e79916b719f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCJTLWbJgPSb6vHuSMM1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":115389,"output_tokens":1054,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":783,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":115389,"cache_creation_input_tokens":783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":783},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":449,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgCJTL9X64zmhYfhtqdRN","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2ff5804-ede2-40ea-8fa9-b82e247396e6","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:25:19.781Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"c2ff5804-ede2-40ea-8fa9-b82e247396e6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCJTLWbJgPSb6vHuSMM1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, exposing either name puts a public listener in front of your tailnet, so the main risk is that anyone on the internet can reach it and probe it. I'm going from the architecture in the plan (Caddy on vps01 proxying over the tailnet to the Mac, with `--require-auth` and QR pairing). I haven't re-audited the live config for this answer.\n\n**Sidecar domain (`sidecar.trilliumsmith.com`)**\n1. **Auth bypass or token theft.** QR pairing is the only gate. A stolen session token or approve URL gives full control of your panes, and Sidecar can write back (reply routing, `drive_pane`). Pairing links should be single-use, short-lived and bound to the session.\n2. **Pairing abuse.** Anyone can load the page and generate pairing QRs, so an attacker can try to trick you into approving theirs. That's social engineering, and it only works if the approve screen doesn't show what you're approving.\n3. **Brute force and DoS.** Public endpoints invite token guessing, request floods and long-lived stream connections. These need rate limits, and the proxy's pass-through to the Mac must be limited to the Sidecar upstream only.\n4. **Content and data exposure.** Panes can show agent output, review beads and decisions. A paired session sees all of it, so a leaked token also leaks that content.\n5. **Software bugs.** Any vulnerability in the Go server (parsing, path handling, the MCP endpoint) is reachable by strangers. Only keep the routes you need public.\n\n**Any exposed vps01 hostname**\n1. **vps01 is now an attack target.** It's on your tailnet (100.83.91.96), so a compromised vps01 is a foothold into everything that node can reach. Its tailnet ACL should allow only the Sidecar port on the Mac.\n2. **Admin surfaces.** SSH, Caddy's admin API, and any other service on that box become discoverable. Exposing `vps01.trilliumsmith.com` itself also reveals the real IP (198.12.123.41) and invites scanning of everything on it.\n3. **TLS and DNS.** The wildcard `*.trilliumsmith.com` pointing at Vercel means a mistake or hijack of DNS records can send traffic, and certificates, somewhere you don't control. A subdomain takeover is the classic failure here.\n4. **Logs.** Proxy logs on vps01 will hold IPs and request paths, and pairing tokens if they ride in URLs. Tokens should go in POST bodies or headers instead.\n\n**Mitigations already in place or planned:** Funnel is off, only the Sidecar upstream is proxied, and auth is required. I observed `/v1/devices` returning 401 and `/pair` returning 404 on the public name.\n\n**Note:** I haven't verified rate limiting, pairing-token expiry, or the vps01 tailnet ACL, and those are the three I'd check first.\n\nWant me to dispatch a scout to audit exactly those three on the live setup?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":115389,"output_tokens":1054,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":783,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":115389,"cache_creation_input_tokens":783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":783},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCJTL9X64zmhYfhtqdRN","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1484be4-464a-4405-8d8b-b7d200e85444","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:25:27.731Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-