{"parentUuid":"7488bd12-9a1f-42bd-8cea-35a4fef8741f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3afa7b96-9b37-424c-9da2-d7cc23a910ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pitc4DQMs75aVDXu4WGhzn","type":"tool_result","content":"## Recommended fixes\n\n**gbu6f (ship-ready, one guard):** in `remoteForwardingActive` (`cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:254`), before `loadRemoteConfig`, return inactive when `BEADS_DIR` is set and `hasBeadsProjectFiles(canonical BEADS_DIR)` is true locally. An explicit local store then wins over the client config.\n\n- Tradeoff: store wrappers on a thin client set `BEADS_DIR=$HOME/data/<store>/.beads`, which usually does not exist locally, so they still forward. A client that also has a local copy at that path would silently go local. Decide whether that is acceptable.\n\n**sl1eq (design decision needed):** a bare `brain` on a client forwards to the host's default store. Narrow fix: in client mode, refuse mutating verbs (`create`, `update`, `close`, `delete`, `import`) when no `BEADS_DIR` is set and no `.beads` workspace is found from cwd. Fail with `no beads workspace here; set BEADS_DIR or BRAIN_REMOTE=off`. Read verbs keep forwarding. This never writes outside an explicit `BEADS_DIR` or the cwd workspace.\n\n- Open question: is bare `brain` in client mode meant to write to the host's default store? If yes, the fix is to make that explicit (wrapper-only), not implicit.\n\n## Not done","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7d4e8821-211e-4055-a48a-392006c1040d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:40:45.469Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Recommended fixes\n\n**gbu6f (ship-ready, one guard):** in `remoteForwardingActive` (`cmd/bd/brain_remote.go:254`), before `loadRemoteConfig`, return inactive when `BEADS_DIR` is set and `hasBeadsProjectFiles(canonical BEADS_DIR)` is true locally. An explicit local store then wins over the client config.\n\n- Tradeoff: store wrappers on a thin client set `BEADS_DIR=$HOME/data/<store>/.beads`, which usually does not exist locally, so they still forward. A client that also has a local copy at that path would silently go local. Decide whether that is acceptable.\n\n**sl1eq (design decision needed):** a bare `brain` on a client forwards to the host's default store. Narrow fix: in client mode, refuse mutating verbs (`create`, `update`, `close`, `delete`, `import`) when no `BEADS_DIR` is set and no `.beads` workspace is found from cwd. Fail with `no beads workspace here; set BEADS_DIR or BRAIN_REMOTE=off`. Read verbs keep forwarding. This never writes outside an explicit `BEADS_DIR` or the cwd workspace.\n\n- Open question: is bare `brain` in client mode meant to write to the host's default store? If yes, the fix is to make that explicit (wrapper-only), not implicit.\n\n## Not done","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7488bd12-9a1f-42bd-8cea-35a4fef8741f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
