{"parentUuid":"b18b73fe-7077-466d-8765-4a9ab12d88d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCLaxDNNdSdjFREip8LX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, I dispatched a second fix this round and I'm waiting on both.\n\n**Robots queue**\n- **`robots-wsv8a`** (`parlay listen` timing out on register-agent): I couldn't reproduce it. The relay on port 4242 is healthy, and three direct register-agent calls each answered in under 50ms, so the failure looks transient. I did not close it. I dispatched `parlay-listen-q1`, a Fable ship in parlay, to add a bounded retry and a clearer error that says whether the server is slow or unreachable.\n- **`robots-sl1eq`** (bare `bd` writing to a foreign store): still working in `brain-sl1eq-q1` from last round.\n\n**Usage:** Claude has 32% left (Fable 21%) with about 2 hours until the 23:59 reset. That is underspent. I have no more safe work to send, because the remaining ready items either need your consent or a credential. I logged the numbers in `status-kdv`.\n\n**What I need from you**\n1. Approve publishing the firstmate fixes (`robots-q22c`, `robots-d8dvl`) so I can dispatch them on Fable.\n2. Give me the MiniMax key or login so pi can take MIT OSS work.\n3. Approve the `tailscale serve` mapping and make the Talon EULA call.\n4. Fix GitHub billing, and say \"land it\" for the Share build branch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_read_input_tokens":137952,"output_tokens":466,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":137952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_crea