{"parentUuid":"44a7836a-4f8f-4941-b514-3bb4dbc0fe62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCMQuyX6e7YwCGzVGMuK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014xbWG8QZxHqrQUhxbKFPLk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /private/tmp/claude-501/rb.txt <<'EOF'\nPURPOSE: every run, a Fable agent audits the captain's development work over the last 24h, finds what slowed velocity, and proposes concrete improvements. Output is a report plus filed beads, not code changes. Trigger: captain asks, or daily. Executor: Fable (claude --model fable, effort xhigh) as a SCOUT (read-only, no PR). Firstmate spawns it; the scout never addresses the captain.\n\nSTATUS: DRAFT, not yet run. Mark steps VERIFIED after a first run.\n\nINPUTS (window = now-24h .. now; state the exact UTC window in the report)\n- Work done: git log --since='24 hours ago' across every project under ~/fm_home/firstmate/projects/ and other homes (macbook-ops, mini0-ops) via git -C <dir> (never cd).\n- Fleet throughput: tasks closed/opened (task list, tasks-axi), PRs opened/merged/closed (gh-axi), data/backlog.md Done section, state/*.status event lines with [at=<epoch>].\n- Time sinks: lifespan store (session ledger), status-kdv poke logs, wake queue/inbox history, robots + violations beads created in the window.\n- Capacity: quota-axi (window remaining vs time), idle vs busy agents.\n- Raw sessions only if a lead needs evidence: ~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl.\n\nSTEPS\n1. Fix the window and list active projects (those with commits, PRs or closed tasks in it). Checkpoint: written window + project list.\n2. Build the timeline: per project, what shipped (merged PRs, landed branches) vs what stalled (done-but-not-landed, blocked, held). Checkpoint: table of shipped vs stalled with ids and full PR URLs.\n3. Measure waits, in hours: time from worker-done to merge; time items sat waiting on a captain decision (open decisions, review/human beads); CI failures and cause (e.g. billing); reaper relaunches; tool defects hit (robots beads). Checkpoint: each wait has a number and a source.\n4. Rank bottlenecks by hours lost, then by recurrence. For each: evidence, root cause, who/what is the constraint (captain decision, tooling defect, capacity, process). Do not guess: label unproven causes as hypotheses.\n5. Propose improvements, max 7, each with expected hours saved, smallest first step, owner store (task/ideas/robots/decisions), and whether it needs the captain's consent (publish, destructive, billing). Prefer removing a wait over adding machinery.\n6. File beads: one task or idea per accepted-shaped proposal in the right store; defects in robots. Checkpoint: list of created ids.\n7. Write report to data/<task-id>/report.md (top: 5-line summary: velocity numbers, top 3 bottlenecks, top 3 fixes). Attach the full report to a brain bead and comment the bead id on the originating task/inbox bead.\n\nFAILURE BRANCHES\n- A source store or CLI is unavailable: record the gap in the report and continue; absence is a finding, bounded by what was searched.\n- Window has little activity: say so, widen to 72h once, state it.\n- Never inflate: counts show activity, not impact. No code, config, or bead-closing changes during the audit.\n\nVERIFICATION: report states window, sources read, numbers with sources, and every proposal has a filed bead id.\nEOF\nrunbooks create \"Runbook: 24h dev-work audit - bottlenecks and improvements (run by Fable)\" 2>&1 | grep -oE 'runbooks-[a-z0-9]+' | head -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":150293,"output_tokens":1488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":190},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":286,"ephemeral_5m_input_tok