\n3. Measure waits, in hours: time from worker-done to merge; time items sat waiting on a captain decision (open decisions, review/human beads); CI failures and cause (e.g. billing); reaper relaunches; tool defects hit (robots beads). Checkpoint: each wait has a number and a source.\n4. Rank bottlenecks by hours lost, then by recurrence. For each: evidence, root cause, who/what is the constraint (captain decision, tooling defect, capacity, process). Do not guess: label unproven causes as hypotheses.\n5. Propose improvements, max 7, each with expected hours saved, smallest first step, owner store (task/ideas/robots/decisions), and whether it needs the captain's consent (publish, destructive, billing). Prefer removing a wait over adding machinery.\n6. File beads: one task or idea per accepted-shaped proposal in the right store; defects in robots. Checkpoint: list of created ids.\n7. Write report to data/<task-id>/report.md (top: 5-line summary: velocity numbers, top 3 bottlenecks, top 3 fixes). Attach the full report to a brain bead and comment the bead id on the originating task/inbox bead.\n\nFAILURE BRANCHES\n- A source store or CLI is unavailable: record the gap in the report and continue; absence is a finding, bounded by what was searched.\n- Window has little activity: say so, widen to 72h once, state it.\n- Never inflate: counts show activity, not impact. No code, config, or bead-closing changes during the audit.\n\nVERIFICATION: report states window, sources read, numbers with sources, and every proposal has a filed bead id.\nEOF\nrunbooks create \"Runbook: 24h dev-work audit - bottlenecks and improvements (run by Fable)\" 2>&1 | grep -oE 'runbooks-[a-z0-9]+' | head -1"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCMQuidWMdqbyG7fwfr1","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd455e7c-c054-4bff-ac29-827ed85c5eae","timestamp":"2026-10-19T22:04:20.497Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint