{"parentUuid":"dc75e10d-2c71-4b1f-9b6b-229c5974e273","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCMSgK2x864tgZYVvrWt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done: the runbook is `runbooks-86h`, \"24h dev-work audit - bottlenecks and improvements (run by Fable)\". It's tagged `project:firstmate`. I wrote it as a draft and haven't run it yet.\n\nFable runs it as a read-only scout on Claude with `--model fable --effort xhigh`. It produces a report and filed beads, with no code changes.\n\n**Steps**\n1. Fix the 24-hour window and list the active projects.\n2. Build a timeline of what shipped versus what stalled, per project.\n3. Measure the waits in hours: done to merge, waiting on your decisions, CI failures, reaper relaunches, tool defects.\n4. Rank the bottlenecks by hours lost and by how often they recur. Unproven causes get labeled as hypotheses.\n5. Propose at most 7 improvements. Each gets an expected time saved, a smallest first step, the store it belongs in, and whether it needs your consent.\n6. File a bead for each proposal.\n7. Write the report with a 5-line summary on top, attach it to a brain bead, and link that bead from the originating task.\n\nThe runbook also covers failure cases: a missing data source is recorded as a gap, a quiet window is widened to 72 hours once, and the audit never changes code, config, or beads. Wall-clock data comes from git history, the PR and task stores, status events, the session ledger, `quota-axi`, and the robots and violations beads.\n\nWant me to run it now on Fable? Claude's window resets at 23:59 and is underspent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":152103,"output_tokens":509,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creat