{"parentUuid":"589c8ae0-ca29-448b-b67a-39b1c62556a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCMmAvjXLsKVaCzjeB2J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, the bare-`bd` fix (`robots-sl1eq`) hit a review checkpoint with three findings, and I decided all three. The worker has my answers and is continuing. Its PR isn't up yet, so nothing is merged.\n\n1. **Fix: a hole in the refusal.** It was skipped whenever `BEADS_DIR` was set, even when that folder wasn't a real store. A bare write could still land in the host's default store, which is the bug itself. The worker is closing that gap and correcting the test that locked in the wrong assumption.\n2. **Skip: widening the list of refused commands.** `q`, `comment`, `label`, `dep`, `edit` and `transfer` can also write. Your original ask covered five commands (`create`, `update`, `close`, `delete`, `import`), so I kept it narrow. The worker has follow-ups `robots-3rm0a`, `robots-ax1b1` and `idea-coyp` filed and will make sure they cover those commands.\n3. **Fix if safe: docs for an unrelated command.** The change also added docs for `bd stores rewrite-wrappers`. The worker removes them unless that breaks the docs-generation check, in which case it leaves them and says why.\n\nI logged the decisions in `status-kdv`. The PR should merge itself once checks pass, and I'll close `robots-sl1eq` with it as evidence."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":157907,"output_tokens":457,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":157907,"cache_creation_input_to