{"parentUuid":"f1a849cb-b4e7-4253-92f2-2d217eb5976e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3bad3673-ad6d-4094-9335-2ccaf8e244e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015WddnJVYkQ6R55jzx1N3qR","type":"tool_result","content":"run: 01M5B2ZHP4ZB6Z4PWMNHEZXQ6Z\nstep: review\ngate: awaiting_approval\nask-user findings: 3\n\n---\nid: sl1eq-boundary-bedis\nseverity: error\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\nline: 316\ndescription: Intent conformance: the refusal is skipped whenever BEADS_DIR is non-empty, but a non-project BEADS_DIR still forwards a bare write. Source path: BEADS_DIR=/new/place/.beads brain create x -> remoteForwardingActive returns active (line 316 condition false) -> sshArgs/remoteScript (brain_remote.go:181, 240) carry only BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE-less argv and never pass BEADS_DIR -> host runs its default 'brain' wrapper -> write lands in the host default store, not the explicit BEADS_DIR and not the cwd workspace. The intent criterion 'This never writes outside an explicit BEADS_DIR or the cwd workspace' is violated by this hunk. The test at brain_remote_test.go:285-291 locks this in on the premise 'a thin client's wrapper sets one', but remoteWrapperBody (brain_remote.go:833-835) sets only BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE, so that premise is false in this source. Remedy (either refuse writes when BEADS_DIR names a non-project path, or forward BEADS_DIR to the host) changes behavior beyond the narrow fix and needs an authorized decision.\nauthority: ask-user\n\n---\nid: sl1eq-unguarded-write-verbs\nseverity: warning\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\nline: 256\ndescription: Bare write verbs outside the intent's list still forward with no store named, so the reported foreign-store write persists for them. cmd/bd/quick.go defines top-level 'q [title]' (a bead-creating verb, documented in CLAUDE.md as 'inbox q'); comment.go ('comment <id>'), brain_transfer.go ('transfer <id> <dest>'), edit.go, label.go and dep.go are also mutating. Example: fresh git dir, client config present, no BEADS_DIR, 'brain q \"idea\"' forwards and writes to the host default store. The intent explicitly enumerates create/update/close/delete/import, so this is within the authored narrow scope, but the remedy (widening remoteWriteVerbs) extends the authored list and needs authorization.\nauthority: ask-user\n\n---\nid: sl1eq-unrelated-docs\nseverity: info\nfile: docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md\nline: 6646\ndescription: The change adds reference docs for 'bd stores rewrite-wrappers' (CLI_REFERENCE.md, website/docs/cli-reference/brain.md, stores.md). That command is unrelated to the bare-write refusal in this intent and is not changed by this diff. Remove those hunks from this change, or split them out, so the diff matches the stated fix.\nauthority: ask-user\npaused [at=1792447744]: pipeline fix round for sl1eq-boundary-bedis running (run 01M5B2ZHP4ZB6Z4PWMNHEZXQ6Z); resumes when the drive call returns the next gate, CI-ready, or outcome","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e7d67a32-8185-4e11-81f9-83710516be1a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T22:13:06.709Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"run: 01M5B2ZHP4ZB6Z4PWMNHEZXQ6Z\nstep: review\ngate: awaiting_approval\nask-user findings: 3\n\n---\nid: sl1eq-boundary-bedis\nseverity: error\nfile: cmd/bd/brain_remote.go\nline: 316\ndescription: Intent conformance: the refusal is skipped whenever BEADS_DIR is non-empty, but a non-project BEADS_DIR still forwards a bare write. Source path: BEADS_DIR=/new/place/.beads brain create x -> remoteForwardingActive returns active (line 316 condition false) -> sshArgs/remoteScript (brain_remote.go:181, 240) carry only BRAIN_REMOTE_STORE-less argv and never pass BEADS_DIR -> host runs its default 'brain' wrapper -> write lands in the host default store, not the explicit BEADS_DIR and not the cwd workspace. The intent criterion 'This never writes outside an explicit BEADS_DIR or the cwd workspace' is violated by this hunk. The test at brain_remote_test.go:285-291 locks this in on the premise 'a thi