{"parentUuid":"2c226b14-7ac1-4b0b-9508-1d38e3f69b83","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3bad3673-ad6d-4094-9335-2ccaf8e244e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Standing nudge (12 items), repeated each poke:\n     - Log all actions in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked).\n     - Put durable work in the right bead.\n     - Never have a no-work turn.\n     - Pull from projects, task ready, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review.\n     - Keep Sidecar (project-yg4v, runbooks-5vr) and the Talon palette (project-7u7w, idea-7d0b) moving.\n     - Overnight usability/onboarding plans.\n     - Idle design review (runbooks-b6e).\n     - Take the top open robots items, diagnose or dispatch a fix, and close with evidence.\n     - Check quota-axi and speed metrics each poke and spend underused usage (prefer Fable).\n     - Keep the queue deep and review PRs/reports.\n   - Automated \"Continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes: handle, then ack with `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`, and ack the wake with the exact `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G` command.\n   - Captain requests this segment, all handled or answered as noted in the analysis:\n     - Status of fm-hooks and of Sidecar off-tailnet pairing.\n     - Security threats of exposing vps01/sidecar.trilliumsmith.com.\n     - Read a Gmail message via gog (could not; asked for sender/subject).\n     - MiniMax-M3.1-Flash free usage: use Claude/Fable for planning and pi on MiniMax (\"spacebunny\") for MIT OSS work for 3 days (until 2026-10-22). Blocked by the missing MiniMax credential.\n     - `self tabs` (fixed).\n     - Which herdr tabs are done/landed and closable (answered; nothing closed yet).\n     - Create task bead for `mergetest` CLI (task-u08t5).\n     - Runbook for the 24h dev-work audit run by Fable (runbooks-86h).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling: `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, exact `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`, `fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N` (refused for non-captain-outcome seqs like 2142), `fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`. Export `FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate`. Never top-level `cd` (persistent-cd hook denies it); use absolute paths or `git -C`. Foreground `sleep` is blocked.\n   - Delivery flow: `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M`, fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} via `python3 -I`, `fm-tasks-axi.sh add <id> '<title>' --kind ship`, `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> projects/<p> --mode M --yolo on --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh`, `fm-pr-merge.sh <id> <url>` (refuses red/unreported checks or non-open PRs), `fm-teardown.sh <id>`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`, `fm-send.sh <task> [--resolve-key K] \"$(cat file)\"`, `fm-crew-state.sh <id>`.\n   - ask-user-authority: firstmate decides findings that are unambiguous toward the accepted design and escalates ambiguous or contract-expanding ones; the worker answers through the active no-mistakes gate (never `--yes`).\n   - Project postures: fm-hooks (firstmate_hooks) direct-PR +yolo; brain, forefront, forefront-backend, parlay no-mistakes +yolo; dotfiles and the macbook-ops projects local-only (landing needs the captain's word); GitHub Actions fail from account billing (captain-only fix).\n   - Sidecar: Go repo in macbook-ops/projects/sidecar. QR pairing (task-l9vv0). Public at https://sidecar.trilliumsmith.com via an A record to vps01 plus a Caddy vhost proxying over the tailnet to the Mac. Funnel off. Status bead status-vkr.\n   - Quota (2026-10-19): claude all_models 29% / fable 16%, now projected_exhaustion, resets ~2026-10-20T00:00Z. codex 100% but the binary is missing on the Mac. minimax auth_required. opencode-go 43% monthly.\n   - herdr: `self` script, `herdr pane current --current`, `herdr tab list --workspace`. HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID env was stale (wY1 vs actual wY7).\n   - Beads Bridge MCP is currently down (bead_create UNAVAILABLE); use the store CLIs directly.\n   - Store CLIs: task, robots, runbooks, projects, status, ideas, brain, etc.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/.local/bin/self (edited): cmd_tabs and cmd_panes now resolve the workspace via herdr first.\n     ```\n     local ws; ws=$(herdr pane current --current 2>/dev/null | jq -r '.result.pane.workspace_id // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)\n     [ -n \"$ws\" ] || ws=\"${HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID:-}\"\n     ```\n     Replaced the old `local ws=\"${HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID:-}\"` in both functions. Not version controlled. Output also tees to pbcopy.\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/brain-sl1eq-q1/brief.md: ship brief for robots-sl1eq (option B: refuse client-mode mutating verbs create/update/close/delete/import when BEADS_DIR is unset and no .beads is found from cwd; error 'no beads workspace here; set BEADS_DIR or BRAIN_REMOTE=off'; reads keep forwarding; tests; BEADS_DIR guard already in PR 45).\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/parlay-listen-q1/brief.md: ship brief for robots-wsv8a (bounded retry/backoff on register-agent plus a clearer error in `parlay listen`; tests).\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/brain-sl1eq-q1/nm-01M5B2ZHP4ZB6Z4PWMNHEZXQ6Z-findings.txt: the first gate's 3 findings. Newest gate details are in nm-drive-2.log (2 findings).\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/bd-store-resolution-scout-q1/report.md: scout report with recommended fixes (gbu6f one guard; sl1eq options A/B/C, scout recommends B).\n   - ~/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/memory/three-day-routing-oct19.md (created) and a pointer line added to MEMORY.md: Fable plans, pi + free MiniMax builds MIT OSS until 2026-10-22.\n   - /private/tmp/claude-501/rb.txt: runbook text, stored in runbooks-86h.\n   - /private/tmp/claude-501/sl1.txt, unl.txt: fm-send message bodies.\n   - Beads created or touched: task-u245d (3-day routing + MiniMax blocker), task-u08t5 (mergetest CLI), robots-jecsr (Beads Bridge MCP down), runbooks-86h (24h audit runbook, label project:firstmate), robots-59gm1 (closed), robots-sl1eq and robots-wsv8a (commented, open pending PRs), status-kdv (poke logs).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Gmail URL token (FMfcg…) rejected by `gog gmail read` (\"Invalid id value\"): searched the inbox instead and asked the captain for sender/subject; account index /u/3 may differ from trillium@trilliumsmith.com.\n   - `fm-pr-merge` said \"invalid PR merge request\" on a bad invocation: re-ran with the exact command and found PRs 10 and 11 already merged.\n   - `mark-processed --through 2142` refused (not an unprocessed captain outcome): ignored; acks still worked.\n   - persistent-cd hook denied a `cd`: used absolute paths and `git -C`.\n   - `task comment` without text errored: found the bead id with `task search` and re-ran.\n   - `self tabs` showed the wrong or empty workspace: fixed in the script (see above).\n   - Foreground `sleep 45` blocked by the harness: dropped the sleep and re-checked state instead.\n   - Beads Bridge MCP outage: worked around with the CLI and filed robots-jecsr.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: fm-hooks cursor tmp-file fix landed (PR 12) and the other fm-hooks PRs 10/11 confirmed merged; Talon phone injection and command execution proven on device; `self tabs` fixed; mergetest bead created; the runbook created; wsv8a diagnosed as transient and a ship dispatched; sl1eq decided and the ship driven through the first review gate.\n   - Ongoing: brain-sl1eq-q1 is parked at a second review gate with 2 findings; parlay-listen-q1 is working; macbook-ops is doing Talon real-noise/corpus testing; MiniMax credential missing blocks pi routing; GitHub billing blocks red PRs.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Repeated standing nudge text (pasted blocks, items 1–12), several times.\n   - \"where are we on the intended fm_hooks? where are we on sidecar, sidecar pairing for off-tailnet machiens?\"\n   - \"if we expose vps01.trilliumsmith.com or sidecar.trilliumsmith.com what are the potenital security threats from that exposure?\"\n   - \"read this email https://mail.google.com/mail/u/3/#inbox/FMfcgzQhWxXdmkFcdPQPsrKBTnDdNDNs with `gog` trillium@trilliumsmith.com\"\n   - \"oh its $5 maximum for free accounts, lame - does opencode offer this?\"\n   - \"this meaning the minimax MiniMax-M3.1-Flash https://x.com/opencode/status/2112156205938626954 guess it was spacebunny, there is free usage, lets use claude for fable smarts tasks, planning, and then drop into spacebunny pi for MIT OSS stuff for the next 3 days\"\n   - \"`self` command, I want to be able to get the tabs in the contained workspace `self tabs` maybe?\"\n   - Pasted `self tabs` output (27 tabs) with \"this is us, this is all the tabs, which ones are done/landed and can be closed?\"\n   - Pasted DEBUG: bead_create failed (Store: task; Title: Build `mergetest` CLI for non-mutating merge conflict checks; Beads Bridge MCP UNAVAILABLE).\n   - \"make a runbook for `audit my development work in the last 24h, identify bottlenecks that slowed down my velocity, and propose improvements` where the ask is that fable does this\"\n   - Automated system notifications (Stop-hook wakes, task notifications) are not user messages.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Immediately: answer brain-sl1eq-q1's second review gate (2 findings; see Current Work), then ack. Close robots-sl1eq on merge with the PR as evidence.\n   - parlay-listen-q1: when its PR is ready, merge it via fm-pr-merge, close robots-wsv8a with evidence, tear down.\n   - Offered but not yet authorized: run runbooks-86h on Fable now (usage is now tight, so probably wait for the window reset).\n   - Offered: close the two truly done tabs (forefront-config-auth-q2 and sms-eval-q1) and idle panes; not done, awaiting the captain's word.\n   - Offered: scout audit of