this second gate was not yet confirmed; the status log should show a new `needs-decision [key=...]` line.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Decide and answer brain-sl1eq-q1's second gate through the worker, passing the new decision key with `--resolve-key`. The decision should be: review-1, Fix by refusing in-workspace bare writes (or otherwise guaranteeing a bare write cannot land in the host default store) because the accepted contract says the client never writes outside an explicit BEADS_DIR or the cwd workspace. This also means updating the \"write inside a workspace must forward\" test. Before that, confirm that the premise is not a legitimate wrapper-forwarding design (workspace forwarding vs store-wrapper behavior); if it is ambiguous, escalate to the captain with the five-element form. review-2, Fix (revert the hunk). Then ack the wake, log in status-kdv, and continue to monitor for the PR, then merge via `fm-pr-merge.sh brain-sl1eq-q1 <url>` and close robots-sl1eq with evidence. Quote of where I left off: \"Latest wake… `state: parked · source: run-step · parked at review: 2 finding(s) · ask-user: authority decision · run: 01M5B2ZHP4ZB6Z4PWMNHEZXQ6Z`\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isC