{"parentUuid":"aec610da-6611-463f-b70c-86bc5715fa8f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0792ce07-edec-457e-a32e-1471fe661b18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TL8vfJwducbKS3uE5j815t","type":"tool_result","content":"no-mistakes run 01M5B3XEE65BXFVR1AJ340MGYD — gate: review (status awaiting_approval, risk medium)\nbranch fm/parlay-listen-q1, head c96d4b6fdbe5b014177f0e39cc22fa3ec0ecaa0c\nGate findings, verbatim and unparaphrased (the gate gave no line column; \"line\" below is quoted from the description where it names one).\n\n---- finding 1 ----\nid: wsv8a-clipped-attempt-message\nseverity: warning\nfile: tools/cli/internal/httpc/retry.go\nline: (not given by the gate; description cites \"line 155\")\nauthority: auto-fix\ndescription: Exhausted message reports every attempt as waiting the full PerAttempt, but the final attempt is clipped to the remaining Budget (e.g. 8.5s of 10s). The stated wait is wrong; the same stale value feeds the dial-timeout text at line 155. Fix: pass the actual waited duration of the last attempt.\n\n---- finding 2 ----\nid: wsv8a-unrequired-classifier\nseverity: warning\nfile: tools/cli/internal/httpc/retry.go\nline: (not given by the gate)\nauthority: ask-user\ndescription: The four-way reachKind classifier, httptrace connection tracking in postOnce, and SLOW/UNREACHABLE/UNSTABLE messages (~180 lines in shared httpc) are not required by the intent, which only needs transient enrollment failures retried. Remedy is removing this classification and keeping a single retry loop with the existing 'Cannot reach Parlay server at <base>' message; removal is the remedy, so it needs authorization.\n\n==== What a Fix would commit to (crewmate's reading of the remedies; not part of the gate text) ====\n\nwsv8a-clipped-attempt-message (auto-fix): the pipeline edits retry.go so the exhausted \"Cannot reach Parlay server ...\" message and the dial-timeout wording report the duration the LAST attempt actually waited (the budget-clipped value) instead of the policy's PerAttempt. Message-text-only change in httpc; no behavior change to retry/backoff/budget; existing tests assert on attempt tallies and verdict words, not on the per-attempt duration string, so they should stay green.\n\nwsv8a-unrequired-classifier (ask-user): the pipeline removes the reachKind classifier, the httptrace GotConn tracking in postOnce, and the SLOW / UNREACHABLE / UNSTABLE verdict text, leaving one bounded retry loop that dies with the pre-existing \"Cannot reach Parlay server at <base>: <err>\" message. That also commits to deleting or rewriting everything that pins the verdict: httpc tests TestPostJSONRetryGivesUpAtAttemptsAndSaysSlow, TestPostJSONRetryRefusedConnectionSaysUnreachable, TestClassifyTransport; monitor tests asserting \"SLOW, not down\" / \"UNREACHABLE\"; the listen help sentence in internal/help/help.go; the docs/monitor.md paragraph and the docs/agent-notes/internal-httpc-has-exactly-one-timeout-robots-gxlb.md section that describe the verdict; and the e2e proof in e2e-summary.md would no longer match the shipped message.\n\nContext for the decision (factual, not a recommendation): the no-mistakes --intent was the captain's text only (per the brief), which says \"transient (likely server busy or an overly tight client deadline)\". The Firstmate spec that drove the implementation additionally asked for \"a clearer error that says whether the server is slow or unreachable\"; the reviewer did not see that sentence, which is why it classifies the verdict as unrequired.\n\nResponse commands the decision maps to (I run the chosen one from the worktree, backgrounded, never --yes):\n  approve as-is ............ no-mistakes axi respond --action approve\n  fix only the auto-fix .... no-mistakes axi respond --action fix --findings wsv8a-clipped-attempt-message\n  fix both ................. no-mistakes axi respond --action fix --findings wsv8a-clipped-attempt-message,wsv8a-unrequired-classifier\n  skip the review step ..... no-mistakes axi respond --action skip","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0cb149f6-8e7a-4bf7-b877-daff155d0000","timestamp":"2026-10-19T22:24:57.864Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"no-mistakes run 01M5B3XEE65BXFVR1AJ340MGYD — gate: review (status awaiting_approval, risk medium)\nbranch fm/parlay-listen-q1, head c96d4b6fdbe5b014177f0e39cc22fa3ec0ecaa0c\nGate findings, verbatim and unparaphrased (the gate gave no line column; \"line\" below is quoted from the description where it names one).\n\n---- finding 1 ----\nid: wsv8a-clipped-attempt-message\nseverity: warning\nfile: tools/cli/internal/httpc/retry.go\nline: (not given by the gate; description cites \"line 155\")\nauthority: auto-fix\ndescription: Exhausted message reports every attempt as waiting the full PerAttempt, but the final attempt is clipped to the remaining Budget (e.g. 8.5s of 10s). The stated wait is wrong; the same stale value feeds the dial-timeout text at line 155. Fix: pass the actual waited duration of the last attempt.\n\n---- finding 2 ----\nid: wsv8a-unrequired-classifier\nseverity: warning\nfile: tools/cli/internal/httpc/retry.go\nline: (not given by the gate)\nauthority: ask-user\ndescription: The four-way reachKind classifier, httptrace connection tracking in postOnce, and SLOW/UNREACHABLE/UNSTABLE messages (~180 lines in shared httpc) are not required by the intent, which only needs transient enrollment failures retried. Remedy is removing this classification and keeping a single retry loop with the existing 'Cannot reach Parlay server at <base>' message; removal is the remedy, so it needs authorization.\n\n==== What a Fix would commit to (crewmate's reading of the remedies; not part of the gate text) ====\n\nwsv8a-clipped-attempt-message (auto-fix): the pipeline edits retry.go so the exhausted \"Cannot reach Parlay server ...\" message and the dial-timeout wording report the duration the LAST attempt actually waited (the budget-clipped value) instead of the policy's PerAttempt. Message-text-only change in httpc; no behavior change to retry/backoff/budget; existing tests assert on attempt tallies and verdict words, not on the per-attempt duration string, so they should stay green.\n\nwsv8a-unrequired-classifier (ask-user): the pipeline removes the reachKind classifier, the httptrace GotConn tracking in postOnce, and the SLOW / UNREACHABLE / UNSTABLE verdict text, leaving one bounded retry loop that dies with the pre-existing \"Cannot reach Parlay server at <base>: <err>\" message. That also commits to deleting or rewriting everything that pins the verdict: httpc tests TestPostJSONRetryGivesUpAtAttemptsAndSaysSlow, TestPostJSONRetryRefusedConnectionSaysUnreachable, TestClassifyTransport; monitor tests asserting \"SLOW, not down\" / \"UNREACHABLE\"; the listen help sentence in internal/help/help.go; the docs/monitor.md paragraph and the docs/agent-notes/internal-httpc-has-exactly-one-timeout-robots-gxlb.md section that describe the verdict; and the e2e proof in e2e-summary.md would no longer match the shipped message.\n\nContext for the decision (factual, not a recommendation): the no-mistakes --intent was the captain's text only (per the brief), which says \"transient (likely server busy or an overly tight client deadline)\". The Firstmate spec that drove the implementation additionally asked for \"a clearer error that says whether the server is slow or unreachable\"; the reviewer did not see that sentence, which is why it classifies the verdict as unrequired.\n\nResponse commands the decision maps to (I run the chosen one from the worktree, backgrounded, never --yes):\n  approve as-is ............ no-mistakes axi respond --action approve\n  fix only the auto-fix .... no-mistakes axi respond --action fix --findings wsv8a-clipped-attempt-message\n  fix both ................. no-mistakes axi respond --action fix --findings wsv8a-clipped-attempt-message,wsv8a-unrequired-classifier\n  skip the review step ..... no-mistakes axi respond --action skip","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aec610da-6611-463f-b70c-86bc5715fa8f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
