{"parentUuid":"4a135930-9dcf-4478-b06b-9bfebb991258","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCR9LJ1gXPDqYbDCpkor","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_read_input_tokens":137863,"output_tokens":1280,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":314},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":137863,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8219,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgCR9L1uFBv2EbfJz98JY","type":"assistant","uuid":"e03bca76-9942-4794-b4b3-90680c37d1d2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T22:53:11.306Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"e03bca76-9942-4794-b4b3-90680c37d1d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCR9LJ1gXPDqYbDCpkor","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, we have 112 commits on top of upstream. About 6,100 lines of the 13,300 added are real firstmate fixes. The rest is non-code clutter that can be deleted.\n\nI measured everything from the last commit we share with upstream, via `git diff` and `git log`.\n\n**What differs**\n\n| Area | Size | What it is |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bin/` | 6,095 lines, 34 files | Fixes and features for how we run (list below) |\n| `tests/` | 4,266 lines, 56 files | Tests for those fixes |\n| `acceptance-out/` | 1,704 lines, 120 files | Stray run artifacts, not code |\n| `assets/`, `OPENCLAW_TALK_PREP.md` | about 960 lines | Stray local files, committed so main would be clean for local-only landing |\n| `docs/`, `.agents/`, `.github/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `fm-hooks.rules.json` | about 450 lines | Small docs and config |\n\nOf the 112 commits, 30 are `fix:` and 5 are `feat:`. They fall into these groups:\n- **Spawn and teardown safety:** refuse a worktree held by a live sibling, refuse to tear down ships with open PRs, bounded polling uses `/bin/sleep`, dot-free window names.\n- **Our multi-machine setup:** configurable remote Herdr session, secondmate state kept in the home that registers it, the fleet view showing secondmates.\n- **Reliability under load:** stale-lock reclaim, wake-queue lock holder named, a launchctl retry on transient errors, a stale-worker reaper, the Claude-limit failover watchdog, Pi trust-dialog handling.\n- **Our own tooling:** a `doctor` health check, the Jev dispatch log, the lavish and pulse-page skills, an exemption for your account (`trillium`) from the no-mistakes gate.\n\n**Why it diverged**\n1. This home runs as a firstmate user, so it can't publish to upstream without your consent. Every fix we hit lands only here.\n2. Those fixes were real bugs in our setup. They are the queued firstmate-repo fixes (`robots-q22c`, `d8dvl`, `wajev`, `8swcz`, `q4lpu`) that are waiting on that same consent.\n3. Local-only landing means nothing flows upstream on its own, so the divergence grows each week.\n\nI'm in the middle of merging upstream's latest into main, which has 5 conflicts.\n1. I resolved all 5 by keeping both sides' intent. The tests are running in the background.\n2. I haven't committed the merge yet.\n\n**Options:** you could consent to a one-time upstream PR batch for the real fixes, or I can first split the clutter out of the diff so the remaining difference is only fixes. Tell me which and I'll start."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_read_input_tokens":137863,"output_tokens":1280,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":314},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":137863,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2024},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgCR9L1uFBv2EbfJz98JY","type":"assistant","uuid":"d22a616f-01c8-4c2e-af31-aa1cbe892f31","timestamp":"2026-10-19T22:53:12.528Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
