l","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"e11e30bf-9eb0-4a13-a20f-ced4a4b76566","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d4ab255f-606e-4d39-b771-772119ed2d4d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YKcLapybptuxBG5uED6t9M","type":"tool_result","content":"23:19Z\n  claude,all_models,7,61.8732,projected_exhaustion,established,five_hour,\"2026-10-19T23:49:59.585524+00:00\"\n  claude,\"model:fable\",7,46.8406,projected_exhaustion,established,five_hour,\"2026-10-19T23:49:59.585524+00:00\"\n  claude,all_models,1216,\"2026-10-19T23:39:36.639Z\",five_hour\n  claude,\"model:fable\",1216,\"2026-10-19T23:39:36.639Z\",five_hour\nScaffold a crewmate brief or persistent secondmate charter at\ndata/<task-id>/brief.md under the active firstmate home.\nFor ordinary tasks, the standard Setup/Rules/Definition-of-done contract is\nfilled in. Ship and scout `# Task` sections have two subsections Firstmate\nfills before dispatch: `{TASK}` under `## Captain's intent` (the captain's\nown ask plus the context needed to read it, including the substance of any\nreport, decision, or PR the ask refers to, without added speaker labels or\ndirect address) and `{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}`\nunder `## Firstmate spec` (build instructions, which are never the captain's\nintent). bin/fm-dod-lib.sh owns the no-mistakes `--intent` contract those\nsubsections feed; bin/fm-spawn.sh refuses leftover placeholders and a\n`## Captain's intent` line opening with a Captain label or address. Secondmate\ncharters still use a single `{TASK}` charter fill. Firstmate may adjust other\nsections when the task genuinely deviates (e.g. working an existing external\nPR instead of shipping a new one).\nUsage: fm-brief.sh <task-id> <repo-name> --mode <no-mistakes|direct-PR|local-only> [--branch-prefix <prefix>] [--base-branch <branch>] [--forge <none|gerrit|forgejo|exter\n       fm-brief.sh <task-id> <repo-name> --scout [--base-branch <branch>] [--herdr-lab]\n       fm-brief.sh <task-id> --secondmate {<project>...|--no-projects}\n  --scout writes the scout contract instead: the deliverable is a report at\n  data/<task-id>/report.md (no branch, no push, no PR) and the worktree is scratch.\n  It offers the Lavish review loop only when `fm-bootstrap.sh lavish-compatible`\n  confirms the legacy board-compatibility floor; otherwise it asks for a text report.\n  --secondmate writes a persistent secondmate charter. The project list\n  is cloned into the secondmate home, while the natural-language scope\n  tells the main firstmate when to route work there; routine churn stays in its own home;\n  captain-relevant escalations and marked from-firstmate replies append to this\n  home's status file.\n  --no-projects writes a project-less charter for a domain whose subject is the\n  firstmate repo itself (its home is a firstmate worktree, its crews take pooled\n  worktrees of the same repo). It is mutually exclusive with a project list, and\n- federated-markdown-bridge [local-only] - Store-backed Markdown bridge for Firstmate customizations (added 2026-09-27)\n# --- migrated from ~/code/firstmate/data/projects.md on 2026-09-27 (task-pgjq4); entries below are the other home's registry verbatim ---\n- tasks-axi [direct-PR] - tasks-axi backlog CLI (TS/npm), the tool firstmate uses for data/backlog.md; fork of kunchenguid/tasks-axi at tril\n- iphone-contacts-sync [local-only] - local iPhone<->macOS contact sync/merge tool (Swift iOS app + Bun/TS cli/server/web), LAN + Tailscale,\n- firstmate_mcp [direct-PR] - First Mate MCP smarts layer (typed tools over firstmate, approval-gated, launch yes code no); origin at trilli\n- captains-deck [direct-PR +yolo] - Captain's Deck: Herdr kanban board plugin for Firstmate (Python TUI): read-only fleet board projected fr\n- parlay-voice-pwa [local-only +yolo] - Parlay Voice Input PWA: iPhone-first remote text-input surface for Parlay (Vite + TypeScript + Effec\n- fm-hooks [direct-PR +yolo] - External fm_* semantic-event hook layer: observes Firstmate calls from harness-native hooks and enqueues foll\n- firstmate-upstream [local-only] - Clean read-only clone of upstream kunchenguid/firstmate for studying how work launches and what re-trigg\n- firstmate [direct-PR +yolo] - Trillium fork of Firstmate itself (origin=trillium/firstmate); PRs target the fork only, never upstream kunc\n- barter [no-mistakes-prod-only +yolo] - Barterboo (barterboo.com) trading app, Next.js; origin trillium/barter; clone at ~/code/barter (sym","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d2e8fc8a-db21-4c52-9491-4b54ac2b2987","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:19:20.395Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"23:19Z\n  claude,all_models,7,61.8732,projected_exhaustion,established,five_hour,\"2026-10-19T23:49:59.585524+00:00\"\n  claude,\"model:fable\",7,46.8406,projected_exhaustion,established,five_hour,\"2026-10-19T23:49:59.585524+00:00\"\n  claude,all_models,1216,\"2026-10-19T23:39:36.639Z\",five_hour\n  claude,\"model:fable\",1216,\"2026-10-19T23:39:36.639Z\",five_hour\nScaffold a crewmate brief or persistent secondmate charter at\ndata/<task-id>/brief.md under the active firstmate home.\nFor ordinary tasks, the standard Setup/Rules/Definition-of-done contract is\nfilled in. Ship and scout `# Task` sections have two subsections Firstmate\nfills before dispatch: `{TASK}` under `## Captain's intent` (the captain's\nown ask plus the context needed to read it, including the substance of any\nreport, decision, or PR the ask refers to, without added speaker labels or\ndirect address) and `{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}`\nunder `## Firstmate spec` (build instructions, which are never the captain's\nintent). bin/fm-dod-lib.sh owns the no-mistakes `--intent` contract those\nsubsections feed; bin/fm-spawn.sh refuses leftover placeholders and a\n`## Captain's intent` line opening with a Captain label or address. Secondmate\ncharters still use a single `{TASK}` charter fill. Firstmate may adjust other\nsections when the task genuinely deviates (e.g. working an existing external\nPR instead of shipping a new one).\nUsage: fm