{"parentUuid":"8dc150f0-b94a-4bd8-a7c5-625a817eda59","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d4ab255f-606e-4d39-b771-772119ed2d4d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Standing nudge (12 items), repeated on each poke:\n     - Log all actions in status-kdv (Done / In flight / Next / Blocked).\n     - Put durable work in the right bead.\n     - Never have a no-work turn.\n     - Pull from projects, task ready, ideas, questions, nightshift-tasks, review.\n     - Keep Sidecar (project-yg4v, runbooks-5vr) and the Talon palette (project-7u7w, idea-7d0b) moving.\n     - Overnight usability/onboarding plans.\n     - Idle design review (runbooks-b6e).\n     - Take the top open robots items and close them with evidence.\n     - Check quota-axi and speed metrics each poke, and spend underused usage (prefer Fable).\n     - Keep the queue deep and review PRs/reports.\n   - Automated \"Continue the work already authorized\" inbox notes: handle them, ack with `bin/fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`, then ack the wake with the exact `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`.\n   - Captain asks this segment, with their status:\n     - Done: merged brain PR 48 and parlay PR 348, closing robots-sl1eq and robots-wsv8a.\n     - Done: resolved the 5 upstream-merge conflicts and committed the merge locally as f92089d7.\n     - Done: explained how the fork diverges from standard firstmate and why. The captain is trying to avoid divergence. The decision is still open as task-kj3ni.\n     - Done: recorded \"firstmate share\" scope (send screenshots to different firstmates) on project-p16v.\n     - Done: listed Fable-ready tasks as a collection only (\"do not run them, this is a collection\").\n     - CURRENT: \"we have 7% left this window, then TEN MINUTES before a full reset. The intent is to go HAM HAM in those 10 minutes to get some insane level work done, then pause back to normal levels.\" Clarified: \"window ends 4:50pm, full reset 5pm.\" Dispatch a burst of high-value Fable work before the window ends and the usage expires.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Wake handling: `LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh`, exact `--ack-through N --recovery-generation G`, `fm-branch-outcome.sh mark-processed --through N`, `fm-inbox.sh drain --ack <id>`. Export `FM_HOME=/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate`. Never a top-level `cd` (the persistent-cd hook denies it); use absolute paths, `git -C`, or subshells. Foreground sleep is limited: use `/bin/sleep` in short loops under 120s per call. Long tests go in the background.\n   - Delivery flow: `fm-brief.sh <id> <project> --mode M` (or `--scout`), fill {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} via `python3 -I`, `fm-tasks-axi.sh add <id> '<title>' --kind ship`, `HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 fm-spawn.sh <id> projects/<p> --mode M --yolo on --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh` (or `--scout`), `fm-pr-merge.sh <id> <url>` (refuses red or unreported checks), `fm-teardown.sh <id>`, `fm-fleet-sync.sh`, `fm-send.sh <task> [--resolve-key K] \"$(cat file)\"`, `fm-crew-state.sh <id>`.\n   - ask-user-authority: firstmate decides findings that are unambiguous toward the accepted design and escalates ambiguous or contract-expanding ones; the worker answers through the no-mistakes gate (never `--yes`). A worker must write a keyed needs-decision status line before firstmate decides.\n   - firstmate-self-repo: this home is user/operator, so publishing to upstream needs a maintainer opt-in or a one-task `--upstream-consent`. Pulling from upstream is allowed.\n   - Project postures: brain, parlay, forefront, forefront-backend are no-mistakes +yolo; fm-hooks and firstmate (fork) are direct-PR +yolo; barter is no-mistakes-prod-only +yolo; dotfiles and the macbook-ops projects are local-only (landing needs the captain's word).\n   - Quota (Mac, 2026-10-19, local PDT = UTC-7): claude all_models 7% / fable 7%, five_hour window ending 23:50Z (4:50pm), full reset ~00:00Z (5pm). codex 100% but its binary is missing on the Mac; agy 95-97%; opencode-go 43%; grok creds expired; minimax needs auth.\n   - Stores: task, robots, runbooks, projects, status, ideas, brain, guard, and others, via their CLIs. The Beads Bridge MCP is down (robots-jecsr).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - /private/tmp/claude-501/sl2.txt, pl2.txt: fm-send decision bodies for the sl1eq and wsv8a gates.\n   - /private/tmp/claude-501/resolve.py: python3 -I resolver for the 5 merge conflicts. Key behaviors:\n     - ci.yml: pinned Pi step with a combined comment.\n     - fm-git-strip-ai-trailers.sh: `$(sentinel_body)` then `$strip_line`.\n     - fm-spawn.sh: `${wt_polls} polls of ${wt_poll_interval}s ... $(spawn_endpoint_hint)`.\n     - fm-control-relaunch.test.sh: take upstream's `fm_test_remove_tree` and `fm_test_cleanup`, keep both new tests.\n     - fm-spawn-worktree-settle.test.sh: keep both tests, with the `}` between them.\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/tests/fm-control-relaunch.test.sh (edited): removed the top-level `export FM_FAKE_COMPOSER_READ_FAIL=1` in test_relaunch_proceeds_when_composer_is_unproven_but_interactive_ready, and scoped it: `out=$(FM_FAKE_COMPOSER_READ_FAIL=1 run_control \"$dir\" rl80 relaunch --note \"preserve\") || rc=$?`.\n   - Merge commit f92089d7 \"Merge upstream/main (45dd50a5) into main\" (local only). Remaining dirty working tree is unrelated: M .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json, .cursor/hooks.json, CHANGELOG.md; ?? .agents/hooks.json, .entire/, .opencode/plugins/entire.ts.\n   - /Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate/data/brain-sl1eq-q1/ and data/parlay-listen-q1/: briefs, findings files, and e2e logs. Both tasks are torn down.\n   - ~/.local/bin/fm-nudge and the poke text ~/.fm-nudge.text (read, unchanged).\n   - ~/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/memory/MEMORY.md (reloaded; includes the three-day-routing line).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `fm-send` printed \"queued wakes pending\": drained the wakes, and the decision had in fact been delivered and resolved.\n   - A persistent-cd hook denial on `cd`: switched to absolute paths and `git -C`.\n   - The `$G` variable `git -C ...` in one shell call failed with \"no such file or directory\": use the literal command.\n   - `fm-pr-merge` refused parlay PR 348 while CodeRabbit was pending: waited for it to pass, then merged.\n   - A too-broad `lsof -p ... -iTCP` produced noisy output while hunting the beads-bridge port: abandoned it, recorded the finding on robots-jecsr, port still unfound.\n   - fm-control-relaunch test: a first-run timing failure (\"relaunch did not reach trace delivery\") was transient under load. The real failure was the leaked `FM_FAKE_COMPOSER_READ_FAIL` env breaking upstream's away-branch test; fixed by scoping the variable. Final rerun rc=0 with 0 \"not ok\".\n   - Stop hooks: continuation-guard (fixed by doing the work), testing-offload-guard false positive (labeled fp via `guard label add guard-gx029 fp` and `guard update`).\n   - `fm-inbox.sh show` is not a valid subcommand: read `state/inbox/*<id>*` directly instead.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: sl1eq and wsv8a fixed, merged, and closed with evidence. The upstream merge resolved, tested, and committed locally. The fork-divergence analysis delivered, with task-kj3ni holding the open decision. The Firstmate Share scope recorded. The Fable-ready task collection listed.\n   - Ongoing: robots-jecsr (bridge port not found); the Fable burst (see Current Work); the divergence decision in task-kj3ni; GitHub Actions billing; the missing MiniMax credential.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Repeated standing nudge text (pasted blocks, items 1–12), several times, including mid-turn deliveries.\n   - Pasted `git fetch upstream && git merge upstream/main` output showing 5 conflicts.\n   - \"we're starting to diverge again from standard firstamte, this is a thing I am trying to avoid - how is our code different and why is it differnet?\"\n   - \"firstmate share - we need the abiltiy to send the screenshot to different firstmates, that would be helpful\"\n   - \"what tasks right now do we have that are ready to run with fable? what needs that level of smarts?\"\n   - \"do not run them, this is a collection\"\n   - \"so we ahve 7% left this window, then we have TEN MINUTES before a full reset. The intent is to go HAM HAM in those 10 minutes to get some insane level work done, then pause back to normal levels.\"\n   - \"window ends 4:50pm, full reset 5[pm\"\n   - (System/Stop-hook notifications and the \"user hasn't heard from you\" prompts are automated, not user messages.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Immediately: ack wake 318674 and the inbox note 1792451820-WJGKPu.\n   - Run the Fable burst before 4:50pm local (23:50Z) using the remaining 7%.\n   - After the 5pm reset, dispatch the next robots items (q22c, 7iaq, ek6rg, 3rm0a likely fixed by brain PR 48 and needing confirmation) and run runbooks-86h on Fable.\n   - Captain decisions still open: task-kj3ni (upstream PR batch consent vs moving clutter), MiniMax key/login, GitHub billing fix, \"land it\" for local-only branches, the Talon EULA call, consent to publish firstmate-repo fixes, mini0-ops holds, macbook-ops \"unlock your Mac screen\".\n   - Firstmate Share target-selection design (project-p16v) to scope into a build.\n   - robots-jecsr: find the bridge port, then curl /mcp. Merge of upstream into main is not pushed.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Preparing the \"HAM HAM\" Fable burst. It was 16:19 local (23:19Z) with Fable at 7% and the window ending 4:50pm. I had just probed the scout scaffold flow:\n   - `fm-brief.sh fable-burst-probe firstmate --scout` showed placeholders `{TASK}` (line 5) and `{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}` (line 8); I removed the probe dir.\n   - `fm-spawn.sh <id> <project-dir> --scout [--harness ...] [--model ...] [--effort ...]` is the spawn form.\n   Planned scouts (no PR, so no publish or merge risk) from the Fable-worthy collection:\n   - task-03lms: Barterboo RLS fix (barter project; a ship, otherwise a scout).\n   - task-75rn7: Markdown bridge plan (federated-markdown-bridge, local-only).\n   - task-vp1tv: scoping which projects are active.\n   - runbooks-86h: the 24h audit.\n   - project-p16v: Firstmate Share target selection design.\n   - task-aml2o / task-6bvt0: firstmate-repo defects, as scouts so nothing is published.\n   Project names in the registry: barter, firstmate, federated-markdown-bridge, firstmate_mcp, parlay, trillium_talon, behavioral-hooks, and others under projects/.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Ack wake 318674 (`LC_ALL=C bin/fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 318674 --recovery-generation 21758.1792451919.nkS2uS`) and inbox note 1792451820-WJGKPu. Then immediately scaffold and spawn the Fable scouts before 4:50pm local, filling each brief's {TASK}/{FIRSTMATE_SPEC} via `python3 -I`, adding backlog items with `fm-tasks-axi.sh add`, and spawning with `--scout --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh`. Log the burst in status-kdv. This follows directly from the captain's latest instruction: \"The intent is to go HAM HAM in those 10 minutes to get some insane level work done, then pause back to normal levels\" and \"window ends 4:50pm, full reset 5[pm\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/trilliumsmith/.claude/projects/-Users-trilliumsmith-fm-home-firstmate/3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"7384e116-6623-4cbe-a919-e9df494875ad","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:22:43.260Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":441,"turnIndex":873},"turnOrigin":"human","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
