.md'\ns=open(p).read().replace('{TASK}',intent,1).replace('{FIRSTMATE_SPEC}',spec,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nmk(){ python3 -I /private/tmp/claude-501/burst.py \"$@\" &amp;&amp; $B/fm-tasks-axi.sh add \"$1\" \"$5\" --kind scout &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1; HERDR_PANE_ID=wY7:p1 $B/fm-spawn.sh \"$1\" projects/$2 --scout --harness claude --model fable --effort xhigh 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-140; }\nS=\"Deliver a decision-ready report at data/&lt;id&gt;/report.md: findings, a recommended design, the smallest first slice, risks, and what needs the captain. Read-only: no edits to any project.\"\nmk fable-fmshare-q1 firstmate \"Firstmate Share (iOS share-sheet app, project-p16v) must be able to send a screenshot, and shares generally, to different firstmates (selectable target among the user's firstmate homes and secondmates) rather than one fixed endpoint.\" \"Design target selection: how the app learns the target list, how a chosen home receives it (inbox note per home vs existing poke path), auth, and the smallest buildable slice. $S\" \"Design Firstmate Share multi-firstmate targeting\"\nmk fable-mdbridge-q1 federated-markdown-bridge \"Plan a store-backed Markdown bridge for Firstmate customizations (task-75rn7) so local customizations stop diverging this fork from upstream firstmate.\" \"Read the project and the fork divergence summary in task-kj3ni; propose an architecture that moves our local customizations out of the tracked firstmate tree. $S\" \"Plan markdown bridge for firstmate customizations\"\nmk fable-scope-q1 firstmate \"Scoping (task-vp1tv): telling firstmate which projects are active, what needs work, and making world-blocks visible.\" \"Propose the data model, commands and session-start display. $S\" \"Scope active-project and world-block visibility\"\nmk fable-steward-q1 firstmate \"Establish autonomous stewardship across projects and tasks (task-fkewo).\" \"Define what autonomous stewardship means here, guardrails given the hard rules in AGENTS.md, and a first slice. $S\" \"Design autonomous stewardship\"\" completed (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"4e1caf6d-34c1-4c0d-8597-c8e121c0d6dd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14908208 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9a24a01c-180f-4501-a124-2735819be96d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:23:15.174Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14908208 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
{"parentUuid":"9a24a01c-180f-4501-a124-2735819be96d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCTT24Prfc2a9R3nama2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Captain, four Fable scouts are running. They cover Firstmate Share multi-target design, the Markdown bridge plan, project scoping, and autonomous stewardship.\n\n**Your question: sending to another firstmate on another machine**\n\n1. **Where we are:** the receiver works, but only for one firstmate. It is a tailnet-only HTTPS endpoint on this MacBook. It files an inbox bead, and the inbox watch wakes this firstmate. Two simulated shares were verified end to end (project-p16v, Firstmate Share). The app and share extension are built, but OTA install is blocked on the Xcode Apple ID. Choosing a target isn't built yet. The scout `fable-fmshare-q1` is designing that now.\n2. **Do we need a receiver on every machine?** Not necessarily. Two options:\n   - **One receiver, forward by ssh (recommended).** The phone talks only to the MacBook endpoint. The share carries a `target` field. The receiver files the inbox bead in the target home. For a remote home it forwards over the existing ssh path that remote secondmates already use (docs/remote-secondmates.md). The app needs one URL and one secret, and the phone doesn't need to know where each firstmate lives.\n   - **A receiver on each machine.** The phone would hold a list of URLs. That means more daemons to run and more secrets to manage. Choose this only if a machine must work while the MacBook is off.\n3. **What the target list is:** the receiver serves it from `data/secondmates.md` plus this home. The app fetches it, so adding a secondmate needs no app update.\n\nI've sent this to the scout as the leading option. Its report will confirm or overturn it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4058,"cache_read_input_tokens":84590,"output_tokens":557,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4058,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":84590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4058},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgCTT1SgPU59gcZYXpMuH","type":"assistant","uuid":"b74cb22b-4886-4969-8ea6-cf814046ee43","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:23:21.017Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/trilliumsmith/fm_home/firstmate","sessionId":"3b59b3ab-40e2-4906-ae5b-518d2b1a7b53","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floating-tinkering-lemur"}
